window.__dlg("parmenides",{"slug":"parmenides","title":"Parmenides","hi":"पार्मेनाइडीज़ — एक और प्रत्ययों पर संवाद","kicker":"Plato · The One and the Forms","range":"Stephanus 126a–166c","blurb":"The aged Parmenides presses the young Socrates with objections to the theory of Forms, including the Third Man, then shows the training a philosopher needs.","words":18858,"intro":["All three parts follow the same 29 sections, so a passage can be found in any version by its section tag. The tags (126a, 132a, 142b …) are approximate Stephanus numbers marking where each section begins, so you can match these pages against the Gill–Ryan translation and against citations in answers and commentaries. The section titles are editorial additions.","Cephalus retells a conversation from long ago. Young Socrates answers Zeno's paradoxes with the theory of Forms (to 130a), and the aged Parmenides then raises his famous objections: which things have Forms, how things can share in a Form, the \"Third Man\" regress (132a), Forms as thoughts or as patterns, and the greatest difficulty, that the Forms would be unknowable to us (133b). He does not reject the Forms; instead he prescribes training (135c) and demonstrates it with Aristoteles as respondent. That demonstration fills the rest of the dialogue: a series of deductions on the hypotheses \"if the one is\" (137c–160b) and \"if the one is not\" (160b–166c), ending in the conclusion that, whether the one is or is not, the one and the others both are and are not, and both appear and do not appear.","The English is Jowett's Victorian translation, which is in the public domain; its wording differs from Gill and Ryan's but follows the same argument. The dialogue is narrated, so speakers are named inside the text (\"said Socrates\") rather than in labels; in the long second part every question is Parmenides' and every short answer is Aristoteles'. Jowett's numbering of the deductions (1.a, 1.b, 1.aa, 1.bb, 2.a, 2.b, 2.aa, 2.bb) is kept. The Hinglish and Hindi versions translate Jowett paragraph by paragraph."],"terms":[["idea, form","eidos, idea","प्रत्यय (रूप)"],["participation","methexis","सहभागिता"],["likeness, pattern","homoiotēs, paradeigma","सादृश्य, आदर्श"],["one / many","hen / polla","एक / अनेक"],["being / not-being","to on / to mē on","सत् / असत्"],["same / other","tauton / heteron","समान / अन्य"],["like / unlike","homoion / anomoion","सदृश / असदूश"],["whole / part","holon / meros","संपूर्ण / भाग"],["limit / unlimited","peras / apeiron","सीमा / असीमित"],["hypothesis","hupothesis","परिकल्पना"],["the instant","to exaiphnēs","क्षण"]],"parts":{"en":[{"tag":"126a","title":"Prologue: Cephalus, Antiphon and the visit of Parmenides","paras":[["","Cephalus rehearses a dialogue which is supposed to have been narrated in his presence by Antiphon, the half-brother of Adeimantus and Glaucon, to certain Clazomenians.","in"],["","We had come from our home at Clazomenae to Athens, and met Adeimantus and Glaucon in the Agora. Welcome, Cephalus, said Adeimantus, taking me by the hand; is there anything which we can do for you in Athens?"],["","Yes; that is why I am here; I wish to ask a favour of you."],["","What may that be? he said."],["","I want you to tell me the name of your half brother, which I have forgotten; he was a mere child when I last came hither from Clazomenae, but that was a long time ago; his father's name, if I remember rightly, was Pyrilampes?"],["","Yes, he said, and the name of our brother, Antiphon; but why do you ask?"],["","Let me introduce some countrymen of mine, I said; they are lovers of philosophy, and have heard that Antiphon was intimate with a certain Pythodorus, a friend of Zeno, and remembers a conversation which took place between Socrates, Zeno, and Parmenides many years ago, Pythodorus having often recited it to him."],["","Quite true."],["","And could we hear it? I asked."],["","Nothing easier, he replied; when he was a youth he made a careful study of the piece; at present his thoughts run in another direction; like his grandfather Antiphon he is devoted to horses. But, if that is what you want, let us go and look for him; he dwells at Melita, which is quite near, and he has only just left us to go home."],["","Accordingly we went to look for him; he was at home, and in the act of giving a bridle to a smith to be fitted. When he had done with the smith, his brothers told him the purpose of our visit; and he saluted me as an acquaintance whom he remembered from my former visit, and we asked him to repeat the dialogue. At first he was not very willing, and complained of the trouble, but at length he consented. He told us that Pythodorus had described to him the appearance of Parmenides and Zeno; they came to Athens, as he said, at the great Panathenaea; the former was, at the time of his visit, about 65 years old, very white with age, but well favoured. Zeno was nearly 40 years of age, tall and fair to look upon; in the days of his youth he was reported to have been beloved by Parmenides. He said that they lodged with Pythodorus in the Ceramicus, outside the wall, whither Socrates, then a very young man, came to see them, and many others with him; they wanted to hear the writings of Zeno, which had been brought to Athens for the first time on the occasion of their visit. These Zeno himself read to them in the absence of Parmenides, and had very nearly finished when Pythodorus entered, and with him Parmenides and Aristoteles who was afterwards one of the Thirty, and heard the little that remained of the dialogue. Pythodorus had heard Zeno repeat them before."]]},{"tag":"127d","title":"Zeno's argument and Socrates' theory of Forms","paras":[["","When the recitation was completed, Socrates requested that the first thesis of the first argument might be read over again, and this having been done, he said: What is your meaning, Zeno? Do you maintain that if being is many, it must be both like and unlike, and that this is impossible, for neither can the like be unlike, nor the unlike like—is that your position?"],["","Just so, said Zeno."],["","And if the unlike cannot be like, or the like unlike, then according to you, being could not be many; for this would involve an impossibility. In all that you say have you any other purpose except to disprove the being of the many? and is not each division of your treatise intended to furnish a separate proof of this, there being in all as many proofs of the not-being of the many as you have composed arguments? Is that your meaning, or have I misunderstood you?"],["","No, said Zeno; you have correctly understood my general purpose."],["","I see, Parmenides, said Socrates, that Zeno would like to be not only one with you in friendship but your second self in his writings too; he puts what you say in another way, and would fain make believe that he is telling us something which is new. For you, in your poems, say The All is one, and of this you adduce excellent proofs; and he on the other hand says There is no many; and on behalf of this he offers overwhelming evidence. You affirm unity, he denies plurality. And so you deceive the world into believing that you are saying different things when really you are saying much the same. This is a strain of art beyond the reach of most of us."],["","Yes, Socrates, said Zeno. But although you are as keen as a Spartan hound in pursuing the track, you do not fully apprehend the true motive of the composition, which is not really such an artificial work as you imagine; for what you speak of was an accident; there was no pretence of a great purpose; nor any serious intention of deceiving the world. The truth is, that these writings of mine were meant to protect the arguments of Parmenides against those who make fun of him and seek to show the many ridiculous and contradictory results which they suppose to follow from the affirmation of the one. My answer is addressed to the partisans of the many, whose attack I return with interest by retorting upon them that their hypothesis of the being of many, if carried out, appears to be still more ridiculous than the hypothesis of the being of one. Zeal for my master led me to write the book in the days of my youth, but some one stole the copy; and therefore I had no choice whether it should be published or not; the motive, however, of writing, was not the ambition of an elder man, but the pugnacity of a young one. This you do not seem to see, Socrates; though in other respects, as I was saying, your notion is a very just one."],["","I understand, said Socrates, and quite accept your account. But tell me, Zeno, do you not further think that there is an idea of likeness in itself, and another idea of unlikeness, which is the opposite of likeness, and that in these two, you and I and all other things to which we apply the term many, participate—things which participate in likeness become in that degree and manner like; and so far as they participate in unlikeness become in that degree unlike, or both like and unlike in the degree in which they participate in both? And may not all things partake of both opposites, and be both like and unlike, by reason of this participation?—Where is the wonder? Now if a person could prove the absolute like to become unlike, or the absolute unlike to become like, that, in my opinion, would indeed be a wonder; but there is nothing extraordinary, Zeno, in showing that the things which only partake of likeness and unlikeness experience both. Nor, again, if a person were to show that all is one by partaking of one, and at the same time many by partaking of many, would that be very astonishing. But if he were to show me that the absolute one was many, or the absolute many one, I should be truly amazed. And so of all the rest: I should be surprised to hear that the natures or ideas themselves had these opposite qualities; but not if a person wanted to prove of me that I was many and also one. When he wanted to show that I was many he would say that I have a right and a left side, and a front and a back, and an upper and a lower half, for I cannot deny that I partake of multitude; when, on the other hand, he wants to prove that I am one, he will say, that we who are here assembled are seven, and that I am one and partake of the one. In both instances he proves his case. So again, if a person shows that such things as wood, stones, and the like, being many are also one, we admit that he shows the coexistence of the one and many, but he does not show that the many are one or the one many; he is uttering not a paradox but a truism. If however, as I just now suggested, some one were to abstract simple notions of like, unlike, one, many, rest, motion, and similar ideas, and then to show that these admit of admixture and separation in themselves, I should be very much astonished. This part of the argument appears to be treated by you, Zeno, in a very spirited manner; but, as I was saying, I should be far more amazed if any one found in the ideas themselves which are apprehended by reason, the same puzzle and entanglement which you have shown to exist in visible objects."],["","While Socrates was speaking, Pythodorus thought that Parmenides and Zeno were not altogether pleased at the successive steps of the argument; but still they gave the closest attention, and often looked at one another, and smiled as if in admiration of him. When he had finished, Parmenides expressed their feelings in the following words:—"]]},{"tag":"130a","title":"Which things have Forms?","paras":[["","Socrates, he said, I admire the bent of your mind towards philosophy; tell me now, was this your own distinction between ideas in themselves and the things which partake of them? and do you think that there is an idea of likeness apart from the likeness which we possess, and of the one and many, and of the other things which Zeno mentioned?"],["","I think that there are such ideas, said Socrates."],["","Parmenides proceeded: And would you also make absolute ideas of the just and the beautiful and the good, and of all that class?"],["","Yes, he said, I should."],["","And would you make an idea of man apart from us and from all other human creatures, or of fire and water?"],["","I am often undecided, Parmenides, as to whether I ought to include them or not."],["","And would you feel equally undecided, Socrates, about things of which the mention may provoke a smile?—I mean such things as hair, mud, dirt, or anything else which is vile and paltry; would you suppose that each of these has an idea distinct from the actual objects with which we come into contact, or not?"],["","Certainly not, said Socrates; visible things like these are such as they appear to us, and I am afraid that there would be an absurdity in assuming any idea of them, although I sometimes get disturbed, and begin to think that there is nothing without an idea; but then again, when I have taken up this position, I run away, because I am afraid that I may fall into a bottomless pit of nonsense, and perish; and so I return to the ideas of which I was just now speaking, and occupy myself with them."],["","Yes, Socrates, said Parmenides; that is because you are still young; the time will come, if I am not mistaken, when philosophy will have a firmer grasp of you, and then you will not despise even the meanest things; at your age, you are too much disposed to regard the opinions of men. But I should like to know whether you mean that there are certain ideas of which all other things partake, and from which they derive their names; that similars, for example, become similar, because they partake of similarity; and great things become great, because they partake of greatness; and that just and beautiful things become just and beautiful, because they partake of justice and beauty?"],["","Yes, certainly, said Socrates that is my meaning."]]},{"tag":"131a","title":"Participation: whole or part? The sail","paras":[["","Then each individual partakes either of the whole of the idea or else of a part of the idea? Can there be any other mode of participation?"],["","There cannot be, he said."],["","Then do you think that the whole idea is one, and yet, being one, is in each one of the many?"],["","Why not, Parmenides? said Socrates."],["","Because one and the same thing will exist as a whole at the same time in many separate individuals, and will therefore be in a state of separation from itself."],["","Nay, but the idea may be like the day which is one and the same in many places at once, and yet continuous with itself; in this way each idea may be one and the same in all at the same time."],["","I like your way, Socrates, of making one in many places at once. You mean to say, that if I were to spread out a sail and cover a number of men, there would be one whole including many—is not that your meaning?"],["","I think so."],["","And would you say that the whole sail includes each man, or a part of it only, and different parts different men?"],["","The latter."],["","Then, Socrates, the ideas themselves will be divisible, and things which participate in them will have a part of them only and not the whole idea existing in each of them?"],["","That seems to follow."],["","Then would you like to say, Socrates, that the one idea is really divisible and yet remains one?"],["","Certainly not, he said."],["","Suppose that you divide absolute greatness, and that of the many great things, each one is great in virtue of a portion of greatness less than absolute greatness—is that conceivable?"],["","No."],["","Or will each equal thing, if possessing some small portion of equality less than absolute equality, be equal to some other thing by virtue of that portion only?"],["","Impossible."],["","Or suppose one of us to have a portion of smallness; this is but a part of the small, and therefore the absolutely small is greater; if the absolutely small be greater, that to which the part of the small is added will be smaller and not greater than before."],["","How absurd!"],["","Then in what way, Socrates, will all things participate in the ideas, if they are unable to participate in them either as parts or wholes?"],["","Indeed, he said, you have asked a question which is not easily answered."],["","Well, said Parmenides, and what do you say of another question?"],["","What question?"]]},{"tag":"132a","title":"The 'Third Man': greatness regress","paras":[["","I imagine that the way in which you are led to assume one idea of each kind is as follows:—You see a number of great objects, and when you look at them there seems to you to be one and the same idea (or nature) in them all; hence you conceive of greatness as one."],["","Very true, said Socrates."],["","And if you go on and allow your mind in like manner to embrace in one view the idea of greatness and of great things which are not the idea, and to compare them, will not another greatness arise, which will appear to be the source of all these?"],["","It would seem so."],["","Then another idea of greatness now comes into view over and above absolute greatness, and the individuals which partake of it; and then another, over and above all these, by virtue of which they will all be great, and so each idea instead of being one will be infinitely multiplied."]]},{"tag":"132b","title":"Forms as thoughts","paras":[["","But may not the ideas, asked Socrates, be thoughts only, and have no proper existence except in our minds, Parmenides? For in that case each idea may still be one, and not experience this infinite multiplication."],["","And can there be individual thoughts which are thoughts of nothing?"],["","Impossible, he said."],["","The thought must be of something?"],["","Yes."],["","Of something which is or which is not?"],["","Of something which is."],["","Must it not be of a single something, which the thought recognizes as attaching to all, being a single form or nature?"],["","Yes."],["","And will not the something which is apprehended as one and the same in all, be an idea?"],["","From that, again, there is no escape."],["","Then, said Parmenides, if you say that everything else participates in the ideas, must you not say either that everything is made up of thoughts, and that all things think; or that they are thoughts but have no thought?"]]},{"tag":"132d","title":"Forms as patterns: the likeness regress","paras":[["","The latter view, Parmenides, is no more rational than the previous one. In my opinion, the ideas are, as it were, patterns fixed in nature, and other things are like them, and resemblances of them—what is meant by the participation of other things in the ideas, is really assimilation to them."],["","But if, said he, the individual is like the idea, must not the idea also be like the individual, in so far as the individual is a resemblance of the idea? That which is like, cannot be conceived of as other than the like of like."],["","Impossible."],["","And when two things are alike, must they not partake of the same idea?"],["","They must."],["","And will not that of which the two partake, and which makes them alike, be the idea itself?"],["","Certainly."],["","Then the idea cannot be like the individual, or the individual like the idea; for if they are alike, some further idea of likeness will always be coming to light, and if that be like anything else, another; and new ideas will be always arising, if the idea resembles that which partakes of it?"],["","Quite true."],["","The theory, then, that other things participate in the ideas by resemblance, has to be given up, and some other mode of participation devised?"],["","It would seem so."],["","Do you see then, Socrates, how great is the difficulty of affirming the ideas to be absolute?"],["","Yes, indeed."],["","And, further, let me say that as yet you only understand a small part of the difficulty which is involved if you make of each thing a single idea, parting it off from other things."],["","What difficulty? he said."]]},{"tag":"133b","title":"The greatest difficulty: the Forms unknowable","paras":[["","There are many, but the greatest of all is this:—If an opponent argues that these ideas, being such as we say they ought to be, must remain unknown, no one can prove to him that he is wrong, unless he who denies their existence be a man of great ability and knowledge, and is willing to follow a long and laborious demonstration; he will remain unconvinced, and still insist that they cannot be known."],["","What do you mean, Parmenides? said Socrates."],["","In the first place, I think, Socrates, that you, or any one who maintains the existence of absolute essences, will admit that they cannot exist in us."],["","No, said Socrates; for then they would be no longer absolute."],["","True, he said; and therefore when ideas are what they are in relation to one another, their essence is determined by a relation among themselves, and has nothing to do with the resemblances, or whatever they are to be termed, which are in our sphere, and from which we receive this or that name when we partake of them. And the things which are within our sphere and have the same names with them, are likewise only relative to one another, and not to the ideas which have the same names with them, but belong to themselves and not to them."],["","What do you mean? said Socrates."],["","I may illustrate my meaning in this way, said Parmenides:—A master has a slave; now there is nothing absolute in the relation between them, which is simply a relation of one man to another. But there is also an idea of mastership in the abstract, which is relative to the idea of slavery in the abstract. These natures have nothing to do with us, nor we with them; they are concerned with themselves only, and we with ourselves. Do you see my meaning?"],["","Yes, said Socrates, I quite see your meaning."],["","And will not knowledge—I mean absolute knowledge—answer to absolute truth?"],["","Certainly."],["","And each kind of absolute knowledge will answer to each kind of absolute being?"],["","Yes."],["","But the knowledge which we have, will answer to the truth which we have; and again, each kind of knowledge which we have, will be a knowledge of each kind of being which we have?"],["","Certainly."],["","But the ideas themselves, as you admit, we have not, and cannot have?"],["","No, we cannot."],["","And the absolute natures or kinds are known severally by the absolute idea of knowledge?"],["","Yes."],["","And we have not got the idea of knowledge?"],["","No."],["","Then none of the ideas are known to us, because we have no share in absolute knowledge?"],["","I suppose not."],["","Then the nature of the beautiful in itself, and of the good in itself, and all other ideas which we suppose to exist absolutely, are unknown to us?"],["","It would seem so."],["","I think that there is a stranger consequence still."],["","What is it?"],["","Would you, or would you not say, that absolute knowledge, if there is such a thing, must be a far more exact knowledge than our knowledge; and the same of beauty and of the rest?"],["","Yes."],["","And if there be such a thing as participation in absolute knowledge, no one is more likely than God to have this most exact knowledge?"],["","Certainly."],["","But then, will God, having absolute knowledge, have a knowledge of human things?"],["","Why not?"],["","Because, Socrates, said Parmenides, we have admitted that the ideas are not valid in relation to human things; nor human things in relation to them; the relations of either are limited to their respective spheres."],["","Yes, that has been admitted."],["","And if God has this perfect authority, and perfect knowledge, his authority cannot rule us, nor his knowledge know us, or any human thing; just as our authority does not extend to the gods, nor our knowledge know anything which is divine, so by parity of reason they, being gods, are not our masters, neither do they know the things of men."],["","Yet, surely, said Socrates, to deprive God of knowledge is monstrous."],["","These, Socrates, said Parmenides, are a few, and only a few of the difficulties in which we are involved if ideas really are and we determine each one of them to be an absolute unity. He who hears what may be said against them will deny the very existence of them—and even if they do exist, he will say that they must of necessity be unknown to man; and he will seem to have reason on his side, and as we were remarking just now, will be very difficult to convince; a man must be gifted with very considerable ability before he can learn that everything has a class and an absolute essence; and still more remarkable will he be who discovers all these things for himself, and having thoroughly investigated them is able to teach them to others."],["","I agree with you, Parmenides, said Socrates; and what you say is very much to my mind."],["","And yet, Socrates, said Parmenides, if a man, fixing his attention on these and the like difficulties, does away with ideas of things and will not admit that every individual thing has its own determinate idea which is always one and the same, he will have nothing on which his mind can rest; and so he will utterly destroy the power of reasoning, as you seem to me to have particularly noted."],["","Very true, he said."],["","But, then, what is to become of philosophy? Whither shall we turn, if the ideas are unknown?"],["","I certainly do not see my way at present."]]},{"tag":"135c","title":"The need for training in dialectic","paras":[["","Yes, said Parmenides; and I think that this arises, Socrates, out of your attempting to define the beautiful, the just, the good, and the ideas generally, without sufficient previous training. I noticed your deficiency, when I heard you talking here with your friend Aristoteles, the day before yesterday. The impulse that carries you towards philosophy is assuredly noble and divine; but there is an art which is called by the vulgar idle talking, and which is often imagined to be useless; in that you must train and exercise yourself, now that you are young, or truth will elude your grasp."],["","And what is the nature of this exercise, Parmenides, which you would recommend?"],["","That which you heard Zeno practising; at the same time, I give you credit for saying to him that you did not care to examine the perplexity in reference to visible things, or to consider the question that way; but only in reference to objects of thought, and to what may be called ideas."],["","Why, yes, he said, there appears to me to be no difficulty in showing by this method that visible things are like and unlike and may experience anything."],["","Quite true, said Parmenides; but I think that you should go a step further, and consider not only the consequences which flow from a given hypothesis, but also the consequences which flow from denying the hypothesis; and that will be still better training for you."],["","What do you mean? he said."],["","I mean, for example, that in the case of this very hypothesis of Zeno's about the many, you should inquire not only what will be the consequences to the many in relation to themselves and to the one, and to the one in relation to itself and the many, on the hypothesis of the being of the many, but also what will be the consequences to the one and the many in their relation to themselves and to each other, on the opposite hypothesis. Or, again, if likeness is or is not, what will be the consequences in either of these cases to the subjects of the hypothesis, and to other things, in relation both to themselves and to one another, and so of unlikeness; and the same holds good of motion and rest, of generation and destruction, and even of being and not-being. In a word, when you suppose anything to be or not to be, or to be in any way affected, you must look at the consequences in relation to the thing itself, and to any other things which you choose,—to each of them singly, to more than one, and to all; and so of other things, you must look at them in relation to themselves and to anything else which you suppose either to be or not to be, if you would train yourself perfectly and see the real truth."],["","That, Parmenides, is a tremendous business of which you speak, and I do not quite understand you; will you take some hypothesis and go through the steps?—then I shall apprehend you better."],["","That, Socrates, is a serious task to impose on a man of my years."],["","Then will you, Zeno? said Socrates."],["","Zeno answered with a smile:—Let us make our petition to Parmenides himself, who is quite right in saying that you are hardly aware of the extent of the task which you are imposing on him; and if there were more of us I should not ask him, for these are not subjects which any one, especially at his age, can well speak of before a large audience; most people are not aware that this roundabout progress through all things is the only way in which the mind can attain truth and wisdom. And therefore, Parmenides, I join in the request of Socrates, that I may hear the process again which I have not heard for a long time."]]},{"tag":"136e","title":"Parmenides agrees; Aristoteles will answer","paras":[["","When Zeno had thus spoken, Pythodorus, according to Antiphon's report of him, said, that he himself and Aristoteles and the whole company entreated Parmenides to give an example of the process. I cannot refuse, said Parmenides; and yet I feel rather like Ibycus, who, when in his old age, against his will, he fell in love, compared himself to an old racehorse, who was about to run in a chariot race, shaking with fear at the course he knew so well—this was his simile of himself. And I also experience a trembling when I remember through what an ocean of words I have to wade at my time of life. But I must indulge you, as Zeno says that I ought, and we are alone. Where shall I begin? And what shall be our first hypothesis, if I am to attempt this laborious pastime? Shall I begin with myself, and take my own hypothesis the one? and consider the consequences which follow on the supposition either of the being or of the not-being of one?"],["","By all means, said Zeno."],["","And who will answer me? he said. Shall I propose the youngest? He will not make difficulties and will be the most likely to say what he thinks; and his answers will give me time to breathe."],["","I am the one whom you mean, Parmenides, said Aristoteles; for I am the youngest and at your service. Ask, and I will answer."]]},{"tag":"137c","title":"Deduction 1: if the one is, it is not many","paras":[["","Parmenides proceeded: 1.a. If one is, he said, the one cannot be many?"],["","Impossible."],["","Then the one cannot have parts, and cannot be a whole?"],["","Why not?"],["","Because every part is part of a whole; is it not?"],["","Yes."],["","And what is a whole? would not that of which no part is wanting be a whole?"],["","Certainly."],["","Then, in either case, the one would be made up of parts; both as being a whole, and also as having parts?"],["","To be sure."],["","And in either case, the one would be many, and not one?"],["","True."],["","But, surely, it ought to be one and not many?"],["","It ought."],["","Then, if the one is to remain one, it will not be a whole, and will not have parts?"],["","No."],["","But if it has no parts, it will have neither beginning, middle, nor end; for these would of course be parts of it."],["","Right."],["","But then, again, a beginning and an end are the limits of everything?"],["","Certainly."],["","Then the one, having neither beginning nor end, is unlimited?"],["","Yes, unlimited."],["","And therefore formless; for it cannot partake either of round or straight."],["","But why?"],["","Why, because the round is that of which all the extreme points are equidistant from the centre?"],["","Yes."],["","And the straight is that of which the centre intercepts the view of the extremes?"],["","True."],["","Then the one would have parts and would be many, if it partook either of a straight or of a circular form?"],["","Assuredly."],["","But having no parts, it will be neither straight nor round?"],["","Right."],["","And, being of such a nature, it cannot be in any place, for it cannot be either in another or in itself."],["","How so?"],["","Because if it were in another, it would be encircled by that in which it was, and would touch it at many places and with many parts; but that which is one and indivisible, and does not partake of a circular nature, cannot be touched all round in many places."],["","Certainly not."],["","But if, on the other hand, one were in itself, it would also be contained by nothing else but itself; that is to say, if it were really in itself; for nothing can be in anything which does not contain it."],["","Impossible."],["","But then, that which contains must be other than that which is contained? for the same whole cannot do and suffer both at once; and if so, one will be no longer one, but two?"],["","True."],["","Then one cannot be anywhere, either in itself or in another?"],["","No."]]},{"tag":"138b","title":"Neither in motion nor at rest","paras":[["","Further consider, whether that which is of such a nature can have either rest or motion."],["","Why not?"],["","Why, because the one, if it were moved, would be either moved in place or changed in nature; for these are the only kinds of motion."],["","Yes."],["","And the one, when it changes and ceases to be itself, cannot be any longer one."],["","It cannot."],["","It cannot therefore experience the sort of motion which is change of nature?"],["","Clearly not."],["","Then can the motion of the one be in place?"],["","Perhaps."],["","But if the one moved in place, must it not either move round and round in the same place, or from one place to another?"],["","It must."],["","And that which moves in a circle must rest upon a centre; and that which goes round upon a centre must have parts which are different from the centre; but that which has no centre and no parts cannot possibly be carried round upon a centre?"],["","Impossible."],["","But perhaps the motion of the one consists in change of place?"],["","Perhaps so, if it moves at all."],["","And have we not already shown that it cannot be in anything?"],["","Yes."],["","Then its coming into being in anything is still more impossible; is it not?"],["","I do not see why."],["","Why, because anything which comes into being in anything, can neither as yet be in that other thing while still coming into being, nor be altogether out of it, if already coming into being in it."],["","Certainly not."],["","And therefore whatever comes into being in another must have parts, and then one part may be in, and another part out of that other; but that which has no parts can never be at one and the same time neither wholly within nor wholly without anything."],["","True."],["","And is there not a still greater impossibility in that which has no parts, and is not a whole, coming into being anywhere, since it cannot come into being either as a part or as a whole?"],["","Clearly."],["","Then it does not change place by revolving in the same spot, nor by going somewhere and coming into being in something; nor again, by change in itself?"],["","Very true."],["","Then in respect of any kind of motion the one is immoveable?"],["","Immoveable."],["","But neither can the one be in anything, as we affirm?"],["","Yes, we said so."],["","Then it is never in the same?"],["","Why not?"],["","Because if it were in the same it would be in something."],["","Certainly."],["","And we said that it could not be in itself, and could not be in other?"],["","True."],["","Then one is never in the same place?"],["","It would seem not."],["","But that which is never in the same place is never quiet or at rest?"],["","Never."],["","One then, as would seem, is neither at rest nor in motion?"],["","It certainly appears so."]]},{"tag":"139b","title":"Neither same nor other, like nor unlike","paras":[["","Neither will it be the same with itself or other; nor again, other than itself or other."],["","How is that?"],["","If other than itself it would be other than one, and would not be one."],["","True."],["","And if the same with other, it would be that other, and not itself; so that upon this supposition too, it would not have the nature of one, but would be other than one?"],["","It would."],["","Then it will not be the same with other, or other than itself?"],["","It will not."],["","Neither will it be other than other, while it remains one; for not one, but only other, can be other than other, and nothing else."],["","True."],["","Then not by virtue of being one will it be other?"],["","Certainly not."],["","But if not by virtue of being one, not by virtue of itself; and if not by virtue of itself, not itself, and itself not being other at all, will not be other than anything?"],["","Right."],["","Neither will one be the same with itself."],["","How not?"],["","Surely the nature of the one is not the nature of the same."],["","Why not?"],["","It is not when anything becomes the same with anything that it becomes one."],["","What of that?"],["","Anything which becomes the same with the many, necessarily becomes many and not one."],["","True."],["","But, if there were no difference between the one and the same, when a thing became the same, it would always become one; and when it became one, the same?"],["","Certainly."],["","And, therefore, if one be the same with itself, it is not one with itself, and will therefore be one and also not one."],["","Surely that is impossible."],["","And therefore the one can neither be other than other, nor the same with itself."],["","Impossible."],["","And thus the one can neither be the same, nor other, either in relation to itself or other?"],["","No."],["","Neither will the one be like anything or unlike itself or other."],["","Why not?"],["","Because likeness is sameness of affections."],["","Yes."],["","And sameness has been shown to be of a nature distinct from oneness?"],["","That has been shown."],["","But if the one had any other affection than that of being one, it would be affected in such a way as to be more than one; which is impossible."],["","True."],["","Then the one can never be so affected as to be the same either with another or with itself?"],["","Clearly not."],["","Then it cannot be like another, or like itself?"],["","No."],["","Nor can it be affected so as to be other, for then it would be affected in such a way as to be more than one."],["","It would."],["","That which is affected otherwise than itself or another, will be unlike itself or another, for sameness of affections is likeness."],["","True."],["","But the one, as appears, never being affected otherwise, is never unlike itself or other?"],["","Never."],["","Then the one will never be either like or unlike itself or other?"],["","Plainly not."]]},{"tag":"140b","title":"Neither equal nor unequal, older nor younger","paras":[["","Again, being of this nature, it can neither be equal nor unequal either to itself or to other."],["","How is that?"],["","Why, because the one if equal must be of the same measures as that to which it is equal."],["","True."],["","And if greater or less than things which are commensurable with it, the one will have more measures than that which is less, and fewer than that which is greater?"],["","Yes."],["","And so of things which are not commensurate with it, the one will have greater measures than that which is less and smaller than that which is greater."],["","Certainly."],["","But how can that which does not partake of sameness, have either the same measures or have anything else the same?"],["","Impossible."],["","And not having the same measures, the one cannot be equal either with itself or with another?"],["","It appears so."],["","But again, whether it have fewer or more measures, it will have as many parts as it has measures; and thus again the one will be no longer one but will have as many parts as measures."],["","Right."],["","And if it were of one measure, it would be equal to that measure; yet it has been shown to be incapable of equality."],["","It has."],["","Then it will neither partake of one measure, nor of many, nor of few, nor of the same at all, nor be equal to itself or another; nor be greater or less than itself, or other?"],["","Certainly."],["","Well, and do we suppose that one can be older, or younger than anything, or of the same age with it?"],["","Why not?"],["","Why, because that which is of the same age with itself or other, must partake of equality or likeness of time; and we said that the one did not partake either of equality or of likeness?"],["","We did say so."],["","And we also said, that it did not partake of inequality or unlikeness."],["","Very true."],["","How then can one, being of this nature, be either older or younger than anything, or have the same age with it?"],["","In no way."],["","Then one cannot be older or younger, or of the same age, either with itself or with another?"],["","Clearly not."]]},{"tag":"141a","title":"Not in time, and not at all","paras":[["","Then the one, being of this nature, cannot be in time at all; for must not that which is in time, be always growing older than itself?"],["","Certainly."],["","And that which is older, must always be older than something which is younger?"],["","True."],["","Then, that which becomes older than itself, also becomes at the same time younger than itself, if it is to have something to become older than."],["","What do you mean?"],["","I mean this:—A thing does not need to become different from another thing which is already different; it IS different, and if its different has become, it has become different; if its different will be, it will be different; but of that which is becoming different, there cannot have been, or be about to be, or yet be, a different—the only different possible is one which is becoming."],["","That is inevitable."],["","But, surely, the elder is a difference relative to the younger, and to nothing else."],["","True."],["","Then that which becomes older than itself must also, at the same time, become younger than itself?"],["","Yes."],["","But again, it is true that it cannot become for a longer or for a shorter time than itself, but it must become, and be, and have become, and be about to be, for the same time with itself?"],["","That again is inevitable."],["","Then things which are in time, and partake of time, must in every case, I suppose, be of the same age with themselves; and must also become at once older and younger than themselves?"],["","Yes."],["","But the one did not partake of those affections?"],["","Not at all."],["","Then it does not partake of time, and is not in any time?"],["","So the argument shows."],["","Well, but do not the expressions 'was,' and 'has become,' and 'was becoming,' signify a participation of past time?"],["","Certainly."],["","And do not 'will be,' 'will become,' 'will have become,' signify a participation of future time?"],["","Yes."],["","And 'is,' or 'becomes,' signifies a participation of present time?"],["","Certainly."],["","And if the one is absolutely without participation in time, it never had become, or was becoming, or was at any time, or is now become or is becoming, or is, or will become, or will have become, or will be, hereafter."],["","Most true."],["","But are there any modes of partaking of being other than these?"],["","There are none."],["","Then the one cannot possibly partake of being?"],["","That is the inference."],["","Then the one is not at all?"],["","Clearly not."],["","Then the one does not exist in such way as to be one; for if it were and partook of being, it would already be; but if the argument is to be trusted, the one neither is nor is one?"],["","True."],["","But that which is not admits of no attribute or relation?"],["","Of course not."],["","Then there is no name, nor expression, nor perception, nor opinion, nor knowledge of it?"],["","Clearly not."],["","Then it is neither named, nor expressed, nor opined, nor known, nor does anything that is perceive it."],["","So we must infer."],["","But can all this be true about the one?"],["","I think not."]]},{"tag":"142b","title":"Deduction 2: the one that is","paras":[["","1.b. Suppose, now, that we return once more to the original hypothesis; let us see whether, on a further review, any new aspect of the question appears."],["","I shall be very happy to do so."],["","We say that we have to work out together all the consequences, whatever they may be, which follow, if the one is?"],["","Yes."],["","Then we will begin at the beginning:—If one is, can one be, and not partake of being?"],["","Impossible."],["","Then the one will have being, but its being will not be the same with the one; for if the same, it would not be the being of the one; nor would the one have participated in being, for the proposition that one is would have been identical with the proposition that one is one; but our hypothesis is not if one is one, what will follow, but if one is:—am I not right?"],["","Quite right."],["","We mean to say, that being has not the same significance as one?"],["","Of course."],["","And when we put them together shortly, and say 'One is,' that is equivalent to saying, 'partakes of being'?"],["","Quite true."],["","Once more then let us ask, if one is what will follow. Does not this hypothesis necessarily imply that one is of such a nature as to have parts?"],["","How so?"],["","In this way:—If being is predicated of the one, if the one is, and one of being, if being is one; and if being and one are not the same; and since the one, which we have assumed, is, must not the whole, if it is one, itself be, and have for its parts, one and being?"],["","Certainly."],["","And is each of these parts—one and being—to be simply called a part, or must the word 'part' be relative to the word 'whole'?"],["","The latter."],["","Then that which is one is both a whole and has a part?"],["","Certainly."],["","Again, of the parts of the one, if it is—I mean being and one—does either fail to imply the other? is the one wanting to being, or being to the one?"],["","Impossible."],["","Thus, each of the parts also has in turn both one and being, and is at the least made up of two parts; and the same principle goes on for ever, and every part whatever has always these two parts; for being always involves one, and one being; so that one is always disappearing, and becoming two."],["","Certainly."],["","And so the one, if it is, must be infinite in multiplicity?"],["","Clearly."]]},{"tag":"143a","title":"The one generates number","paras":[["","Let us take another direction."],["","What direction?"],["","We say that the one partakes of being and therefore it is?"],["","Yes."],["","And in this way, the one, if it has being, has turned out to be many?"],["","True."],["","But now, let us abstract the one which, as we say, partakes of being, and try to imagine it apart from that of which, as we say, it partakes—will this abstract one be one only or many?"],["","One, I think."],["","Let us see:—Must not the being of one be other than one? for the one is not being, but, considered as one, only partook of being?"],["","Certainly."],["","If being and the one be two different things, it is not because the one is one that it is other than being; nor because being is being that it is other than the one; but they differ from one another in virtue of otherness and difference."],["","Certainly."],["","So that the other is not the same—either with the one or with being?"],["","Certainly not."],["","And therefore whether we take being and the other, or being and the one, or the one and the other, in every such case we take two things, which may be rightly called both."],["","How so."],["","In this way—you may speak of being?"],["","Yes."],["","And also of one?"],["","Yes."],["","Then now we have spoken of either of them?"],["","Yes."],["","Well, and when I speak of being and one, I speak of them both?"],["","Certainly."],["","And if I speak of being and the other, or of the one and the other,—in any such case do I not speak of both?"],["","Yes."],["","And must not that which is correctly called both, be also two?"],["","Undoubtedly."],["","And of two things how can either by any possibility not be one?"],["","It cannot."],["","Then, if the individuals of the pair are together two, they must be severally one?"],["","Clearly."],["","And if each of them is one, then by the addition of any one to any pair, the whole becomes three?"],["","Yes."],["","And three are odd, and two are even?"],["","Of course."],["","And if there are two there must also be twice, and if there are three there must be thrice; that is, if twice one makes two, and thrice one three?"],["","Certainly."],["","There are two, and twice, and therefore there must be twice two; and there are three, and there is thrice, and therefore there must be thrice three?"],["","Of course."],["","If there are three and twice, there is twice three; and if there are two and thrice, there is thrice two?"],["","Undoubtedly."],["","Here, then, we have even taken even times, and odd taken odd times, and even taken odd times, and odd taken even times."],["","True."],["","And if this is so, does any number remain which has no necessity to be?"],["","None whatever."],["","Then if one is, number must also be?"],["","It must."],["","But if there is number, there must also be many, and infinite multiplicity of being; for number is infinite in multiplicity, and partakes also of being: am I not right?"],["","Certainly."],["","And if all number participates in being, every part of number will also participate?"],["","Yes."],["","Then being is distributed over the whole multitude of things, and nothing that is, however small or however great, is devoid of it? And, indeed, the very supposition of this is absurd, for how can that which is, be devoid of being?"],["","In no way."],["","And it is divided into the greatest and into the smallest, and into being of all sizes, and is broken up more than all things; the divisions of it have no limit."],["","True."],["","Then it has the greatest number of parts?"],["","Yes, the greatest number."],["","Is there any of these which is a part of being, and yet no part?"],["","Impossible."],["","But if it is at all and so long as it is, it must be one, and cannot be none?"],["","Certainly."],["","Then the one attaches to every single part of being, and does not fail in any part, whether great or small, or whatever may be the size of it?"],["","True."],["","But reflect:—Can one, in its entirety, be in many places at the same time?"],["","No; I see the impossibility of that."],["","And if not in its entirety, then it is divided; for it cannot be present with all the parts of being, unless divided."],["","True."],["","And that which has parts will be as many as the parts are?"],["","Certainly."],["","Then we were wrong in saying just now, that being was distributed into the greatest number of parts. For it is not distributed into parts more than the one, into parts equal to the one; the one is never wanting to being, or being to the one, but being two they are co-equal and co-extensive."],["","Certainly that is true."],["","The one itself, then, having been broken up into parts by being, is many and infinite?"],["","True."],["","Then not only the one which has being is many, but the one itself distributed by being, must also be many?"],["","Certainly."],["","Further, inasmuch as the parts are parts of a whole, the one, as a whole, will be limited; for are not the parts contained by the whole?"],["","Certainly."],["","And that which contains, is a limit?"],["","Of course."],["","Then the one if it has being is one and many, whole and parts, having limits and yet unlimited in number?"],["","Clearly."],["","And because having limits, also having extremes?"],["","Certainly."],["","And if a whole, having beginning and middle and end. For can anything be a whole without these three? And if any one of them is wanting to anything, will that any longer be a whole?"],["","No."],["","Then the one, as appears, will have beginning, middle, and end."],["","It will."],["","But, again, the middle will be equidistant from the extremes; or it would not be in the middle?"],["","Yes."],["","Then the one will partake of figure, either rectilinear or round, or a union of the two?"],["","True."],["","And if this is the case, it will be both in itself and in another too."],["","How?"],["","Every part is in the whole, and none is outside the whole."],["","True."],["","And all the parts are contained by the whole?"],["","Yes."],["","And the one is all its parts, and neither more nor less than all?"],["","No."],["","And the one is the whole?"],["","Of course."],["","But if all the parts are in the whole, and the one is all of them and the whole, and they are all contained by the whole, the one will be contained by the one; and thus the one will be in itself."],["","That is true."],["","But then, again, the whole is not in the parts—neither in all the parts, nor in some one of them. For if it is in all, it must be in one; for if there were any one in which it was not, it could not be in all the parts; for the part in which it is wanting is one of all, and if the whole is not in this, how can it be in them all?"],["","It cannot."],["","Nor can the whole be in some of the parts; for if the whole were in some of the parts, the greater would be in the less, which is impossible."],["","Yes, impossible."],["","But if the whole is neither in one, nor in more than one, nor in all of the parts, it must be in something else, or cease to be anywhere at all?"],["","Certainly."],["","If it were nowhere, it would be nothing; but being a whole, and not being in itself, it must be in another."],["","Very true."],["","The one then, regarded as a whole, is in another, but regarded as being all its parts, is in itself; and therefore the one must be itself in itself and also in another."],["","Certainly."],["","The one then, being of this nature, is of necessity both at rest and in motion?"],["","How?"],["","The one is at rest since it is in itself, for being in one, and not passing out of this, it is in the same, which is itself."],["","True."],["","And that which is ever in the same, must be ever at rest?"],["","Certainly."],["","Well, and must not that, on the contrary, which is ever in other, never be in the same; and if never in the same, never at rest, and if not at rest, in motion?"],["","True."],["","Then the one being always itself in itself and other, must always be both at rest and in motion?"],["","Clearly."],["","And must be the same with itself, and other than itself; and also the same with the others, and other than the others; this follows from its previous affections."],["","How so?"],["","Everything in relation to every other thing, is either the same or other; or if neither the same nor other, then in the relation of a part to a whole, or of a whole to a part."],["","Clearly."],["","And is the one a part of itself?"],["","Certainly not."],["","Since it is not a part in relation to itself it cannot be related to itself as whole to part?"],["","It cannot."],["","But is the one other than one?"],["","No."],["","And therefore not other than itself?"],["","Certainly not."],["","If then it be neither other, nor a whole, nor a part in relation to itself, must it not be the same with itself?"],["","Certainly."],["","But then, again, a thing which is in another place from 'itself,' if this 'itself' remains in the same place with itself, must be other than 'itself,' for it will be in another place?"],["","True."],["","Then the one has been shown to be at once in itself and in another?"],["","Yes."],["","Thus, then, as appears, the one will be other than itself?"],["","True."],["","Well, then, if anything be other than anything, will it not be other than that which is other?"],["","Certainly."],["","And will not all things that are not one, be other than the one, and the one other than the not-one?"],["","Of course."],["","Then the one will be other than the others?"],["","True."],["","But, consider:—Are not the absolute same, and the absolute other, opposites to one another?"],["","Of course."],["","Then will the same ever be in the other, or the other in the same?"],["","They will not."],["","If then the other is never in the same, there is nothing in which the other is during any space of time; for during that space of time, however small, the other would be in the same. Is not that true?"],["","Yes."],["","And since the other is never in the same, it can never be in anything that is."],["","True."],["","Then the other will never be either in the not-one, or in the one?"],["","Certainly not."],["","Then not by reason of otherness is the one other than the not-one, or the not-one other than the one."],["","No."],["","Nor by reason of themselves will they be other than one another, if not partaking of the other."],["","How can they be?"],["","But if they are not other, either by reason of themselves or of the other, will they not altogether escape being other than one another?"],["","They will."],["","Again, the not-one cannot partake of the one; otherwise it would not have been not-one, but would have been in some way one."],["","True."],["","Nor can the not-one be number; for having number, it would not have been not-one at all."],["","It would not."],["","Again, is the not-one part of the one; or rather, would it not in that case partake of the one?"],["","It would."],["","If then, in every point of view, the one and the not-one are distinct, then neither is the one part or whole of the not-one, nor is the not-one part or whole of the one?"],["","No."],["","But we said that things which are neither parts nor wholes of one another, nor other than one another, will be the same with one another:—so we said?"],["","Yes."],["","Then shall we say that the one, being in this relation to the not-one, is the same with it?"],["","Let us say so."],["","Then it is the same with itself and the others, and also other than itself and the others."],["","That appears to be the inference."],["","And it will also be like and unlike itself and the others?"],["","Perhaps."],["","Since the one was shown to be other than the others, the others will also be other than the one."],["","Yes."],["","And the one is other than the others in the same degree that the others are other than it, and neither more nor less?"],["","True."],["","And if neither more nor less, then in a like degree?"],["","Yes."],["","In virtue of the affection by which the one is other than others and others in like manner other than it, the one will be affected like the others and the others like the one."],["","How do you mean?"],["","I may take as an illustration the case of names: You give a name to a thing?"],["","Yes."],["","And you may say the name once or oftener?"],["","Yes."],["","And when you say it once, you mention that of which it is the name? and when more than once, is it something else which you mention? or must it always be the same thing of which you speak, whether you utter the name once or more than once?"],["","Of course it is the same."],["","And is not 'other' a name given to a thing?"],["","Certainly."],["","Whenever, then, you use the word 'other,' whether once or oftener, you name that of which it is the name, and to no other do you give the name?"],["","True."],["","Then when we say that the others are other than the one, and the one other than the others, in repeating the word 'other' we speak of that nature to which the name is applied, and of no other?"],["","Quite true."],["","Then the one which is other than others, and the other which is other than the one, in that the word 'other' is applied to both, will be in the same condition; and that which is in the same condition is like?"],["","Yes."],["","Then in virtue of the affection by which the one is other than the others, every thing will be like every thing, for every thing is other than every thing."],["","True."],["","Again, the like is opposed to the unlike?"],["","Yes."],["","And the other to the same?"],["","True again."],["","And the one was also shown to be the same with the others?"],["","Yes."],["","And to be the same with the others is the opposite of being other than the others?"],["","Certainly."],["","And in that it was other it was shown to be like?"],["","Yes."],["","But in that it was the same it will be unlike by virtue of the opposite affection to that which made it like; and this was the affection of otherness."],["","Yes."],["","The same then will make it unlike; otherwise it will not be the opposite of the other."],["","True."],["","Then the one will be both like and unlike the others; like in so far as it is other, and unlike in so far as it is the same."],["","Yes, that argument may be used."],["","And there is another argument."],["","What?"],["","In so far as it is affected in the same way it is not affected otherwise, and not being affected otherwise is not unlike, and not being unlike, is like; but in so far as it is affected by other it is otherwise, and being otherwise affected is unlike."],["","True."],["","Then because the one is the same with the others and other than the others, on either of these two grounds, or on both of them, it will be both like and unlike the others?"],["","Certainly."],["","And in the same way as being other than itself and the same with itself, on either of these two grounds and on both of them, it will be like and unlike itself?"],["","Of course."]]},{"tag":"148d","title":"Touching and not touching","paras":[["","Again, how far can the one touch or not touch itself and others?—consider."],["","I am considering."],["","The one was shown to be in itself which was a whole?"],["","True."],["","And also in other things?"],["","Yes."],["","In so far as it is in other things it would touch other things, but in so far as it is in itself it would be debarred from touching them, and would touch itself only."],["","Clearly."],["","Then the inference is that it would touch both?"],["","It would."],["","But what do you say to a new point of view? Must not that which is to touch another be next to that which it is to touch, and occupy the place nearest to that in which what it touches is situated?"],["","True."],["","Then the one, if it is to touch itself, ought to be situated next to itself, and occupy the place next to that in which itself is?"],["","It ought."],["","And that would require that the one should be two, and be in two places at once, and this, while it is one, will never happen."],["","No."],["","Then the one cannot touch itself any more than it can be two?"],["","It cannot."],["","Neither can it touch others."],["","Why not?"],["","The reason is, that whatever is to touch another must be in separation from, and next to, that which it is to touch, and no third thing can be between them."],["","True."],["","Two things, then, at the least are necessary to make contact possible?"],["","They are."],["","And if to the two a third be added in due order, the number of terms will be three, and the contacts two?"],["","Yes."],["","And every additional term makes one additional contact, whence it follows that the contacts are one less in number than the terms; the first two terms exceeded the number of contacts by one, and the whole number of terms exceeds the whole number of contacts by one in like manner; and for every one which is afterwards added to the number of terms, one contact is added to the contacts."],["","True."],["","Whatever is the whole number of things, the contacts will be always one less."],["","True."],["","But if there be only one, and not two, there will be no contact?"],["","How can there be?"],["","And do we not say that the others being other than the one are not one and have no part in the one?"],["","True."],["","Then they have no number, if they have no one in them?"],["","Of course not."],["","Then the others are neither one nor two, nor are they called by the name of any number?"],["","No."],["","One, then, alone is one, and two do not exist?"],["","Clearly not."],["","And if there are not two, there is no contact?"],["","There is not."],["","Then neither does the one touch the others, nor the others the one, if there is no contact?"],["","Certainly not."],["","For all which reasons the one touches and does not touch itself and the others?"],["","True."]]},{"tag":"149d","title":"Equal and unequal, greater and less","paras":[["","Further—is the one equal and unequal to itself and others?"],["","How do you mean?"],["","If the one were greater or less than the others, or the others greater or less than the one, they would not be greater or less than each other in virtue of their being the one and the others; but, if in addition to their being what they are they had equality, they would be equal to one another, or if the one had smallness and the others greatness, or the one had greatness and the others smallness—whichever kind had greatness would be greater, and whichever had smallness would be smaller?"],["","Certainly."],["","Then there are two such ideas as greatness and smallness; for if they were not they could not be opposed to each other and be present in that which is."],["","How could they?"],["","If, then, smallness is present in the one it will be present either in the whole or in a part of the whole?"],["","Certainly."],["","Suppose the first; it will be either co-equal and co-extensive with the whole one, or will contain the one?"],["","Clearly."],["","If it be co-extensive with the one it will be co-equal with the one, or if containing the one it will be greater than the one?"],["","Of course."],["","But can smallness be equal to anything or greater than anything, and have the functions of greatness and equality and not its own functions?"],["","Impossible."],["","Then smallness cannot be in the whole of one, but, if at all, in a part only?"],["","Yes."],["","And surely not in all of a part, for then the difficulty of the whole will recur; it will be equal to or greater than any part in which it is."],["","Certainly."],["","Then smallness will not be in anything, whether in a whole or in a part; nor will there be anything small but actual smallness."],["","True."],["","Neither will greatness be in the one, for if greatness be in anything there will be something greater other and besides greatness itself, namely, that in which greatness is; and this too when the small itself is not there, which the one, if it is great, must exceed; this, however, is impossible, seeing that smallness is wholly absent."],["","True."],["","But absolute greatness is only greater than absolute smallness, and smallness is only smaller than absolute greatness."],["","Very true."],["","Then other things not greater or less than the one, if they have neither greatness nor smallness; nor have greatness or smallness any power of exceeding or being exceeded in relation to the one, but only in relation to one another; nor will the one be greater or less than them or others, if it has neither greatness nor smallness."],["","Clearly not."],["","Then if the one is neither greater nor less than the others, it cannot either exceed or be exceeded by them?"],["","Certainly not."],["","And that which neither exceeds nor is exceeded, must be on an equality; and being on an equality, must be equal."],["","Of course."],["","And this will be true also of the relation of the one to itself; having neither greatness nor smallness in itself, it will neither exceed nor be exceeded by itself, but will be on an equality with and equal to itself."],["","Certainly."],["","Then the one will be equal both to itself and the others?"],["","Clearly so."],["","And yet the one, being itself in itself, will also surround and be without itself; and, as containing itself, will be greater than itself; and, as contained in itself, will be less; and will thus be greater and less than itself."],["","It will."],["","Now there cannot possibly be anything which is not included in the one and the others?"],["","Of course not."],["","But, surely, that which is must always be somewhere?"],["","Yes."],["","But that which is in anything will be less, and that in which it is will be greater; in no other way can one thing be in another."],["","True."],["","And since there is nothing other or besides the one and the others, and they must be in something, must they not be in one another, the one in the others and the others in the one, if they are to be anywhere?"],["","That is clear."],["","But inasmuch as the one is in the others, the others will be greater than the one, because they contain the one, which will be less than the others, because it is contained in them; and inasmuch as the others are in the one, the one on the same principle will be greater than the others, and the others less than the one."],["","True."],["","The one, then, will be equal to and greater and less than itself and the others?"],["","Clearly."],["","And if it be greater and less and equal, it will be of equal and more and less measures or divisions than itself and the others, and if of measures, also of parts?"],["","Of course."],["","And if of equal and more and less measures or divisions, it will be in number more or less than itself and the others, and likewise equal in number to itself and to the others?"],["","How is that?"],["","It will be of more measures than those things which it exceeds, and of as many parts as measures; and so with that to which it is equal, and that than which it is less."],["","True."],["","And being greater and less than itself, and equal to itself, it will be of equal measures with itself and of more and fewer measures than itself; and if of measures then also of parts?"],["","It will."],["","And being of equal parts with itself, it will be numerically equal to itself; and being of more parts, more, and being of less, less than itself?"],["","Certainly."],["","And the same will hold of its relation to other things; inasmuch as it is greater than them, it will be more in number than them; and inasmuch as it is smaller, it will be less in number; and inasmuch as it is equal in size to other things, it will be equal to them in number."],["","Certainly."],["","Once more, then, as would appear, the one will be in number both equal to and more and less than both itself and all other things."],["","It will."]]},{"tag":"151e","title":"The one and time","paras":[["","Does the one also partake of time? And is it and does it become older and younger than itself and others, and again, neither younger nor older than itself and others, by virtue of participation in time?"],["","How do you mean?"],["","If one is, being must be predicated of it?"],["","Yes."],["","But to be (einai) is only participation of being in present time, and to have been is the participation of being at a past time, and to be about to be is the participation of being at a future time?"],["","Very true."],["","Then the one, since it partakes of being, partakes of time?"],["","Certainly."],["","And is not time always moving forward?"],["","Yes."],["","Then the one is always becoming older than itself, since it moves forward in time?"],["","Certainly."],["","And do you remember that the older becomes older than that which becomes younger?"],["","I remember."],["","Then since the one becomes older than itself, it becomes younger at the same time?"],["","Certainly."],["","Thus, then, the one becomes older as well as younger than itself?"],["","Yes."],["","And it is older (is it not?) when in becoming, it gets to the point of time between 'was' and 'will be,' which is 'now': for surely in going from the past to the future, it cannot skip the present?"],["","No."],["","And when it arrives at the present it stops from becoming older, and no longer becomes, but is older, for if it went on it would never be reached by the present, for it is the nature of that which goes on, to touch both the present and the future, letting go the present and seizing the future, while in process of becoming between them."],["","True."],["","But that which is becoming cannot skip the present; when it reaches the present it ceases to become, and is then whatever it may happen to be becoming."],["","Clearly."],["","And so the one, when in becoming older it reaches the present, ceases to become, and is then older."],["","Certainly."],["","And it is older than that than which it was becoming older, and it was becoming older than itself."],["","Yes."],["","And that which is older is older than that which is younger?"],["","True."],["","Then the one is younger than itself, when in becoming older it reaches the present?"],["","Certainly."],["","But the present is always present with the one during all its being; for whenever it is it is always now."],["","Certainly."],["","Then the one always both is and becomes older and younger than itself?"],["","Truly."],["","And is it or does it become a longer time than itself or an equal time with itself?"],["","An equal time."],["","But if it becomes or is for an equal time with itself, it is of the same age with itself?"],["","Of course."],["","And that which is of the same age, is neither older nor younger?"],["","No."],["","The one, then, becoming and being the same time with itself, neither is nor becomes older or younger than itself?"],["","I should say not."],["","And what are its relations to other things? Is it or does it become older or younger than they?"],["","I cannot tell you."],["","You can at least tell me that others than the one are more than the one—other would have been one, but the others have multitude, and are more than one?"],["","They will have multitude."],["","And a multitude implies a number larger than one?"],["","Of course."],["","And shall we say that the lesser or the greater is the first to come or to have come into existence?"],["","The lesser."],["","Then the least is the first? And that is the one?"],["","Yes."],["","Then the one of all things that have number is the first to come into being; but all other things have also number, being plural and not singular."],["","They have."],["","And since it came into being first it must be supposed to have come into being prior to the others, and the others later; and the things which came into being later, are younger than that which preceded them? And so the other things will be younger than the one, and the one older than other things?"],["","True."],["","What would you say of another question? Can the one have come into being contrary to its own nature, or is that impossible?"],["","Impossible."],["","And yet, surely, the one was shown to have parts; and if parts, then a beginning, middle and end?"],["","Yes."],["","And a beginning, both of the one itself and of all other things, comes into being first of all; and after the beginning, the others follow, until you reach the end?"],["","Certainly."],["","And all these others we shall affirm to be parts of the whole and of the one, which, as soon as the end is reached, has become whole and one?"],["","Yes; that is what we shall say."],["","But the end comes last, and the one is of such a nature as to come into being with the last; and, since the one cannot come into being except in accordance with its own nature, its nature will require that it should come into being after the others, simultaneously with the end."],["","Clearly."],["","Then the one is younger than the others and the others older than the one."],["","That also is clear in my judgment."],["","Well, and must not a beginning or any other part of the one or of anything, if it be a part and not parts, being a part, be also of necessity one?"],["","Certainly."],["","And will not the one come into being together with each part—together with the first part when that comes into being, and together with the second part and with all the rest, and will not be wanting to any part, which is added to any other part until it has reached the last and become one whole; it will be wanting neither to the middle, nor to the first, nor to the last, nor to any of them, while the process of becoming is going on?"],["","True."],["","Then the one is of the same age with all the others, so that if the one itself does not contradict its own nature, it will be neither prior nor posterior to the others, but simultaneous; and according to this argument the one will be neither older nor younger than the others, nor the others than the one, but according to the previous argument the one will be older and younger than the others and the others than the one."],["","Certainly."],["","After this manner then the one is and has become. But as to its becoming older and younger than the others, and the others than the one, and neither older nor younger, what shall we say? Shall we say as of being so also of becoming, or otherwise?"],["","I cannot answer."],["","But I can venture to say, that even if one thing were older or younger than another, it could not become older or younger in a greater degree than it was at first; for equals added to unequals, whether to periods of time or to anything else, leave the difference between them the same as at first."],["","Of course."],["","Then that which is, cannot become older or younger than that which is, since the difference of age is always the same; the one is and has become older and the other younger; but they are no longer becoming so."],["","True."],["","And the one which is does not therefore become either older or younger than the others which are."],["","No."],["","But consider whether they may not become older and younger in another way."],["","In what way?"],["","Just as the one was proven to be older than the others and the others than the one."],["","And what of that?"],["","If the one is older than the others, has come into being a longer time than the others."],["","Yes."],["","But consider again; if we add equal time to a greater and a less time, will the greater differ from the less time by an equal or by a smaller portion than before?"],["","By a smaller portion."],["","Then the difference between the age of the one and the age of the others will not be afterwards so great as at first, but if an equal time be added to both of them they will differ less and less in age?"],["","Yes."],["","And that which differs in age from some other less than formerly, from being older will become younger in relation to that other than which it was older?"],["","Yes, younger."],["","And if the one becomes younger the others aforesaid will become older than they were before, in relation to the one."],["","Certainly."],["","Then that which had become younger becomes older relatively to that which previously had become and was older; it never really is older, but is always becoming, for the one is always growing on the side of youth and the other on the side of age. And in like manner the older is always in process of becoming younger than the younger; for as they are always going in opposite directions they become in ways the opposite to one another, the younger older than the older, and the older younger than the younger. They cannot, however, have become; for if they had already become they would be and not merely become. But that is impossible; for they are always becoming both older and younger than one another: the one becomes younger than the others because it was seen to be older and prior, and the others become older than the one because they came into being later; and in the same way the others are in the same relation to the one, because they were seen to be older, and prior to the one."],["","That is clear."],["","Inasmuch then, one thing does not become older or younger than another, in that they always differ from each other by an equal number, the one cannot become older or younger than the others, nor the others than the one; but inasmuch as that which came into being earlier and that which came into being later must continually differ from each other by a different portion—in this point of view the others must become older and younger than the one, and the one than the others."],["","Certainly."],["","For all these reasons, then, the one is and becomes older and younger than itself and the others, and neither is nor becomes older or younger than itself or the others."],["","Certainly."],["","But since the one partakes of time, and partakes of becoming older and younger, must it not also partake of the past, the present, and the future?"],["","Of course it must."],["","Then the one was and is and will be, and was becoming and is becoming and will become?"],["","Certainly."],["","And there is and was and will be something which is in relation to it and belongs to it?"],["","True."],["","And since we have at this moment opinion and knowledge and perception of the one, there is opinion and knowledge and perception of it?"],["","Quite right."],["","Then there is name and expression for it, and it is named and expressed, and everything of this kind which appertains to other things appertains to the one."],["","Certainly, that is true."]]},{"tag":"155e","title":"Taking and losing being","paras":[["","Yet once more and for the third time, let us consider: If the one is both one and many, as we have described, and is neither one nor many, and participates in time, must it not, in as far as it is one, at times partake of being, and in as far as it is not one, at times not partake of being?"],["","Certainly."],["","But can it partake of being when not partaking of being, or not partake of being when partaking of being?"],["","Impossible."],["","Then the one partakes and does not partake of being at different times, for that is the only way in which it can partake and not partake of the same."],["","True."],["","And is there not also a time at which it assumes being and relinquishes being—for how can it have and not have the same thing unless it receives and also gives it up at some time?"],["","Impossible."],["","And the assuming of being is what you would call becoming?"],["","I should."],["","And the relinquishing of being you would call destruction?"],["","I should."],["","The one then, as would appear, becomes and is destroyed by taking and giving up being."],["","Certainly."],["","And being one and many and in process of becoming and being destroyed, when it becomes one it ceases to be many, and when many, it ceases to be one?"],["","Certainly."],["","And as it becomes one and many, must it not inevitably experience separation and aggregation?"],["","Inevitably."],["","And whenever it becomes like and unlike it must be assimilated and dissimilated?"],["","Yes."],["","And when it becomes greater or less or equal it must grow or diminish or be equalized?"],["","True."],["","And when being in motion it rests, and when being at rest it changes to motion, it can surely be in no time at all?"],["","How can it?"],["","But that a thing which is previously at rest should be afterwards in motion, or previously in motion and afterwards at rest, without experiencing change, is impossible."],["","Impossible."],["","And surely there cannot be a time in which a thing can be at once neither in motion nor at rest?"],["","There cannot."],["","But neither can it change without changing."],["","True."],["","When then does it change; for it cannot change either when at rest, or when in motion, or when in time?"],["","It cannot."]]},{"tag":"156d","title":"The instant","paras":[["","And does this strange thing in which it is at the time of changing really exist?"],["","What thing?"],["","The moment. For the moment seems to imply a something out of which change takes place into either of two states; for the change is not from the state of rest as such, nor from the state of motion as such; but there is this curious nature which we call the moment lying between rest and motion, not being in any time; and into this and out of this what is in motion changes into rest, and what is at rest into motion."],["","So it appears."],["","And the one then, since it is at rest and also in motion, will change to either, for only in this way can it be in both. And in changing it changes in a moment, and when it is changing it will be in no time, and will not then be either in motion or at rest."],["","It will not."],["","And it will be in the same case in relation to the other changes, when it passes from being into cessation of being, or from not-being into becoming—then it passes between certain states of motion and rest, and neither is nor is not, nor becomes nor is destroyed."],["","Very true."],["","And on the same principle, in the passage from one to many and from many to one, the one is neither one nor many, neither separated nor aggregated; and in the passage from like to unlike, and from unlike to like, it is neither like nor unlike, neither in a state of assimilation nor of dissimilation; and in the passage from small to great and equal and back again, it will be neither small nor great, nor equal, nor in a state of increase, or diminution, or equalization."],["","True."],["","All these, then, are the affections of the one, if the one has being."],["","Of course."]]},{"tag":"157b","title":"If the one is: the others","paras":[["","1.aa. But if one is, what will happen to the others—is not that also to be considered?"],["","Yes."],["","Let us show then, if one is, what will be the affections of the others than the one."],["","Let us do so."],["","Inasmuch as there are things other than the one, the others are not the one; for if they were they could not be other than the one."],["","Very true."],["","Nor are the others altogether without the one, but in a certain way they participate in the one."],["","In what way?"],["","Because the others are other than the one inasmuch as they have parts; for if they had no parts they would be simply one."],["","Right."],["","And parts, as we affirm, have relation to a whole?"],["","So we say."],["","And a whole must necessarily be one made up of many; and the parts will be parts of the one, for each of the parts is not a part of many, but of a whole."],["","How do you mean?"],["","If anything were a part of many, being itself one of them, it will surely be a part of itself, which is impossible, and it will be a part of each one of the other parts, if of all; for if not a part of some one, it will be a part of all the others but this one, and thus will not be a part of each one; and if not a part of each, one it will not be a part of any one of the many; and not being a part of any one, it cannot be a part or anything else of all those things of none of which it is anything."],["","Clearly not."],["","Then the part is not a part of the many, nor of all, but is of a certain single form, which we call a whole, being one perfect unity framed out of all—of this the part will be a part."],["","Certainly."],["","If, then, the others have parts, they will participate in the whole and in the one."],["","True."],["","Then the others than the one must be one perfect whole, having parts."],["","Certainly."],["","And the same argument holds of each part, for the part must participate in the one; for if each of the parts is a part, this means, I suppose, that it is one separate from the rest and self-related; otherwise it is not each."],["","True."],["","But when we speak of the part participating in the one, it must clearly be other than one; for if not, it would not merely have participated, but would have been one; whereas only the itself can be one."],["","Very true."],["","Both the whole and the part must participate in the one; for the whole will be one whole, of which the parts will be parts; and each part will be one part of the whole which is the whole of the part."],["","True."],["","And will not the things which participate in the one, be other than it?"],["","Of course."],["","And the things which are other than the one will be many; for if the things which are other than the one were neither one nor more than one, they would be nothing."],["","True."],["","But, seeing that the things which participate in the one as a part, and in the one as a whole, are more than one, must not those very things which participate in the one be infinite in number?"],["","How so?"],["","Let us look at the matter thus:—Is it not a fact that in partaking of the one they are not one, and do not partake of the one at the very time when they are partaking of it?"],["","Clearly."],["","They do so then as multitudes in which the one is not present?"],["","Very true."],["","And if we were to abstract from them in idea the very smallest fraction, must not that least fraction, if it does not partake of the one, be a multitude and not one?"],["","It must."],["","And if we continue to look at the other side of their nature, regarded simply, and in itself, will not they, as far as we see them, be unlimited in number?"],["","Certainly."],["","And yet, when each several part becomes a part, then the parts have a limit in relation to the whole and to each other, and the whole in relation to the parts."],["","Just so."],["","The result to the others than the one is that the union of themselves and the one appears to create a new element in them which gives to them limitation in relation to one another; whereas in their own nature they have no limit."],["","That is clear."],["","Then the others than the one, both as whole and parts, are infinite, and also partake of limit."],["","Certainly."],["","Then they are both like and unlike one another and themselves."],["","How is that?"],["","Inasmuch as they are unlimited in their own nature, they are all affected in the same way."],["","True."],["","And inasmuch as they all partake of limit, they are all affected in the same way."],["","Of course."],["","But inasmuch as their state is both limited and unlimited, they are affected in opposite ways."],["","Yes."],["","And opposites are the most unlike of things."],["","Certainly."],["","Considered, then, in regard to either one of their affections, they will be like themselves and one another; considered in reference to both of them together, most opposed and most unlike."],["","That appears to be true."],["","Then the others are both like and unlike themselves and one another?"],["","True."],["","And they are the same and also different from one another, and in motion and at rest, and experience every sort of opposite affection, as may be proved without difficulty of them, since they have been shown to have experienced the affections aforesaid?"],["","True."]]},{"tag":"159b","title":"The others cut off from the one","paras":[["","1.bb. Suppose, now, that we leave the further discussion of these matters as evident, and consider again upon the hypothesis that the one is, whether opposite of all this is or is not equally true of the others."],["","By all means."],["","Then let us begin again, and ask, If one is, what must be the affections of the others?"],["","Let us ask that question."],["","Must not the one be distinct from the others, and the others from the one?"],["","Why so?"],["","Why, because there is nothing else beside them which is distinct from both of them; for the expression 'one and the others' includes all things."],["","Yes, all things."],["","Then we cannot suppose that there is anything different from them in which both the one and the others might exist?"],["","There is nothing."],["","Then the one and the others are never in the same?"],["","True."],["","Then they are separated from each other?"],["","Yes."],["","And we surely cannot say that what is truly one has parts?"],["","Impossible."],["","Then the one will not be in the others as a whole, nor as part, if it be separated from the others, and has no parts?"],["","Impossible."],["","Then there is no way in which the others can partake of the one, if they do not partake either in whole or in part?"],["","It would seem not."],["","Then there is no way in which the others are one, or have in themselves any unity?"],["","There is not."],["","Nor are the others many; for if they were many, each part of them would be a part of the whole; but now the others, not partaking in any way of the one, are neither one nor many, nor whole, nor part."],["","True."],["","Then the others neither are nor contain two or three, if entirely deprived of the one?"],["","True."],["","Then the others are neither like nor unlike the one, nor is likeness and unlikeness in them; for if they were like and unlike, or had in them likeness and unlikeness, they would have two natures in them opposite to one another."],["","That is clear."],["","But for that which partakes of nothing to partake of two things was held by us to be impossible?"],["","Impossible."],["","Then the others are neither like nor unlike nor both, for if they were like or unlike they would partake of one of those two natures, which would be one thing, and if they were both they would partake of opposites which would be two things, and this has been shown to be impossible."],["","True."],["","Therefore they are neither the same, nor other, nor in motion, nor at rest, nor in a state of becoming, nor of being destroyed, nor greater, nor less, nor equal, nor have they experienced anything else of the sort; for, if they are capable of experiencing any such affection, they will participate in one and two and three, and odd and even, and in these, as has been proved, they do not participate, seeing that they are altogether and in every way devoid of the one."],["","Very true."],["","Therefore if one is, the one is all things, and also nothing, both in relation to itself and to other things."],["","Certainly."]]},{"tag":"160b","title":"Deduction: if the one is not","paras":[["","2.a. Well, and ought we not to consider next what will be the consequence if the one is not?"],["","Yes; we ought."],["","What is the meaning of the hypothesis—If the one is not; is there any difference between this and the hypothesis—If the not one is not?"],["","There is a difference, certainly."],["","Is there a difference only, or rather are not the two expressions—if the one is not, and if the not one is not, entirely opposed?"],["","They are entirely opposed."],["","And suppose a person to say:—If greatness is not, if smallness is not, or anything of that sort, does he not mean, whenever he uses such an expression, that 'what is not' is other than other things?"],["","To be sure."],["","And so when he says 'If one is not' he clearly means, that what 'is not' is other than all others; we know what he means—do we not?"],["","Yes, we do."],["","When he says 'one,' he says something which is known; and secondly something which is other than all other things; it makes no difference whether he predicate of one being or not-being, for that which is said 'not to be' is known to be something all the same, and is distinguished from other things."],["","Certainly."],["","Then I will begin again, and ask: If one is not, what are the consequences? In the first place, as would appear, there is a knowledge of it, or the very meaning of the words, 'if one is not,' would not be known."],["","True."],["","Secondly, the others differ from it, or it could not be described as different from the others?"],["","Certainly."],["","Difference, then, belongs to it as well as knowledge; for in speaking of the one as different from the others, we do not speak of a difference in the others, but in the one."],["","Clearly so."],["","Moreover, the one that is not is something and partakes of relation to 'that,' and 'this,' and 'these,' and the like, and is an attribute of 'this'; for the one, or the others than the one, could not have been spoken of, nor could any attribute or relative of the one that is not have been or been spoken of, nor could it have been said to be anything, if it did not partake of 'some,' or of the other relations just now mentioned."],["","True."],["","Being, then, cannot be ascribed to the one, since it is not; but the one that is not may or rather must participate in many things, if it and nothing else is not; if, however, neither the one nor the one that is not is supposed not to be, and we are speaking of something of a different nature, we can predicate nothing of it. But supposing that the one that is not and nothing else is not, then it must participate in the predicate 'that,' and in many others."],["","Certainly."],["","And it will have unlikeness in relation to the others, for the others being different from the one will be of a different kind."],["","Certainly."],["","And are not things of a different kind also other in kind?"],["","Of course."],["","And are not things other in kind unlike?"],["","They are unlike."],["","And if they are unlike the one, that which they are unlike will clearly be unlike them?"],["","Clearly so."],["","Then the one will have unlikeness in respect of which the others are unlike it?"],["","That would seem to be true."],["","And if unlikeness to other things is attributed to it, it must have likeness to itself."],["","How so?"],["","If the one have unlikeness to one, something else must be meant; nor will the hypothesis relate to one; but it will relate to something other than one?"],["","Quite so."],["","But that cannot be."],["","No."],["","Then the one must have likeness to itself?"],["","It must."],["","Again, it is not equal to the others; for if it were equal, then it would at once be and be like them in virtue of the equality; but if one has no being, then it can neither be nor be like?"],["","It cannot."],["","But since it is not equal to the others, neither can the others be equal to it?"],["","Certainly not."],["","And things that are not equal are unequal?"],["","True."],["","And they are unequal to an unequal?"],["","Of course."],["","Then the one partakes of inequality, and in respect of this the others are unequal to it?"],["","Very true."],["","And inequality implies greatness and smallness?"],["","Yes."],["","Then the one, if of such a nature, has greatness and smallness?"],["","That appears to be true."],["","And greatness and smallness always stand apart?"],["","True."],["","Then there is always something between them?"],["","There is."],["","And can you think of anything else which is between them other than equality?"],["","No, it is equality which lies between them."],["","Then that which has greatness and smallness also has equality, which lies between them?"],["","That is clear."],["","Then the one, which is not, partakes, as would appear, of greatness and smallness and equality?"],["","Clearly."]]},{"tag":"161e","title":"The one that is not partakes of being","paras":[["","Further, it must surely in a sort partake of being?"],["","How so?"],["","It must be so, for if not, then we should not speak the truth in saying that the one is not. But if we speak the truth, clearly we must say what is. Am I not right?"],["","Yes."],["","And since we affirm that we speak truly, we must also affirm that we say what is?"],["","Certainly."],["","Then, as would appear, the one, when it is not, is; for if it were not to be when it is not, but (Or, 'to remit something of existence in relation to not-being.') were to relinquish something of being, so as to become not-being, it would at once be."],["","Quite true."],["","Then the one which is not, if it is to maintain itself, must have the being of not-being as the bond of not-being, just as being must have as a bond the not-being of not-being in order to perfect its own being; for the truest assertion of the being of being and of the not-being of not-being is when being partakes of the being of being, and not of the being of not-being—that is, the perfection of being; and when not-being does not partake of the not-being of not-being but of the being of not-being—that is the perfection of not-being."],["","Most true."],["","Since then what is partakes of not-being, and what is not of being, must not the one also partake of being in order not to be?"],["","Certainly."],["","Then the one, if it is not, clearly has being?"],["","Clearly."],["","And has not-being also, if it is not?"],["","Of course."],["","But can anything which is in a certain state not be in that state without changing?"],["","Impossible."],["","Then everything which is and is not in a certain state, implies change?"],["","Certainly."],["","And change is motion—we may say that?"],["","Yes, motion."],["","And the one has been proved both to be and not to be?"],["","Yes."],["","And therefore is and is not in the same state?"],["","Yes."],["","Thus the one that is not has been shown to have motion also, because it changes from being to not-being?"],["","That appears to be true."],["","But surely if it is nowhere among what is, as is the fact, since it is not, it cannot change from one place to another?"],["","Impossible."],["","Then it cannot move by changing place?"],["","No."],["","Nor can it turn on the same spot, for it nowhere touches the same, for the same is, and that which is not cannot be reckoned among things that are?"],["","It cannot."],["","Then the one, if it is not, cannot turn in that in which it is not?"],["","No."],["","Neither can the one, whether it is or is not, be altered into other than itself, for if it altered and became different from itself, then we could not be still speaking of the one, but of something else?"],["","True."],["","But if the one neither suffers alteration, nor turns round in the same place, nor changes place, can it still be capable of motion?"],["","Impossible."],["","Now that which is unmoved must surely be at rest, and that which is at rest must stand still?"],["","Certainly."],["","Then the one that is not, stands still, and is also in motion?"],["","That seems to be true."],["","But if it be in motion it must necessarily undergo alteration, for anything which is moved, in so far as it is moved, is no longer in the same state, but in another?"],["","Yes."],["","Then the one, being moved, is altered?"],["","Yes."],["","And, further, if not moved in any way, it will not be altered in any way?"],["","No."],["","Then, in so far as the one that is not is moved, it is altered, but in so far as it is not moved, it is not altered?"],["","Right."],["","Then the one that is not is altered and is not altered?"],["","That is clear."],["","And must not that which is altered become other than it previously was, and lose its former state and be destroyed; but that which is not altered can neither come into being nor be destroyed?"],["","Very true."],["","And the one that is not, being altered, becomes and is destroyed; and not being altered, neither becomes nor is destroyed; and so the one that is not becomes and is destroyed, and neither becomes nor is destroyed?"],["","True."]]},{"tag":"163b","title":"The one that is not, taken absolutely","paras":[["","2.b. And now, let us go back once more to the beginning, and see whether these or some other consequences will follow."],["","Let us do as you say."],["","If one is not, we ask what will happen in respect of one? That is the question."],["","Yes."],["","Do not the words 'is not' signify absence of being in that to which we apply them?"],["","Just so."],["","And when we say that a thing is not, do we mean that it is not in one way but is in another? or do we mean, absolutely, that what is not has in no sort or way or kind participation of being?"],["","Quite absolutely."],["","Then, that which is not cannot be, or in any way participate in being?"],["","It cannot."],["","And did we not mean by becoming, and being destroyed, the assumption of being and the loss of being?"],["","Nothing else."],["","And can that which has no participation in being, either assume or lose being?"],["","Impossible."],["","The one then, since it in no way is, cannot have or lose or assume being in any way?"],["","True."],["","Then the one that is not, since it in no way partakes of being, neither perishes nor becomes?"],["","No."],["","Then it is not altered at all; for if it were it would become and be destroyed?"],["","True."],["","But if it be not altered it cannot be moved?"],["","Certainly not."],["","Nor can we say that it stands, if it is nowhere; for that which stands must always be in one and the same spot?"],["","Of course."],["","Then we must say that the one which is not never stands still and never moves?"],["","Neither."],["","Nor is there any existing thing which can be attributed to it; for if there had been, it would partake of being?"],["","That is clear."],["","And therefore neither smallness, nor greatness, nor equality, can be attributed to it?"],["","No."],["","Nor yet likeness nor difference, either in relation to itself or to others?"],["","Clearly not."],["","Well, and if nothing should be attributed to it, can other things be attributed to it?"],["","Certainly not."],["","And therefore other things can neither be like or unlike, the same, or different in relation to it?"],["","They cannot."],["","Nor can what is not, be anything, or be this thing, or be related to or the attribute of this or that or other, or be past, present, or future. Nor can knowledge, or opinion, or perception, or expression, or name, or any other thing that is, have any concern with it?"],["","No."],["","Then the one that is not has no condition of any kind?"],["","Such appears to be the conclusion."]]},{"tag":"164b","title":"If the one is not: the others as appearances","paras":[["","2.aa. Yet once more; if one is not, what becomes of the others? Let us determine that."],["","Yes; let us determine that."],["","The others must surely be; for if they, like the one, were not, we could not be now speaking of them."],["","True."],["","But to speak of the others implies difference—the terms 'other' and 'different' are synonymous?"],["","True."],["","Other means other than other, and different, different from the different?"],["","Yes."],["","Then, if there are to be others, there is something than which they will be other?"],["","Certainly."],["","And what can that be?—for if the one is not, they will not be other than the one."],["","They will not."],["","Then they will be other than each other; for the only remaining alternative is that they are other than nothing."],["","True."],["","And they are each other than one another, as being plural and not singular; for if one is not, they cannot be singular, but every particle of them is infinite in number; and even if a person takes that which appears to be the smallest fraction, this, which seemed one, in a moment evanesces into many, as in a dream, and from being the smallest becomes very great, in comparison with the fractions into which it is split up?"],["","Very true."],["","And in such particles the others will be other than one another, if others are, and the one is not?"],["","Exactly."],["","And will there not be many particles, each appearing to be one, but not being one, if one is not?"],["","True."],["","And it would seem that number can be predicated of them if each of them appears to be one, though it is really many?"],["","It can."],["","And there will seem to be odd and even among them, which will also have no reality, if one is not?"],["","Yes."],["","And there will appear to be a least among them; and even this will seem large and manifold in comparison with the many small fractions which are contained in it?"],["","Certainly."],["","And each particle will be imagined to be equal to the many and little; for it could not have appeared to pass from the greater to the less without having appeared to arrive at the middle; and thus would arise the appearance of equality."],["","Yes."],["","And having neither beginning, middle, nor end, each separate particle yet appears to have a limit in relation to itself and other."],["","How so?"],["","Because, when a person conceives of any one of these as such, prior to the beginning another beginning appears, and there is another end, remaining after the end, and in the middle truer middles within but smaller, because no unity can be conceived of any of them, since the one is not."],["","Very true."],["","And so all being, whatever we think of, must be broken up into fractions, for a particle will have to be conceived of without unity?"],["","Certainly."],["","And such being when seen indistinctly and at a distance, appears to be one; but when seen near and with keen intellect, every single thing appears to be infinite, since it is deprived of the one, which is not?"],["","Nothing more certain."],["","Then each of the others must appear to be infinite and finite, and one and many, if others than the one exist and not the one."],["","They must."],["","Then will they not appear to be like and unlike?"],["","In what way?"],["","Just as in a picture things appear to be all one to a person standing at a distance, and to be in the same state and alike?"],["","True."],["","But when you approach them, they appear to be many and different; and because of the appearance of the difference, different in kind from, and unlike, themselves?"],["","True."],["","And so must the particles appear to be like and unlike themselves and each other."],["","Certainly."],["","And must they not be the same and yet different from one another, and in contact with themselves, although they are separated, and having every sort of motion, and every sort of rest, and becoming and being destroyed, and in neither state, and the like, all which things may be easily enumerated, if the one is not and the many are?"],["","Most true."]]},{"tag":"165e","title":"If the one is not, nothing is","paras":[["","2.bb. Once more, let us go back to the beginning, and ask if the one is not, and the others of the one are, what will follow."],["","Let us ask that question."],["","In the first place, the others will not be one?"],["","Impossible."],["","Nor will they be many; for if they were many one would be contained in them. But if no one of them is one, all of them are nought, and therefore they will not be many."],["","True."],["","If there be no one in the others, the others are neither many nor one."],["","They are not."],["","Nor do they appear either as one or many."],["","Why not?"],["","Because the others have no sort or manner or way of communion with any sort of not-being, nor can anything which is not, be connected with any of the others; for that which is not has no parts."],["","True."],["","Nor is there an opinion or any appearance of not-being in connexion with the others, nor is not-being ever in any way attributed to the others."],["","No."],["","Then if one is not, there is no conception of any of the others either as one or many; for you cannot conceive the many without the one."],["","You cannot."],["","Then if one is not, the others neither are, nor can be conceived to be either one or many?"],["","It would seem not."],["","Nor as like or unlike?"],["","No."],["","Nor as the same or different, nor in contact or separation, nor in any of those states which we enumerated as appearing to be;—the others neither are nor appear to be any of these, if one is not?"],["","True."],["","Then may we not sum up the argument in a word and say truly: If one is not, then nothing is?"],["","Certainly."],["","Let thus much be said; and further let us affirm what seems to be the truth, that, whether one is or is not, one and the others in relation to themselves and one another, all of them, in every way, are and are not, and appear to be and appear not to be."],["","Most true."]]}],"hg":[{"tag":"126a","title":"Prastaavana: Cephalus, Antiphon aur Parmenides ka aagman","paras":[["","Cephalus ek dialogue dohraata hai jo maana jaata hai ki uski upasthiti mein Antiphon ne, jo Adeimantus aur Glaucon ka sautela bhai hai, kuch Clazomenians ko sunaaya tha.","in"],["","Hum Clazomenae mein apne ghar se Athens aaye the, aur Agora mein Adeimantus aur Glaucon se mile. Swaagat hai, Cephalus, Adeimantus ne mera haath pakadte hue kaha; kya Athens mein hum tumhare liye kuch kar sakte hain?"],["","Haan; isiliye to main yahan hoon; main tumse ek upkaar maangna chahta hoon."],["","Woh kya ho sakta hai? usne kaha."],["","Main chahta hoon ki tum mujhe apne sautele bhai ka naam batao, jo main bhool gaya hoon; jab main pichhli baar Clazomenae se yahan aaya tha tab woh nanha bachcha tha, par woh bahut pehle ki baat hai; uske pita ka naam, agar mujhe sahi yaad hai, Pyrilampes tha?"],["","Haan, usne kaha, aur hamare bhai ka naam, Antiphon; par tum kyun poochhte ho?"],["","Mujhe apne kuch deshvaasiyon ka parichay karaane do, maine kaha; woh philosophy ke premi hain, aur unhone suna hai ki Antiphon ek Pythodorus ka gehra mitra tha, jo Zeno ka mitra tha, aur use ek baatcheet yaad hai jo kai saal pehle Socrates, Zeno, aur Parmenides ke beech hui thi, kyunki Pythodorus ne use aksar woh sunaai thi."],["","Bilkul true."],["","Aur kya hum use sun sakte hain? maine poochha."],["","Isse aasaan kuch nahi, usne jawaab diya; jab woh yuvak tha to usne is ansh ka dhyaan se adhyayan kiya tha; ab uske vichaar doosri disha mein chalte hain; apne dada Antiphon ki tarah woh ghodon ka deewaana hai. Par, agar tum yahi chahte ho, to chalo use dhoondhte hain; woh Melita mein rehta hai, jo bilkul paas hai, aur woh abhi-abhi hamare paas se ghar gaya hai."],["","Isliye hum use dhoondhne gaye; woh ghar par tha, aur ek lohaar ko lagaam theek karne ke liye de raha tha. Jab woh lohaar se nipat gaya, to uske bhaiyon ne use hamare aane ka uddeshya bataaya; aur usne mujhe ek parichit ki tarah abhivaadan kiya jise woh meri pichhli yaatra se yaad rakhta tha, aur humne usse dialogue dohraane ko kaha. Pehle woh bahut ichchhuk nahi tha, aur pareshaani ki shikaayat ki, par ant mein maan gaya. Usne hamein bataaya ki Pythodorus ne use Parmenides aur Zeno ka roop-rang bataaya tha; woh Athens aaye the, jaisa usne kaha, mahaan Panathenaea par; pehla, apni yaatra ke samay, lagbhag 65 saal ka tha, umra se bahut safed, par sundar. Zeno lagbhag 40 saal ka tha, lamba aur dekhne mein sundar; apni jawaani ke dinon mein kaha jaata tha ki woh Parmenides ka priya tha. Usne kaha ki woh Ceramicus mein, deewaar ke baahar, Pythodorus ke saath thehre the, jahan Socrates, tab bahut yuvak, unse milne aaya, aur uske saath kai aur bhi; woh Zeno ki rachnaayein sunna chahte the, jo unki yaatra ke avsar par pehli baar Athens laayi gayi thi. Inhe Zeno ne khud Parmenides ki anupasthiti mein unhe padh kar sunaaya, aur lagbhag khatm kar chuka tha jab Pythodorus andar aaya, aur uske saath Parmenides aur Aristoteles jo baad mein Tees (the Thirty) mein se ek bana, aur jo thoda bacha tha woh suna. Pythodorus ne Zeno ko unhe pehle dohraate suna tha."]]},{"tag":"127d","title":"Zeno ka argument aur Socrates ki Forms theory","paras":[["","Jab paath poora hua, to Socrates ne anurodh kiya ki pehle argument ki pehli thesis phir se padhi jaaye, aur aisa ho jaane par, usne kaha: Tumhara kya matlab hai, Zeno? Kya tum yeh maante ho ki agar being anek hai, to use samaan aur asamaan dono hona hoga, aur ki yeh asambhav hai, kyunki na samaan asamaan ho sakta hai, na asamaan samaan—kya yahi tumhari sthiti hai?"],["","Bilkul aisa hi, Zeno ne kaha."],["","Aur agar asamaan samaan nahi ho sakta, ya samaan asamaan, to tumhare anusaar, being anek nahi ho sakta; kyunki isme ek asambhavta shaamil hogi. Jo kuch tum kehte ho kya usme tumhara anek ke being ko khandit karne ke alawa koi aur uddeshya hai? aur kya tumhare granth ka har vibhaag iska ek alag pramaan dene ke liye nahi, kul milaakar anek ke not-being ke utne pramaan jitne arguments tumne rache hain? Kya yahi tumhara matlab hai, ya maine tumhe galat samjha?"],["","Nahi, Zeno ne kaha; tumne mera saamaanya uddeshya sahi samjha hai."],["","Main dekhta hoon, Parmenides, Socrates ne kaha, ki Zeno na sirf mitrata mein tumhare saath ek hona chahta hai balki apni rachnaaon mein bhi tumhara doosra roop; woh jo tum kehte ho use doosre dhang se rakhta hai, aur yeh dikhaava karna chahta hai ki woh hamein kuch naya bata raha hai. Kyunki tum, apni kavitaaon mein, kehte ho Sab ek hai (The All is one), aur iske utkrisht pramaan dete ho; aur woh doosri or kehta hai Anek nahi hai; aur iske paksh mein bhaari saakshya deta hai. Tum ekta ko sweekaar karte ho, woh bahulta ko nakaarta hai. Aur is tarah tum duniya ko yeh maanne ka dhokha dete ho ki tum alag-alag baatein keh rahe ho jabki vaastav mein tum lagbhag same baat keh rahe ho. Yeh kala ka aisa kamaal hai jo hum mein se zyaadatar ki pahunch se baahar hai."],["","Haan, Socrates, Zeno ne kaha. Par haalaanki tum nishaan ka peechha karne mein Spartan shikaari kutte jitne tez ho, tum rachna ke sachche uddeshya ko poori tarah nahi samajhte, jo vaastav mein utni kritrim kriti nahi jitni tum kalpana karte ho; kyunki jiski tum baat karte ho woh sanyog tha; kisi bade uddeshya ka dikhaava nahi tha; na duniya ko dhokha dene ka koi gambheer iraada. Sach yeh hai, ki meri yeh rachnaayein Parmenides ke arguments ko un logon se bachaane ke liye thi jo uska mazaak udaate hain aur un anek haasyaaspad aur viroddhi parinaamon ko dikhaane ki koshish karte hain jo unke anusaar ek ki sweekriti se nikalte hain. Mera answer anek ke samarthakon ko sambodhit hai, jinke hamle ko main byaaj sahit lautaata hoon, unhe yeh palatvaar karke ki unki anek ke being ki hypothesis, agar aage badhaayi jaaye, to ek ke being ki hypothesis se bhi zyaada haasyaaspad lagti hai. Apne guru ke prati utsaah ne mujhe apni jawaani ke dinon mein yeh kitaab likhne ko prerit kiya, par kisi ne prati chura li; aur isliye mere paas koi vikalp nahi tha ki woh prakaashit ho ya nahi; likhne ka uddeshya, phir bhi, kisi bade insaan ki mahatvaakaanksha nahi, balki ek yuvak ki ladaaku pravritti thi. Yeh tum dekhte nahi lagte, Socrates; haalaanki doosre maamlon mein, jaisa main keh raha tha, tumhari dhaarna bahut uchit hai."],["","Main samajhta hoon, Socrates ne kaha, aur tumhare varnan ko poori tarah sweekaar karta hoon. Par mujhe batao, Zeno, kya tum aage yeh nahi sochte ki samaanta ka swayam mein ek idea hai, aur asamaanta ka ek aur idea, jo samaanta ka vipreet hai, aur ki in do mein, tum aur main aur sab doosri cheezein jin par hum anek term laagu karte hain, hissa lete hain—jo cheezein samaanta mein hissa leti hain woh us maatra aur dhang mein samaan ho jaati hain; aur jahan tak woh asamaanta mein hissa leti hain us maatra mein asamaan ho jaati hain, ya samaan aur asamaan dono us maatra mein jismein woh dono mein hissa leti hain? Aur kya sab cheezein dono vipreeton mein hissa le kar, is sahbhaagita ke kaaran, samaan aur asamaan dono nahi ho sakti?—Ismein aashcharya kya hai? Ab agar koi yeh siddh kar sake ki nirpeksh samaan asamaan ho jaata hai, ya nirpeksh asamaan samaan ho jaata hai, to woh, meri raay mein, sach mein aashcharya hoga; par isme kuch asaadhaaran nahi, Zeno, yeh dikhaane mein ki jo cheezein sirf samaanta aur asamaanta mein hissa leti hain woh dono ka anubhav karti hain. Na hi, phir, agar koi yeh dikhaaye ki sab kuch ek mein hissa lekar ek hai, aur saath hi anek mein hissa lekar anek, to kya woh bahut chaunkaane wala hoga. Par agar woh mujhe dikhaaye ki nirpeksh ek anek tha, ya nirpeksh anek ek, to main sach mein chakit hounga. Aur baaki sab ke saath bhi aisa hi: mujhe yeh sun kar aashcharya hoga ki natures ya ideas mein khud yeh vipreet gun the; par tab nahi agar koi mere baare mein siddh karna chahe ki main anek tha aur ek bhi. Jab woh dikhaana chahega ki main anek tha to woh kahega ki mera daayaan aur baayaan hissa hai, aur aage aur peechha, aur upari aur nichla aadha, kyunki main nakaar nahi sakta ki main bahulta mein hissa leta hoon; jab, doosri or, woh siddh karna chahta hai ki main ek hoon, to woh kahega, ki hum jo yahan ikattha hain saat hain, aur ki main ek hoon aur ek mein hissa leta hoon. Dono udaaharanon mein woh apni baat siddh karta hai. Isi tarah phir, agar koi yeh dikhaata hai ki lakdi, patthar, aur aisi cheezein, anek hote hue ek bhi hain, to hum maante hain ki woh ek aur anek ka saha-astitva dikhaata hai, par woh yeh nahi dikhaata ki anek ek hain ya ek anek; woh viroddhaabhaas nahi balki ek saadhaaran sach bol raha hai. Par agar, jaisa maine abhi sujhaaya, koi samaan, asamaan, ek, anek, sthirta, gati, aur aise ideas ki saral dhaarnaaon ko alag kare, aur phir dikhaaye ki inmein swayam mein mishran aur alagaav sambhav hai, to main bahut chakit hounga. Argument ka yeh hissa, Zeno, tumne bahut josh ke saath sambhaala lagta hai; par, jaisa main keh raha tha, main kahin zyaada chakit hounga agar koi un ideas mein khud, jo tark se grahan kiye jaate hain, wahi paheli aur uljhan paaye jo tumne drishya vastuon mein dikhaayi hai."],["","Jab Socrates bol raha tha, Pythodorus ne socha ki Parmenides aur Zeno argument ke lagaataar kadamon se poori tarah prasann nahi the; par phir bhi unhone poora dhyaan diya, aur aksar ek doosre ki or dekha, aur muskuraaye maano uski prashansa mein. Jab woh khatm kar chuka, to Parmenides ne nimnalikhit words mein unki bhaavnaayein vyakt ki:—"]]},{"tag":"130a","title":"Kin cheezon ke Forms hain?","paras":[["","Socrates, usne kaha, main philosophy ki or tumhare mind ke jhukaav ki prashansa karta hoon; ab mujhe batao, kya swayam mein ideas aur un cheezon ke beech jo unmein hissa leti hain yeh bhed tumhara apna tha? aur kya tum sochte ho ki samaanta ka ek idea hai jo us samaanta se alag hai jo hamare paas hai, aur ek aur anek ka, aur un doosri cheezon ka jinka Zeno ne ullekh kiya?"],["","Main sochta hoon ki aise ideas hain, Socrates ne kaha."],["","Parmenides ne aage kaha: Aur kya tum nyaayi aur sundar aur achhe ke, aur us poore varg ke nirpeksh ideas bhi banaaoge?"],["","Haan, usne kaha, banaaunga."],["","Aur kya tum insaan ka ek idea banaaoge jo hamse aur sab doosre maanav praaniyon se alag ho, ya aag aur paani ka?"],["","Main aksar anishchit rehta hoon, Parmenides, ki mujhe unhe shaamil karna chahiye ya nahi."],["","Aur kya tum utne hi anishchit hoge, Socrates, un cheezon ke baare mein jinka ullekh muskaan la sakta hai?—mera matlab hai baal, keechad, gandagi, ya koi aur cheez jo neech aur tuchchh ho; kya tum maanoge ki inmein se har ek ka un vaastavik vastuon se alag idea hai jinke hum sampark mein aate hain, ya nahi?"],["","Certainly nahi, Socrates ne kaha; aisi drishya cheezein waisi hi hain jaisi hamein dikhti hain, aur mujhe dar hai ki unka koi idea maanne mein bekaarpan hoga, haalaanki main kabhi-kabhi pareshaan ho jaata hoon, aur sochne lagta hoon ki idea ke bina kuch bhi nahi; par phir, jab main yeh sthiti apna leta hoon, to bhaag jaata hoon, kyunki mujhe dar hai ki main bakvaas ke athaah gaddhe mein gir kar nasht na ho jaaun; aur isliye main un ideas par laut aata hoon jinki main abhi baat kar raha tha, aur unhi mein vyast rehta hoon."],["","Haan, Socrates, Parmenides ne kaha; yeh isliye hai ki tum abhi yuvak ho; samay aayega, agar main galat nahi, jab philosophy ki tum par adhik mazboot pakad hogi, aur tab tum sabse tuchchh cheezon ko bhi tuchchh nahi samjhoge; tumhari umra mein, tum logon ki raayon ka bahut zyaada lihaaz karne ki or jhukte ho. Par main jaanna chahunga ki kya tumhara matlab hai ki kuch ideas hain jinmein baaki sab cheezein hissa leti hain, aur jinse unhe apne naam milte hain; ki samaan cheezein, udaaharan ke liye, samaan ho jaati hain, kyunki woh samaanta mein hissa leti hain; aur badi cheezein badi ho jaati hain, kyunki woh badappan mein hissa leti hain; aur ki nyaayi aur sundar cheezein nyaayi aur sundar ho jaati hain, kyunki woh nyaay aur saundarya mein hissa leti hain?"],["","Haan, certainly, Socrates ne kaha, mera yahi matlab hai."]]},{"tag":"131a","title":"Sahbhaagita: sampoorn ya hissa? Paal","paras":[["","To har vyakti ya to poore idea mein hissa leta hai ya phir idea ke ek hisse mein? Kya sahbhaagita ka koi aur tarika ho sakta hai?"],["","Nahi ho sakta, usne kaha."],["","To kya tum sochte ho ki poora idea ek hai, aur phir bhi, ek hote hue, anek mein se har ek mein hai?"],["","Kyun nahi, Parmenides? Socrates ne kaha."],["","Kyunki ek hi aur same cheez ek hi samay mein anek alag vyaktiyon mein sampoorn roop se maujood hogi, aur isliye khud se alagaav ki avastha mein hogi."],["","Nahi, par idea din ki tarah ho sakta hai jo ek saath anek jagahon mein ek hi aur same hai, aur phir bhi khud se nirantar hai; is tarah har idea ek hi samay mein sab mein ek hi aur same ho sakta hai."],["","Mujhe tumhara tarika pasand hai, Socrates, ek ko ek saath anek jagahon mein banaane ka. Tumhara kehna hai, ki agar main ek paal faila kar kai logon ko dhak doon, to ek sampoorn hoga jo anek ko shaamil karega—kya yahi tumhara matlab nahi?"],["","Mujhe aisa lagta hai."],["","Aur kya tum kahoge ki poora paal har vyakti ko shaamil karta hai, ya sirf uska ek hissa, aur alag-alag hisse alag-alag logon ko?"],["","Baad wala."],["","To, Socrates, ideas khud vibhaajya honge, aur jo cheezein unmein hissa leti hain unke paas unka sirf ek hissa hoga aur har ek mein poora idea maujood nahi hoga?"],["","Aisa hi nikalta lagta hai."],["","To kya tum kehna chahoge, Socrates, ki ek idea vaastav mein vibhaajya hai aur phir bhi ek bana rehta hai?"],["","Certainly nahi, usne kaha."],["","Maan lo ki tum nirpeksh badappan ko baanto, aur ki anek badi cheezon mein se, har ek nirpeksh badappan se kam badappan ke ek hisse ke kaaran badi hai—kya yeh kalpaneeya hai?"],["","Nahi."],["","Ya kya har baraabar cheez, agar nirpeksh baraabari se kam baraabari ka koi chhota hissa rakhti hai, to sirf us hisse ke kaaran kisi doosri cheez ke baraabar hogi?"],["","Asambhav."],["","Ya maan lo ki hum mein se kisi ke paas chhotepan ka ek hissa hai; yeh chhote ka sirf ek hissa hai, aur isliye nirpeksh chhota bada hai; agar nirpeksh chhota bada ho, to jis cheez mein chhote ka hissa joda jaata hai woh pehle se chhoti hogi aur badi nahi."],["","Kitna bekaar!"],["","To kis tarah, Socrates, sab cheezein ideas mein hissa lengi, agar woh unmein na hisson ke roop mein na sampoornon ke roop mein hissa le sakti hain?"],["","Sach mein, usne kaha, tumne aisa question poochha hai jiska aasaani se jawaab nahi diya ja sakta."],["","Achha, Parmenides ne kaha, aur ek aur question ke baare mein tum kya kehte ho?"],["","Kaun-sa question?"]]},{"tag":"132a","title":"'Teesra Aadmi': badappan ka anant kram","paras":[["","Main kalpana karta hoon ki jis tarah tum har prakaar ka ek idea maanne ki or le jaaye jaate ho woh is prakaar hai:—Tum kai badi vastuein dekhte ho, aur jab tum unhe dekhte ho to tumhe un sab mein ek hi aur same idea (ya nature) dikhta hai; isliye tum badappan ko ek ke roop mein samajhte ho."],["","Bahut true, Socrates ne kaha."],["","Aur agar tum aage badho aur apne mind ko isi tarah badappan ke idea aur un badi cheezon ko jo idea nahi hain ek drishti mein samet lene do, aur unki tulna karo, to kya ek aur badappan paida nahi hoga, jo in sab ka srot dikhega?"],["","Aisa lagta hai."],["","To ab nirpeksh badappan, aur us mein hissa lene wale vyaktiyon ke upar ek aur badappan ka idea dikhaai deta hai; aur phir ek aur, in sab ke upar, jiske kaaran woh sab bade honge, aur is tarah har idea ek hone ke bajaay anant guna ho jaayega."]]},{"tag":"132b","title":"Vichaar ke roop mein Forms","paras":[["","Par kya ideas, Socrates ne poochha, sirf vichaar nahi ho sakte, aur hamare minds ke alawa unka koi uchit astitva na ho, Parmenides? Kyunki us sthiti mein har idea phir bhi ek reh sakta hai, aur is anant guna-vriddhi ka anubhav nahi karega."],["","Aur kya aise vyaktigat vichaar ho sakte hain jo kisi cheez ke vichaar na hon?"],["","Asambhav, usne kaha."],["","Vichaar kisi cheez ka hona chahiye?"],["","Haan."],["","Kisi aisi cheez ka jo hai ya jo nahi hai?"],["","Kisi aisi cheez ka jo hai."],["","Kya woh kisi ek cheez ka nahi hona chahiye, jise vichaar sab se juda hua pehchaanta hai, ek akela roop ya nature hote hue?"],["","Haan."],["","Aur kya woh cheez jo sab mein ek hi aur same ke roop mein grahan ki jaati hai, idea nahi hogi?"],["","Usse bhi, phir, bachne ka koi raasta nahi."],["","To, Parmenides ne kaha, agar tum kehte ho ki baaki sab cheezein ideas mein hissa leti hain, to kya tumhe yeh nahi kehna padega ki ya to har cheez vichaaron se bani hai, aur sab cheezein sochti hain; ya ki woh vichaar hain par unmein koi vichaar nahi?"]]},{"tag":"132d","title":"Namoone ke roop mein Forms: samaanta ka anant kram","paras":[["","Baad wala view, Parmenides, pichhle wale se adhik tarksangat nahi. Meri raay mein, ideas, maano, nature mein sthir namoone (patterns) hain, aur doosri cheezein unke jaisi hain, aur unki pratichhaayaayein hain—doosri cheezon ki ideas mein sahbhaagita ka jo arth hai, woh vaastav mein unke saath saadrishya (assimilation) hai."],["","Par agar, usne kaha, vyakti idea jaisa hai, to kya idea bhi vyakti jaisa nahi hona chahiye, jahan tak vyakti idea ki pratichhaaya hai? Jo samaan hai, uski kalpana samaan ke samaan ke alawa kuch aur nahi ki ja sakti."],["","Asambhav."],["","Aur jab do cheezein samaan hain, to kya unhe same idea mein hissa nahi lena chahiye?"],["","Lena chahiye."],["","Aur jis mein dono hissa leti hain, aur jo unhe samaan banaata hai, kya woh khud idea nahi hoga?"],["","Certainly."],["","To idea vyakti jaisa nahi ho sakta, ya vyakti idea jaisa; kyunki agar woh samaan hain, to samaanta ka koi aur idea hamesha saamne aata rahega, aur agar woh kisi aur cheez jaisa ho, to ek aur; aur naye ideas hamesha paida hote rahenge, agar idea us cheez se mel khaata hai jo us mein hissa leti hai?"],["","Bilkul true."],["","To yeh theory, ki doosri cheezein saadrishya se ideas mein hissa leti hain, chhodni hogi, aur sahbhaagita ka koi aur tarika khojna hoga?"],["","Aisa lagta hai."],["","To kya tum dekhte ho, Socrates, ki ideas ko nirpeksh kehne mein kitni badi kathinaai hai?"],["","Haan, sach mein."],["","Aur, aage, mujhe kehne do ki abhi tak tum us kathinaai ka sirf ek chhota hissa samajhte ho jo shaamil hai agar tum har cheez ka ek akela idea banaao, use doosri cheezon se alag karte hue."],["","Kaun-si kathinaai? usne kaha."]]},{"tag":"133b","title":"Sabse badi kathinaai: Forms agyaat","paras":[["","Kai hain, par sabse badi yeh hai:—Agar koi virodhi argue kare ki yeh ideas, waise hote hue jaisa hum kehte hain ki unhe hona chahiye, agyaat hi rahenge, to koi use galat siddh nahi kar sakta, jab tak ki unke astitva ko nakaarne wala bahut yogyata aur knowledge wala insaan na ho, aur ek lambe aur parishramee pradarshan ka anusaran karne ko taiyaar na ho; woh asantusht rahega, aur phir bhi zid karega ki unhe jaana nahi ja sakta."],["","Tumhara kya matlab hai, Parmenides? Socrates ne kaha."],["","Pehle sthaan par, mujhe lagta hai, Socrates, ki tum, ya koi bhi jo nirpeksh saaron (essences) ka astitva maanta hai, sweekaar karega ki woh hamare andar maujood nahi ho sakte."],["","Nahi, Socrates ne kaha; kyunki tab woh nirpeksh nahi rahenge."],["","True, usne kaha; aur isliye jab ideas jo hain woh ek doosre ke sambandh mein hain, to unka saar unke aapsi sambandh se tay hota hai, aur us ka un pratichhaayaaon se, ya unhe jo bhi kaha jaaye, koi lena-dena nahi jo hamare kshetra mein hain, aur jinse hum jab unmein hissa lete hain to yeh ya woh naam paate hain. Aur jo cheezein hamare kshetra mein hain aur unke same naam rakhti hain, woh bhi sirf ek doosre ke saapeksh hain, aur un ideas ke nahi jinke same naam hain, balki apni hain aur unki nahi."],["","Tumhara kya matlab hai? Socrates ne kaha."],["","Main apna matlab is tarah samjha sakta hoon, Parmenides ne kaha:—Ek maalik ka ek daas hai; ab unke beech ke sambandh mein kuch nirpeksh nahi, jo bas ek insaan ka doosre se sambandh hai. Par abstract mein swaamitva ka ek idea bhi hai, jo abstract mein daasta ke idea ke saapeksh hai. In natures ka hamse koi lena-dena nahi, na hamara unse; woh sirf apne aap se sambandhit hain, aur hum apne aap se. Kya tum mera matlab dekhte ho?"],["","Haan, Socrates ne kaha, main tumhara matlab poori tarah dekhta hoon."],["","Aur kya knowledge—mera matlab nirpeksh knowledge—nirpeksh sach ke anuroop nahi hoga?"],["","Certainly."],["","Aur nirpeksh knowledge ka har prakaar nirpeksh being ke har prakaar ke anuroop hoga?"],["","Haan."],["","Par jo knowledge hamare paas hai, woh us sach ke anuroop hoga jo hamare paas hai; aur phir, hamare knowledge ka har prakaar, hamare being ke har prakaar ka knowledge hoga?"],["","Certainly."],["","Par ideas khud, jaisa tum maante ho, hamare paas nahi, aur nahi ho sakte?"],["","Nahi, nahi ho sakte."],["","Aur nirpeksh natures ya kinds alag-alag knowledge ke nirpeksh idea dwara jaane jaate hain?"],["","Haan."],["","Aur hamare paas knowledge ka idea nahi hai?"],["","Nahi."],["","To koi bhi idea hamein gyaat nahi, kyunki nirpeksh knowledge mein hamara koi hissa nahi?"],["","Mujhe lagta hai nahi."],["","To swayam mein sundar ki, aur swayam mein achhe ki nature, aur baaki sab ideas jinhe hum nirpeksh roop se maujood maante hain, hamein agyaat hain?"],["","Aisa lagta hai."],["","Mujhe lagta hai ki ek aur bhi ajeeb parinaam hai."],["","Woh kya hai?"],["","Kya tum kahoge, ya nahi kahoge, ki nirpeksh knowledge, agar aisi koi cheez hai, hamare knowledge se kahin adhik sateek knowledge hona chahiye; aur saundarya aur baaki ke baare mein bhi yahi?"],["","Haan."],["","Aur agar nirpeksh knowledge mein sahbhaagita jaisi koi cheez ho, to God se adhik kisi ke paas yeh sabse sateek knowledge hone ki sambhaavna nahi?"],["","Certainly."],["","Par phir, kya God, nirpeksh knowledge rakhte hue, maanav cheezon ka knowledge rakhega?"],["","Kyun nahi?"],["","Kyunki, Socrates, Parmenides ne kaha, humne maan liya hai ki ideas maanav cheezon ke sambandh mein maanya nahi; na maanav cheezein unke sambandh mein; dono ke sambandh apne-apne kshetron tak seemit hain."],["","Haan, yeh maana ja chuka hai."],["","Aur agar God ke paas yeh poorn adhikaar, aur poorn knowledge hai, to uska adhikaar hum par shaasan nahi kar sakta, na uska knowledge hamein, ya kisi maanav cheez ko jaan sakta hai; jaise hamara adhikaar gods tak nahi pahunchta, na hamara knowledge kuch divya jaanta hai, waise hi usi tark se woh, gods hote hue, hamare maalik nahi, na hi woh insaanon ki cheezein jaante hain."],["","Phir bhi, nishchit roop se, Socrates ne kaha, God ko knowledge se vanchit karna bhayaanak hai."],["","Yeh, Socrates, Parmenides ne kaha, un kathinaaiyon mein se kuch hain, aur sirf kuch, jinmein hum ulajh jaate hain agar ideas vaastav mein hain aur hum unmein se har ek ko nirpeksh ekta tay karte hain. Jo unke viruddh kahi ja sakne waali baatein sunta hai woh unke astitva ko hi nakaar dega—aur agar woh maujood bhi hon, to woh kahega ki woh avashya insaan ke liye agyaat honge; aur tark uske paksh mein lagega, aur jaisa hum abhi keh rahe the, use manaana bahut kathin hoga; insaan ko kaafi badi yogyata se sampann hona chahiye tab woh seekh sakta hai ki har cheez ka ek varg aur ek nirpeksh saar hai; aur woh aur bhi ullekhneeya hoga jo yeh sab cheezein khud khoje, aur unki poori jaanch karke unhe doosron ko sikhaa sake."],["","Main tumse sahmat hoon, Parmenides, Socrates ne kaha; aur jo tum kehte ho woh mere mann ke bahut anukool hai."],["","Aur phir bhi, Socrates, Parmenides ne kaha, agar koi insaan, in aur aisi kathinaaiyon par dhyaan tikaa kar, cheezon ke ideas ko khatm kar de aur yeh na maane ki har vyaktigat cheez ka apna nishchit idea hai jo hamesha ek hi aur same hai, to uske paas kuch nahi hoga jis par uska mind tik sake; aur is tarah woh tark karne ki shakti ko poori tarah nasht kar dega, jaisa tumne, mujhe lagta hai, vishesh roop se dhyaan diya hai."],["","Bahut true, usne kaha."],["","Par, phir, philosophy ka kya hoga? Hum kahan mudein, agar ideas agyaat hain?"],["","Abhi to mujhe nishchit roop se apna raasta nahi dikhta."]]},{"tag":"135c","title":"Dialectic mein prashikshan ki zaroorat","paras":[["","Haan, Parmenides ne kaha; aur mujhe lagta hai ki yeh, Socrates, isliye hota hai ki tum paryaapt poorv prashikshan ke bina sundar, nyaayi, achhe, aur saamaanya roop se ideas ko paribhaashit karne ka prayaas karte ho. Maine tumhari kami dekhi thi, jab maine tumhe parson yahan apne mitra Aristoteles ke saath baat karte suna. Jo prerna tumhe philosophy ki or le jaati hai woh nishchit roop se shreshth aur divya hai; par ek kala hai jise aam log bekaar ki baatcheet kehte hain, aur jise aksar vyarth samjha jaata hai; usmein tumhe khud ko prashikshit aur abhyast karna chahiye, ab jab tum yuvak ho, varna sach tumhari pakad se phisal jaayega."],["","Aur is abhyaas ki nature kya hai, Parmenides, jiski tum siphaarish karoge?"],["","Woh jo tumne Zeno ko karte suna; saath hi, main tumhe is baat ka shrey deta hoon ki tumne usse kaha ki tum drishya cheezon ke sandarbh mein uljhan ki jaanch karna, ya question ko us tarah dekhna pasand nahi karte; balki sirf vichaar ke vishayon ke sandarbh mein, aur jinhe ideas kaha ja sakta hai."],["","Kyun, haan, usne kaha, mujhe is method se yeh dikhaane mein koi kathinaai nahi lagti ki drishya cheezein samaan aur asamaan hain aur kuch bhi anubhav kar sakti hain."],["","Bilkul true, Parmenides ne kaha; par mujhe lagta hai ki tumhe ek kadam aage jaana chahiye, aur na sirf un parinaamon par vichaar karna chahiye jo kisi di gayi hypothesis se nikalte hain, balki un parinaamon par bhi jo hypothesis ko nakaarne se nikalte hain; aur woh tumhare liye aur bhi behtar prashikshan hoga."],["","Tumhara kya matlab hai? usne kaha."],["","Mera matlab hai, udaaharan ke liye, ki anek ke baare mein Zeno ki isi hypothesis ke maamle mein, tumhe na sirf yeh jaanchna chahiye ki anek ke being ki hypothesis par, anek ke liye apne aur ek ke sambandh mein, aur ek ke liye apne aur anek ke sambandh mein kya parinaam honge, balki yeh bhi ki vipreet hypothesis par, ek aur anek ke liye apne aur ek doosre ke sambandh mein kya parinaam honge. Ya, phir, agar samaanta hai ya nahi hai, to in dono maamlon mein hypothesis ke vishayon ke liye, aur doosri cheezon ke liye, apne aur ek doosre dono ke sambandh mein kya parinaam honge, aur isi tarah asamaanta ke; aur yahi gati aur sthirta, utpatti aur vinaash, aur being aur not-being par bhi laagu hota hai. Ek word mein, jab tum kisi cheez ko hona ya na hona, ya kisi bhi tarah prabhaavit hona maano, to tumhe khud us cheez ke sambandh mein, aur kisi bhi doosri cheez ke sambandh mein jise tum chuno, parinaamon ko dekhna chahiye,—unmein se har ek ko akele, ek se adhik ko, aur sab ko; aur isi tarah doosri cheezon ko, tumhe unhe apne aap ke aur kisi bhi aur cheez ke sambandh mein dekhna chahiye jise tum hona ya na hona maano, agar tum khud ko poori tarah prashikshit karna aur vaastavik sach dekhna chahte ho."],["","Woh, Parmenides, ek vishaal kaam hai jiski tum baat karte ho, aur main tumhe poori tarah nahi samajhta; kya tum koi hypothesis lekar kadamon se guzroge?—tab main tumhe behtar samjhunga."],["","Woh, Socrates, meri umra ke insaan par daalne ke liye ek gambheer kaam hai."],["","To kya tum karoge, Zeno? Socrates ne kaha."],["","Zeno ne muskura kar jawaab diya:—Aao khud Parmenides se apni prarthana karein, jo yeh kehne mein bilkul sahi hai ki tum us kaam ki vishaalta se shaayad hi parichit ho jo tum us par daal rahe ho; aur agar hum aur log hote to main usse na kehta, kyunki yeh aise vishay nahi jinke baare mein koi, khaas kar uski umra mein, badi sabha ke saamne achhi tarah bol sake; zyaadatar log yeh nahi jaante ki sab cheezon se hokar yeh ghumaavdaar yaatra hi woh ekmaatra tarika hai jisse mind sach aur wisdom praapt kar sakta hai. Aur isliye, Parmenides, main Socrates ke anurodh mein shaamil hota hoon, taaki main woh prakriya phir se sun sakun jo maine bahut samay se nahi suni."]]},{"tag":"136e","title":"Parmenides maan jaata hai; Aristoteles jawaab dega","paras":[["","Jab Zeno ne aisa kaha, to Pythodorus ne, Antiphon ke bataaye anusaar, kaha, ki usne khud aur Aristoteles aur poori mandali ne Parmenides se prakriya ka udaaharan dene ki vinti ki. Main mana nahi kar sakta, Parmenides ne kaha; aur phir bhi main kuch Ibycus jaisa mehsoos karta hoon, jisne, jab budhaape mein, apni ichchha ke viruddh, use prem hua, to apni tulna ek boodhe daud ke ghode se ki, jo rath-daud mein daudne wala tha, us maarg ke dar se kaanpta hua jise woh itni achhi tarah jaanta tha—yeh uski apni upma thi. Aur mujhe bhi kampkampi mehsoos hoti hai jab main yaad karta hoon ki apni umra ke is padaav par mujhe words ke kaise saagar se guzarna hai. Par mujhe tumhari baat maanni hogi, kyunki Zeno kehta hai ki maanni chahiye, aur hum akele hain. Main kahan se shuru karun? Aur hamari pehli hypothesis kya ho, agar mujhe yeh parishramee manoranjan karna hai? Kya main apne se shuru karun, aur apni hypothesis ek ko lun? aur un parinaamon par vichaar karun jo ek ke being ya not-being ki maanyata par nikalte hain?"],["","Zaroor, Zeno ne kaha."],["","Aur mujhe jawaab kaun dega? usne kaha. Kya main sabse yuvak ka prastaav karun? Woh kathinaaiyaan nahi khadi karega aur jo sochta hai woh kehne ki sabse adhik sambhaavna hai; aur uske answers mujhe saans lene ka samay denge."],["","Main hi woh hoon jiska tum matlab rakhte ho, Parmenides, Aristoteles ne kaha; kyunki main sabse yuvak hoon aur tumhari seva mein hoon. Poochho, aur main jawaab dunga."]]},{"tag":"137c","title":"Pehli nigaman: agar ek hai, to anek nahi","paras":[["","Parmenides ne aage kaha: 1.a. Agar ek hai, usne kaha, to ek anek nahi ho sakta?"],["","Asambhav."],["","To ek ke hisse nahi ho sakte, aur woh sampoorn nahi ho sakta?"],["","Kyun nahi?"],["","Kyunki har hissa ek sampoorn ka hissa hai; hai na?"],["","Haan."],["","Aur sampoorn kya hai? kya woh jiska koi hissa kam na ho sampoorn nahi hoga?"],["","Certainly."],["","To, dono maamlon mein, ek hisson se bana hoga; sampoorn hone ke roop mein bhi, aur hisse rakhne ke roop mein bhi?"],["","Zaroor."],["","Aur dono maamlon mein, ek anek hoga, aur ek nahi?"],["","True."],["","Par, nishchit roop se, use ek hona chahiye aur anek nahi?"],["","Hona chahiye."],["","To, agar ek ko ek bane rehna hai, to woh sampoorn nahi hoga, aur uske hisse nahi honge?"],["","Nahi."],["","Par agar uske hisse nahi, to uska na aarambh hoga, na madhya, na ant; kyunki yeh nissandeh uske hisse honge."],["","Sahi."],["","Par phir, aarambh aur ant har cheez ki seemaayein hain?"],["","Certainly."],["","To ek, jiska na aarambh hai na ant, aseemit hai?"],["","Haan, aseemit."],["","Aur isliye niraakaar; kyunki woh na gol mein hissa le sakta hai na seedhe mein."],["","Par kyun?"],["","Kyun, kyunki gol woh hai jiske sab antim bindu kendra se samaan doori par hain?"],["","Haan."],["","Aur seedha woh hai jiska kendra siron ke drishya ko rokta hai?"],["","True."],["","To ek ke hisse honge aur woh anek hoga, agar woh seedhe ya gol roop mein hissa le?"],["","Nishchit roop se."],["","Par hisse na hone se, woh na seedha hoga na gol?"],["","Sahi."],["","Aur, aisi nature ka hone se, woh kisi sthaan mein nahi ho sakta, kyunki woh na kisi doosre mein ho sakta hai na khud mein."],["","Kaise?"],["","Kyunki agar woh kisi doosre mein hota, to jismein woh tha usse ghira hota, aur use kai jagahon par aur kai hisson se chhoota; par jo ek aur avibhaajya hai, aur gol nature mein hissa nahi leta, use chaaron or kai jagahon par chhua nahi ja sakta."],["","Certainly nahi."],["","Par agar, doosri or, ek khud mein hota, to woh bhi khud ke alawa kisi aur se samaaya nahi hota; arthaat, agar woh vaastav mein khud mein hota; kyunki koi cheez kisi aisi cheez mein nahi ho sakti jo use samaaye na."],["","Asambhav."],["","Par phir, jo samaata hai use us se alag hona chahiye jo samaaya hua hai? kyunki same sampoorn ek saath kartaa aur bhoktaa dono nahi ho sakta; aur agar aisa hai, to ek ek nahi rahega, balki do?"],["","True."],["","To ek kahin nahi ho sakta, na khud mein na kisi doosre mein?"],["","Nahi."]]},{"tag":"138b","title":"Na gati mein na sthir","paras":[["","Aage vichaar karo, ki kya aisi nature wali cheez mein sthirta ya gati ho sakti hai."],["","Kyun nahi?"],["","Kyun, kyunki ek, agar gati karta, to ya to sthaan mein gati karta ya nature mein badalta; kyunki gati ke bas yahi prakaar hain."],["","Haan."],["","Aur ek, jab badalta hai aur khud nahi rehta, to ek nahi reh sakta."],["","Nahi reh sakta."],["","To woh us prakaar ki gati ka anubhav nahi kar sakta jo nature ka badlaav hai?"],["","Spasht roop se nahi."],["","To kya ek ki gati sthaan mein ho sakti hai?"],["","Shaayad."],["","Par agar ek sthaan mein gati kare, to kya use ya to same jagah mein gol-gol ghoomna hoga, ya ek jagah se doosri jagah?"],["","Hona hoga."],["","Aur jo vritt mein ghoomta hai use ek kendra par tikna hoga; aur jo kendra par ghoomta hai uske aise hisse hone chahiye jo kendra se alag hon; par jiska na kendra hai na hisse use kendra par ghumaaya nahi ja sakta?"],["","Asambhav."],["","Par shaayad ek ki gati sthaan-parivartan mein hai?"],["","Shaayad aisa, agar woh gati karta hi hai."],["","Aur kya hum pehle hi nahi dikha chuke ki woh kisi cheez mein nahi ho sakta?"],["","Haan."],["","To uska kisi cheez mein astitva mein aana aur bhi asambhav hai; hai na?"],["","Main nahi dekhta kyun."],["","Kyun, kyunki jo kuch kisi cheez mein astitva mein aata hai, woh astitva mein aate hue abhi us doosri cheez mein nahi ho sakta, na poori tarah usse baahar, agar pehle se usmein astitva mein aa raha hai."],["","Certainly nahi."],["","Aur isliye jo kuch doosre mein astitva mein aata hai uske hisse hone chahiye, aur tab ek hissa us doosre ke andar ho sakta hai, aur doosra baahar; par jiske hisse nahi woh kabhi ek hi samay mein kisi cheez ke na poori tarah andar ho sakta hai na poori tarah baahar."],["","True."],["","Aur kya us cheez mein jiske hisse nahi, aur jo sampoorn nahi, kahin bhi astitva mein aane ki aur bhi badi asambhavta nahi, kyunki woh na hisse ke roop mein na sampoorn ke roop mein astitva mein aa sakti hai?"],["","Spasht roop se."],["","To woh na same jagah par ghoom kar sthaan badalta hai, na kahin jaakar aur kisi cheez mein astitva mein aakar; na phir, khud mein badlaav se?"],["","Bahut true."],["","To kisi bhi prakaar ki gati ke sandarbh mein ek achal hai?"],["","Achal."],["","Par na hi ek kisi cheez mein ho sakta hai, jaisa hum kehte hain?"],["","Haan, humne aisa kaha tha."],["","To woh kabhi same mein nahi?"],["","Kyun nahi?"],["","Kyunki agar woh same mein hota to woh kisi cheez mein hota."],["","Certainly."],["","Aur humne kaha tha ki woh na khud mein ho sakta hai, na doosre mein?"],["","True."],["","To ek kabhi same jagah mein nahi?"],["","Aisa lagta hai ki nahi."],["","Par jo kabhi same jagah mein nahi woh kabhi shaant ya sthir nahi?"],["","Kabhi nahi."],["","To ek, jaisa lagta hai, na sthir hai na gati mein?"],["","Nishchit roop se aisa dikhta hai."]]},{"tag":"139b","title":"Na same na anya, na samaan na asamaan","paras":[["","Na hi woh khud ke ya doosre ke same hoga; na phir, khud se ya doosre se anya (other)."],["","Woh kaise?"],["","Agar khud se anya ho to woh ek se anya hoga, aur ek nahi hoga."],["","True."],["","Aur agar doosre ke same ho, to woh woh doosra hoga, aur khud nahi; to is maanyata par bhi, uski nature ek ki nahi hogi, balki woh ek se anya hoga?"],["","Hoga."],["","To woh na doosre ke same hoga, na khud se anya?"],["","Nahi hoga."],["","Na hi woh doosre se anya hoga, jab tak woh ek bana rehta hai; kyunki ek nahi, balki sirf anya hi, anya se anya ho sakta hai, aur kuch nahi."],["","True."],["","To ek hone ke kaaran woh anya nahi hoga?"],["","Certainly nahi."],["","Par agar ek hone ke kaaran nahi, to khud ke kaaran nahi; aur agar khud ke kaaran nahi, to khud nahi, aur khud bilkul anya na hote hue, kisi cheez se anya nahi hoga?"],["","Sahi."],["","Na hi ek khud ke same hoga."],["","Kaise nahi?"],["","Nishchit roop se ek ki nature same ki nature nahi."],["","Kyun nahi?"],["","Aisa nahi ki jab koi cheez kisi cheez ke same ho jaati hai to woh ek ho jaati hai."],["","To kya?"],["","Jo kuch anek ke same ho jaata hai, woh avashya anek ho jaata hai aur ek nahi."],["","True."],["","Par, agar ek aur same mein koi antar na hota, to jab koi cheez same hoti, woh hamesha ek ho jaati; aur jab ek hoti, to same?"],["","Certainly."],["","Aur, isliye, agar ek khud ke same ho, to woh khud ke saath ek nahi, aur isliye ek bhi hoga aur ek nahi bhi."],["","Nishchit roop se yeh asambhav hai."],["","Aur isliye ek na anya se anya ho sakta hai, na khud ke same."],["","Asambhav."],["","Aur is tarah ek na same ho sakta hai, na anya, na khud ke sambandh mein na doosre ke?"],["","Nahi."],["","Na hi ek kisi cheez ke samaan hoga ya khud ya doosre se asamaan."],["","Kyun nahi?"],["","Kyunki samaanta gunon (affections) ki ekroopta hai."],["","Haan."],["","Aur ekroopta (sameness) ekta se alag nature ki dikhaayi ja chuki hai?"],["","Woh dikhaaya ja chuka hai."],["","Par agar ek mein ek hone ke alawa koi aur gun hota, to woh is tarah prabhaavit hota ki ek se adhik ho jaata; jo asambhav hai."],["","True."],["","To ek kabhi is tarah prabhaavit nahi ho sakta ki doosre ke ya khud ke same ho?"],["","Spasht roop se nahi."],["","To woh doosre ke samaan, ya khud ke samaan nahi ho sakta?"],["","Nahi."],["","Na hi woh is tarah prabhaavit ho sakta hai ki anya ho, kyunki tab woh is tarah prabhaavit hoga ki ek se adhik ho."],["","Hoga."],["","Jo khud se ya doosre se alag dhang se prabhaavit hota hai, woh khud se ya doosre se asamaan hoga, kyunki gunon ki ekroopta samaanta hai."],["","True."],["","Par ek, jaisa dikhta hai, kabhi alag dhang se prabhaavit na hone se, kabhi khud se ya doosre se asamaan nahi?"],["","Kabhi nahi."],["","To ek kabhi na khud ke ya doosre ke samaan hoga na asamaan?"],["","Spasht roop se nahi."]]},{"tag":"140b","title":"Na baraabar na asamaan, na bada na chhota","paras":[["","Phir, is nature ka hone se, woh na khud ke na doosre ke baraabar ho sakta hai na asamaan (unequal)."],["","Woh kaise?"],["","Kyun, kyunki ek agar baraabar ho to use un hi maapon ka hona chahiye jinka woh hai jiske woh baraabar hai."],["","True."],["","Aur agar un cheezon se bada ya chhota ho jo uske saath saamaapya (commensurable) hain, to ek ke paas chhoti cheez se adhik maap honge, aur badi se kam?"],["","Haan."],["","Aur isi tarah un cheezon ke saath jo uske saath saamaapya nahi, ek ke paas chhoti cheez se bade maap honge aur badi se chhote."],["","Certainly."],["","Par jo ekroopta mein hissa nahi leta, uske same maap ya koi aur cheez same kaise ho sakti hai?"],["","Asambhav."],["","Aur same maap na hone se, ek na khud ke baraabar ho sakta hai na doosre ke?"],["","Aisa dikhta hai."],["","Par phir, chaahe uske kam maap hon ya adhik, uske utne hisse honge jitne maap; aur is tarah phir ek ek nahi rahega balki uske utne hisse honge jitne maap."],["","Sahi."],["","Aur agar woh ek maap ka hota, to us maap ke baraabar hota; phir bhi woh baraabari mein asamarth dikhaaya ja chuka hai."],["","Dikhaaya ja chuka hai."],["","To woh na ek maap mein hissa lega, na anek mein, na kam mein, na bilkul same mein, na khud ya doosre ke baraabar hoga; na khud ya doosre se bada ya chhota?"],["","Certainly."],["","Achha, aur kya hum maante hain ki ek kisi cheez se bada ya chhota (umra mein), ya uske same umra ka ho sakta hai?"],["","Kyun nahi?"],["","Kyun, kyunki jo khud ya doosre ke same umra ka hai, use samay ki baraabari ya samaanta mein hissa lena chahiye; aur humne kaha tha ki ek na baraabari mein hissa leta hai na samaanta mein?"],["","Humne aisa kaha tha."],["","Aur humne yeh bhi kaha tha, ki woh asamaanta ya bhinnata mein hissa nahi leta."],["","Bahut true."],["","To ek, is nature ka hote hue, kisi cheez se bada ya chhota kaise ho sakta hai, ya uske same umra ka?"],["","Kisi tarah nahi."],["","To ek na bada ho sakta hai na chhota, na same umra ka, na khud ke saath na doosre ke?"],["","Spasht roop se nahi."]]},{"tag":"141a","title":"Samay mein nahi, aur bilkul nahi","paras":[["","To ek, is nature ka hote hue, samay mein bilkul nahi ho sakta; kyunki kya jo samay mein hai use hamesha khud se bada (older) hote nahi jaana chahiye?"],["","Certainly."],["","Aur jo bada hai, use hamesha kisi chhoti cheez se bada hona chahiye?"],["","True."],["","To, jo khud se bada hota hai, woh saath hi khud se chhota bhi hota hai, agar uske paas kuch hona hai jisse woh bada ho."],["","Tumhara kya matlab hai?"],["","Mera matlab yeh hai:—Kisi cheez ko kisi aisi doosri cheez se alag hone ki zaroorat nahi jo pehle se alag hai; woh alag HAI, aur agar uska alag ho chuka hai, to woh alag ho chuki hai; agar uska alag hoga, to woh alag hogi; par jo alag ho rahi hai, uska koi alag na ho chuka ho sakta hai, na hone wala, na abhi ho—ekmaatra sambhav alag woh hai jo ho raha hai."],["","Yeh anivaarya hai."],["","Par, nishchit roop se, bada (older) chhote ke saapeksh ek antar hai, aur kisi aur ke nahi."],["","True."],["","To jo khud se bada hota hai use, saath hi, khud se chhota bhi hona chahiye?"],["","Haan."],["","Par phir, yeh true hai ki woh khud se adhik ya kam samay ke liye nahi ho sakta, balki use khud ke same samay ke liye hona, aur hona, aur ho chuka hona, aur hone wala hona chahiye?"],["","Woh bhi anivaarya hai."],["","To jo cheezein samay mein hain, aur samay mein hissa leti hain, unhe har maamle mein, mujhe lagta hai, khud ke same umra ka hona chahiye; aur ek saath khud se badi aur chhoti bhi hona chahiye?"],["","Haan."],["","Par ek un gunon mein hissa nahi leta tha?"],["","Bilkul nahi."],["","To woh samay mein hissa nahi leta, aur kisi samay mein nahi hai?"],["","Argument yahi dikhaata hai."],["","Achha, par kya 'tha,' aur 'ho chuka hai,' aur 'ho raha tha,' abhivyaktiyaan beete samay mein sahbhaagita nahi darshaati?"],["","Certainly."],["","Aur kya 'hoga,' 'ho jaayega,' 'ho chuka hoga,' bhavishya samay mein sahbhaagita nahi darshaate?"],["","Haan."],["","Aur 'hai,' ya 'hota hai,' vartamaan samay mein sahbhaagita darshaata hai?"],["","Certainly."],["","Aur agar ek samay mein sahbhaagita se nirpeksh roop se rahit hai, to woh kabhi na hua tha, na ho raha tha, na kabhi kisi samay tha, na ab ho chuka hai na ho raha hai, na hai, na hoga, na ho chuka hoga, na aage hoga."],["","Bilkul true."],["","Par kya being mein hissa lene ke inke alawa koi aur tarike hain?"],["","Koi nahi hain."],["","To ek kisi tarah being mein hissa nahi le sakta?"],["","Yahi nishkarsh hai."],["","To ek bilkul nahi hai?"],["","Spasht roop se nahi."],["","To ek is tarah maujood nahi ki ek ho; kyunki agar woh hota aur being mein hissa leta, to woh pehle se hota; par agar argument par vishwaas kiya jaaye, to ek na hai na ek hai?"],["","True."],["","Par jo nahi hai usmein koi gun ya sambandh sambhav nahi?"],["","Of course nahi."],["","To uska na koi naam hai, na abhivyakti, na perception, na raay, na knowledge?"],["","Spasht roop se nahi."],["","To woh na naamit hai, na vyakt, na raay ka vishay, na gyaat, na koi cheez jo hai use perceive karti hai."],["","Hamein yahi nishkarsh nikaalna hoga."],["","Par kya yeh sab ek ke baare mein true ho sakta hai?"],["","Mujhe lagta hai nahi."]]},{"tag":"142b","title":"Doosra nigaman: woh ek jo hai","paras":[["","1.b. Maan lo, ab, ki hum ek baar phir mool hypothesis par lautein; aao dekhein ki kya, aage ki sameeksha par, question ka koi naya pehlu dikhta hai."],["","Mujhe aisa karke bahut khushi hogi."],["","Hum kehte hain ki hamein milkar woh sab parinaam nikaalne hain, jo bhi woh hon, jo nikalte hain, agar ek hai?"],["","Haan."],["","To hum shuruaat se shuru karenge:—Agar ek hai, to kya ek ho sakta hai, aur being mein hissa na le?"],["","Asambhav."],["","To ek ka being hoga, par uska being ek ke same nahi hoga; kyunki agar same hota, to woh ek ka being nahi hota; na hi ek ne being mein hissa liya hota, kyunki yeh proposition ki ek hai is proposition ke same hota ki ek ek hai; par hamari hypothesis yeh nahi ki agar ek ek hai to kya nikalega, balki agar ek hai:—kya main sahi nahi?"],["","Bilkul sahi."],["","Hamara kehna hai, ki being ka arth ek ke same nahi?"],["","Of course."],["","Aur jab hum unhe sankshep mein jodte hain, aur kehte hain 'Ek hai,' to yeh kehne ke baraabar hai, 'being mein hissa leta hai'?"],["","Bilkul true."],["","To ek baar phir poochhein, agar ek hai to kya nikalega. Kya yeh hypothesis avashya yeh imply nahi karti ki ek aisi nature ka hai ki uske hisse hain?"],["","Kaise?"],["","Is tarah:—Agar being ek par laagu hota hai, agar ek hai, aur ek being par, agar being ek hai; aur agar being aur ek same nahi; aur kyunki ek, jise humne maana hai, hai, to kya sampoorn, agar woh ek hai, khud nahi hoga, aur uske hisse, ek aur being, nahi honge?"],["","Certainly."],["","Aur kya in hisson mein se har ek—ek aur being—ko bas hissa kaha jaaye, ya 'hissa' word 'sampoorn' word ke saapeksh hona chahiye?"],["","Baad wala."],["","To jo ek hai woh sampoorn bhi hai aur uska hissa bhi hai?"],["","Certainly."],["","Phir, ek ke hisson mein, agar woh hai—mera matlab being aur ek—kya koi doosre ko imply karne mein asafal hai? kya ek being se, ya being ek se khaali hai?"],["","Asambhav."],["","Is tarah, har hisse mein bhi baari-baari se ek aur being dono hain, aur woh kam se kam do hisson se bana hai; aur yahi siddhaant hamesha chalta rehta hai, aur har hisse mein hamesha yeh do hisse hote hain; kyunki being mein hamesha ek shaamil hai, aur ek mein being; to ek hamesha gaayab hota aur do banta rehta hai."],["","Certainly."],["","Aur is tarah ek, agar hai, to bahulta mein anant hona chahiye?"],["","Spasht roop se."]]},{"tag":"143a","title":"Ek se sankhya utpann hoti hai","paras":[["","Aao ek aur disha lein."],["","Kaun-si disha?"],["","Hum kehte hain ki ek being mein hissa leta hai aur isliye woh hai?"],["","Haan."],["","Aur is tarah, ek, agar uska being hai, anek nikla hai?"],["","True."],["","Par ab, aao us ek ko alag karein jo, jaisa hum kehte hain, being mein hissa leta hai, aur use us se alag kalpana karne ki koshish karein jismein, jaisa hum kehte hain, woh hissa leta hai—kya yeh abstract ek sirf ek hoga ya anek?"],["","Ek, mujhe lagta hai."],["","Aao dekhein:—Kya ek ka being ek se anya nahi hona chahiye? kyunki ek being nahi, balki, ek ke roop mein dekha jaaye, to sirf being mein hissa leta tha?"],["","Certainly."],["","Agar being aur ek do alag cheezein hain, to aisa nahi ki ek ek hone ke kaaran being se anya hai; na being being hone ke kaaran ek se anya hai; balki woh anyata aur bhinnata ke kaaran ek doosre se alag hain."],["","Certainly."],["","To anya same nahi hai—na ek ke saath na being ke saath?"],["","Certainly nahi."],["","Aur isliye chaahe hum being aur anya ko lein, ya being aur ek ko, ya ek aur anya ko, har aise maamle mein hum do cheezein lete hain, jinhe sahi roop se dono kaha ja sakta hai."],["","Kaise."],["","Is tarah—tum being ki baat kar sakte ho?"],["","Haan."],["","Aur ek ki bhi?"],["","Haan."],["","To ab humne dono mein se har ek ki baat ki hai?"],["","Haan."],["","Achha, aur jab main being aur ek ki baat karta hoon, to main un dono ki baat karta hoon?"],["","Certainly."],["","Aur agar main being aur anya ki, ya ek aur anya ki baat karun,—kya aise kisi bhi maamle mein main dono ki baat nahi karta?"],["","Haan."],["","Aur jise sahi roop se dono kaha jaata hai, kya use do bhi nahi hona chahiye?"],["","Nissandeh."],["","Aur do cheezon mein se koi bhi kisi bhi sambhaavna se ek kaise nahi ho sakti?"],["","Nahi ho sakti."],["","To, agar jode ke sadasya milkar do hain, to unhe alag-alag ek hona chahiye?"],["","Spasht roop se."],["","Aur agar unmein se har ek ek hai, to kisi bhi jode mein kisi ek ko jodne se, sampoorn teen ho jaata hai?"],["","Haan."],["","Aur teen vishamm hai, aur do samm?"],["","Of course."],["","Aur agar do hain to dugna bhi hona chahiye, aur agar teen hain to tigna hona chahiye; arthaat, agar do guna ek do banaata hai, aur teen guna ek teen?"],["","Certainly."],["","Do hain, aur dugna, aur isliye do guna do hona chahiye; aur teen hain, aur tigna hai, aur isliye teen guna teen hona chahiye?"],["","Of course."],["","Agar teen aur dugna hain, to do guna teen hai; aur agar do aur tigna hain, to teen guna do hai?"],["","Nissandeh."],["","Yahan, to, humne samm ko samm baar, aur vishamm ko vishamm baar, aur samm ko vishamm baar, aur vishamm ko samm baar liya hai."],["","True."],["","Aur agar aisa hai, to kya koi sankhya bachti hai jiska hona aavashyak nahi?"],["","Bilkul koi nahi."],["","To agar ek hai, to sankhya bhi honi chahiye?"],["","Honi chahiye."],["","Par agar sankhya hai, to anek bhi hona chahiye, aur being ki anant bahulta; kyunki sankhya bahulta mein anant hai, aur being mein bhi hissa leti hai: kya main sahi nahi?"],["","Certainly."],["","Aur agar saari sankhya being mein hissa leti hai, to sankhya ka har hissa bhi hissa lega?"],["","Haan."],["","To being cheezon ki poori bheed par baanta gaya hai, aur jo kuch hai, chaahe kitna chhota ya kitna bada, usse rahit nahi? Aur, vaastav mein, iski maanyata hi bekaar hai, kyunki jo hai woh being se rahit kaise ho sakta hai?"],["","Kisi tarah nahi."],["","Aur woh sabse bade aur sabse chhote mein, aur har aakaar ke being mein baanta gaya hai, aur sab cheezon se adhik toota hai; uske vibhaajanon ki koi seema nahi."],["","True."],["","To uske sabse adhik sankhya mein hisse hain?"],["","Haan, sabse adhik sankhya."],["","Kya inmein se koi hai jo being ka hissa hai, aur phir bhi koi hissa nahi?"],["","Asambhav."],["","Par agar woh hai hi aur jab tak hai, to use ek hona chahiye, aur koi nahi nahi ho sakta?"],["","Certainly."],["","To ek being ke har ek hisse se juda hai, aur kisi hisse mein kam nahi padta, chaahe bada ho ya chhota, ya uska aakaar jo bhi ho?"],["","True."],["","Par socho:—Kya ek, apni sampoornata mein, ek hi samay mein anek jagahon mein ho sakta hai?"],["","Nahi; main uski asambhavta dekhta hoon."],["","Aur agar apni sampoornata mein nahi, to woh baanta gaya hai; kyunki woh being ke sab hisson ke saath upasthit nahi ho sakta, jab tak baanta na jaaye."],["","True."],["","Aur jiske hisse hain woh utne honge jitne hisse hain?"],["","Certainly."],["","To hum abhi yeh kehne mein galat the, ki being sabse adhik sankhya mein hisson mein baanta gaya tha. Kyunki woh ek se adhik hisson mein nahi baanta gaya, ek ke baraabar hisson mein; ek kabhi being se khaali nahi, na being ek se, balki do hote hue woh sam-maan aur sam-vistaar hain."],["","Nishchit roop se yeh true hai."],["","Ek khud, to, being dwara hisson mein toda jaakar, anek aur anant hai?"],["","True."],["","To na sirf woh ek jiska being hai anek hai, balki being dwara baanta gaya ek khud bhi anek hona chahiye?"],["","Certainly."],["","Aage, kyunki hisse ek sampoorn ke hisse hain, ek, sampoorn ke roop mein, seemit hoga; kyunki kya hisse sampoorn se samaaye nahi hote?"],["","Certainly."],["","Aur jo samaata hai, woh seema hai?"],["","Of course."],["","To ek agar uska being hai to ek aur anek, sampoorn aur hisse, seemaayein rakhte hue aur phir bhi sankhya mein aseemit hai?"],["","Spasht roop se."],["","Aur seemaayein hone ke kaaran, sire (extremes) bhi rakhte hue?"],["","Certainly."],["","Aur agar sampoorn hai, to aarambh aur madhya aur ant rakhte hue. Kyunki kya koi cheez in teen ke bina sampoorn ho sakti hai? Aur agar inmein se koi kisi cheez mein kam ho, to kya woh phir sampoorn hogi?"],["","Nahi."],["","To ek, jaisa dikhta hai, aarambh, madhya, aur ant rakhega."],["","Rakhega."],["","Par, phir, madhya siron se samaan doori par hoga; varna woh madhya mein nahi hoga?"],["","Haan."],["","To ek aakriti mein hissa lega, ya to seedhi rekha wali ya gol, ya dono ka mel?"],["","True."],["","Aur agar aisa hai, to woh khud mein bhi hoga aur doosre mein bhi."],["","Kaise?"],["","Har hissa sampoorn mein hai, aur koi sampoorn ke baahar nahi."],["","True."],["","Aur sab hisse sampoorn se samaaye hain?"],["","Haan."],["","Aur ek apne sab hisse hai, aur sab se na adhik na kam?"],["","Nahi."],["","Aur ek sampoorn hai?"],["","Of course."],["","Par agar sab hisse sampoorn mein hain, aur ek un sab aur sampoorn hai, aur woh sab sampoorn se samaaye hain, to ek ek se samaaya hoga; aur is tarah ek khud mein hoga."],["","Yeh true hai."],["","Par phir, sampoorn hisson mein nahi—na sab hisson mein, na unmein se kisi ek mein. Kyunki agar woh sab mein hai, to use ek mein hona chahiye; kyunki agar koi ek hota jismein woh nahi tha, to woh sab hisson mein nahi ho sakta; kyunki jis hisse mein woh nahi woh sab mein se ek hai, aur agar sampoorn ismein nahi, to woh un sab mein kaise ho sakta hai?"],["","Nahi ho sakta."],["","Na hi sampoorn kuch hisson mein ho sakta hai; kyunki agar sampoorn kuch hisson mein hota, to bada chhote mein hota, jo asambhav hai."],["","Haan, asambhav."],["","Par agar sampoorn na ek mein, na ek se adhik mein, na sab hisson mein hai, to use kisi aur cheez mein hona chahiye, ya kahin bhi hona band kar dena chahiye?"],["","Certainly."],["","Agar woh kahin nahi hota, to woh kuch nahi hota; par sampoorn hote hue, aur khud mein na hote hue, use doosre mein hona chahiye."],["","Bahut true."],["","Ek, to, sampoorn ke roop mein dekha jaaye, to doosre mein hai, par apne sab hisse hone ke roop mein dekha jaaye, to khud mein hai; aur isliye ek ko khud khud mein aur doosre mein bhi hona chahiye."],["","Certainly."],["","Ek, to, is nature ka hote hue, avashya sthir aur gati mein dono hai?"],["","Kaise?"],["","Ek sthir hai kyunki woh khud mein hai, kyunki ek mein hote hue, aur isse baahar na jaate hue, woh same mein hai, jo woh khud hai."],["","True."],["","Aur jo hamesha same mein hai, use hamesha sthir hona chahiye?"],["","Certainly."],["","Achha, aur kya, iske vipreet, jo hamesha doosre mein hai, use kabhi same mein nahi hona chahiye; aur agar kabhi same mein nahi, to kabhi sthir nahi, aur agar sthir nahi, to gati mein?"],["","True."],["","To ek hamesha khud khud mein aur doosre mein hote hue, hamesha sthir aur gati mein dono hona chahiye?"],["","Spasht roop se."],["","Aur use khud ke same, aur khud se anya hona chahiye; aur doosron ke same bhi, aur doosron se anya bhi; yeh uske pichhle gunon se nikalta hai."],["","Kaise?"],["","Har cheez har doosri cheez ke sambandh mein, ya to same hai ya anya; ya agar na same na anya, to hisse ka sampoorn se, ya sampoorn ka hisse se sambandh mein."],["","Spasht roop se."],["","Aur kya ek khud ka hissa hai?"],["","Certainly nahi."],["","Kyunki woh khud ke sambandh mein hissa nahi, woh khud se sampoorn aur hisse ki tarah sambandhit nahi ho sakta?"],["","Nahi ho sakta."],["","Par kya ek ek se anya hai?"],["","Nahi."],["","Aur isliye khud se anya nahi?"],["","Certainly nahi."],["","To agar woh khud ke sambandh mein na anya hai, na sampoorn, na hissa, to kya use khud ke same nahi hona chahiye?"],["","Certainly."],["","Par phir, ek cheez jo 'khud' se doosri jagah mein hai, agar yeh 'khud' khud ke saath same jagah mein rehta hai, to use 'khud' se anya hona chahiye, kyunki woh doosri jagah mein hogi?"],["","True."],["","To ek ek saath khud mein aur doosre mein dikhaaya ja chuka hai?"],["","Haan."],["","Is tarah, to, jaisa dikhta hai, ek khud se anya hoga?"],["","True."],["","Achha, to, agar koi cheez kisi cheez se anya ho, to kya woh us se anya nahi hogi jo anya hai?"],["","Certainly."],["","Aur kya sab cheezein jo ek nahi hain, ek se anya nahi hongi, aur ek na-ek se anya?"],["","Of course."],["","To ek doosron se anya hoga?"],["","True."],["","Par, vichaar karo:—Kya nirpeksh same, aur nirpeksh anya, ek doosre ke vipreet nahi?"],["","Of course."],["","To kya same kabhi anya mein hoga, ya anya same mein?"],["","Nahi honge."],["","To agar anya kabhi same mein nahi, to aisa kuch nahi jismein anya kisi bhi samay-avadhi ke dauraan ho; kyunki us samay-avadhi ke dauraan, chaahe kitni chhoti, anya same mein hoga. Kya yeh true nahi?"],["","Haan."],["","Aur kyunki anya kabhi same mein nahi, woh kabhi kisi aisi cheez mein nahi ho sakta jo hai."],["","True."],["","To anya kabhi na na-ek mein hoga, na ek mein?"],["","Certainly nahi."],["","To anyata ke kaaran ek na-ek se anya nahi, na na-ek ek se anya."],["","Nahi."],["","Na hi apne kaaran woh ek doosre se anya honge, agar anya mein hissa nahi lete."],["","Kaise ho sakte hain?"],["","Par agar woh anya nahi hain, na apne kaaran na anya ke kaaran, to kya woh ek doosre se anya hone se poori tarah bach nahi jaayenge?"],["","Bach jaayenge."],["","Phir, na-ek ek mein hissa nahi le sakta; varna woh na-ek nahi hota, balki kisi tarah ek hota."],["","True."],["","Na hi na-ek sankhya ho sakta hai; kyunki sankhya rakhte hue, woh bilkul na-ek nahi hota."],["","Nahi hota."],["","Phir, kya na-ek ek ka hissa hai; ya balki, kya us sthiti mein woh ek mein hissa nahi lega?"],["","Lega."],["","To agar, har drishti se, ek aur na-ek alag hain, to na ek na-ek ka hissa ya sampoorn hai, na na-ek ek ka hissa ya sampoorn?"],["","Nahi."],["","Par humne kaha tha ki jo cheezein na ek doosre ke hisse hain na sampoorn, na ek doosre se anya, woh ek doosre ke same hongi:—humne aisa kaha tha?"],["","Haan."],["","To kya hum kahein ki ek, na-ek ke saath is sambandh mein hote hue, uske same hai?"],["","Aao aisa kahein."],["","To woh khud ke aur doosron ke same hai, aur khud se aur doosron se anya bhi."],["","Yahi nishkarsh dikhta hai."],["","Aur woh khud ke aur doosron ke samaan aur asamaan bhi hoga?"],["","Shaayad."],["","Kyunki ek doosron se anya dikhaaya gaya tha, to doosre bhi ek se anya honge."],["","Haan."],["","Aur ek doosron se usi maatra mein anya hai jitna doosre usse anya hain, aur na adhik na kam?"],["","True."],["","Aur agar na adhik na kam, to samaan maatra mein?"],["","Haan."],["","Us gun ke kaaran jisse ek doosron se anya hai aur doosre isi tarah usse anya, ek doosron jaisa prabhaavit hoga aur doosre ek jaise."],["","Tumhara kya matlab hai?"],["","Main naamon ka maamla udaaharan ke roop mein le sakta hoon: Tum kisi cheez ko naam dete ho?"],["","Haan."],["","Aur tum naam ek baar ya adhik baar keh sakte ho?"],["","Haan."],["","Aur jab tum use ek baar kehte ho, to tum uska ullekh karte ho jiska woh naam hai? aur jab ek se adhik baar, to kya tum kisi aur cheez ka ullekh karte ho? ya kya woh hamesha same cheez honi chahiye jiski tum baat karte ho, chaahe tum naam ek baar bolo ya ek se adhik baar?"],["","Of course woh same hai."],["","Aur kya 'anya' kisi cheez ko diya gaya naam nahi?"],["","Certainly."],["","Jab bhi, to, tum 'anya' word ka prayog karte ho, chaahe ek baar ya adhik baar, tum use naam dete ho jiska woh naam hai, aur kisi aur ko naam nahi dete?"],["","True."],["","To jab hum kehte hain ki doosre ek se anya hain, aur ek doosron se anya, to 'anya' word dohraate hue hum us nature ki baat karte hain jis par naam laagu hota hai, aur kisi aur ki nahi?"],["","Bilkul true."],["","To ek jo doosron se anya hai, aur anya jo ek se anya hai, kyunki 'anya' word dono par laagu hota hai, same sthiti mein honge; aur jo same sthiti mein hai woh samaan hai?"],["","Haan."],["","To us gun ke kaaran jisse ek doosron se anya hai, har cheez har cheez ke samaan hogi, kyunki har cheez har cheez se anya hai."],["","True."],["","Phir, samaan asamaan ka vipreet hai?"],["","Haan."],["","Aur anya same ka?"],["","Phir true."],["","Aur ek doosron ke same bhi dikhaaya gaya tha?"],["","Haan."],["","Aur doosron ke same hona doosron se anya hone ka vipreet hai?"],["","Certainly."],["","Aur jahan tak woh anya tha, use samaan dikhaaya gaya tha?"],["","Haan."],["","Par jahan tak woh same tha, woh us gun ke vipreet gun ke kaaran asamaan hoga jisne use samaan banaaya; aur woh anyata ka gun tha."],["","Haan."],["","To same use asamaan banaayega; varna woh anya ka vipreet nahi hoga."],["","True."],["","To ek doosron ke samaan aur asamaan dono hoga; samaan jahan tak woh anya hai, aur asamaan jahan tak woh same hai."],["","Haan, yeh argument istemaal kiya ja sakta hai."],["","Aur ek aur argument hai."],["","Kya?"],["","Jahan tak woh same tarah prabhaavit hai woh alag tarah prabhaavit nahi, aur alag tarah prabhaavit na hone se asamaan nahi, aur asamaan na hone se, samaan hai; par jahan tak woh anya se prabhaavit hai woh alag hai, aur alag tarah prabhaavit hone se asamaan hai."],["","True."],["","To kyunki ek doosron ke same hai aur doosron se anya, in do aadhaaron mein se kisi par bhi, ya dono par, woh doosron ke samaan aur asamaan dono hoga?"],["","Certainly."],["","Aur isi tarah khud se anya aur khud ke same hone se, in do aadhaaron mein se kisi par bhi aur dono par, woh khud ke samaan aur asamaan hoga?"],["","Of course."]]},{"tag":"148d","title":"Chhoona aur na chhoona","paras":[["","Phir, ek khud ko aur doosron ko kahan tak chhoo sakta hai ya nahi chhoo sakta?—vichaar karo."],["","Main vichaar kar raha hoon."],["","Ek ko khud mein dikhaaya gaya tha jo ek sampoorn tha?"],["","True."],["","Aur doosri cheezon mein bhi?"],["","Haan."],["","Jahan tak woh doosri cheezon mein hai woh doosri cheezon ko chhooega, par jahan tak woh khud mein hai woh unhe chhoone se roka jaayega, aur sirf khud ko chhooega."],["","Spasht roop se."],["","To nishkarsh yeh hai ki woh dono ko chhooega?"],["","Chhooega."],["","Par ek naye drishtikon par tum kya kehte ho? Kya jo kisi doosre ko chhoone wala hai use us ke bagal mein nahi hona chahiye jise use chhoona hai, aur us jagah ke sabse nikat ki jagah nahi gherni chahiye jismein woh hai jise woh chhoota hai?"],["","True."],["","To ek, agar use khud ko chhoona hai, to khud ke bagal mein sthit hona chahiye, aur us jagah ke bagal ki jagah gherni chahiye jismein woh khud hai?"],["","Hona chahiye."],["","Aur iske liye aavashyak hoga ki ek do ho, aur ek saath do jagahon mein ho, aur yeh, jab tak woh ek hai, kabhi nahi hoga."],["","Nahi."],["","To ek khud ko utna hi nahi chhoo sakta jitna woh do nahi ho sakta?"],["","Nahi chhoo sakta."],["","Na hi woh doosron ko chhoo sakta hai."],["","Kyun nahi?"],["","Kaaran yeh hai, ki jo kuch kisi doosre ko chhoone wala hai use us se alag, aur uske bagal mein hona chahiye jise use chhoona hai, aur unke beech koi teesri cheez nahi ho sakti."],["","True."],["","To sampark sambhav banaane ke liye kam se kam do cheezein zaroori hain?"],["","Hain."],["","Aur agar do mein uchit kram mein ek teesri jodi jaaye, to padon ki sankhya teen hogi, aur sampark do?"],["","Haan."],["","Aur har atirikt pad ek atirikt sampark banaata hai, jisse yeh nikalta hai ki sampark sankhya mein padon se ek kam hain; pehle do pad samparkon ki sankhya se ek adhik the, aur padon ki poori sankhya isi tarah samparkon ki poori sankhya se ek adhik hai; aur har ek ke liye jo baad mein padon ki sankhya mein joda jaata hai, samparkon mein ek sampark judta hai."],["","True."],["","Cheezon ki poori sankhya jo bhi ho, sampark hamesha ek kam honge."],["","True."],["","Par agar sirf ek ho, aur do nahi, to koi sampark nahi hoga?"],["","Kaise ho sakta hai?"],["","Aur kya hum nahi kehte ki doosre ek se anya hone ke kaaran ek nahi hain aur ek mein unka koi hissa nahi?"],["","True."],["","To unki koi sankhya nahi, agar unmein koi ek nahi?"],["","Of course nahi."],["","To doosre na ek hain na do, na woh kisi sankhya ke naam se pukaare jaate hain?"],["","Nahi."],["","Ek, to, akela ek hai, aur do maujood nahi?"],["","Spasht roop se nahi."],["","Aur agar do nahi hain, to koi sampark nahi?"],["","Nahi hai."],["","To na ek doosron ko chhoota hai, na doosre ek ko, agar koi sampark nahi?"],["","Certainly nahi."],["","In sab kaaranon se ek khud ko aur doosron ko chhoota bhi hai aur nahi bhi chhoota?"],["","True."]]},{"tag":"149d","title":"Baraabar aur asamaan, bada aur chhota","paras":[["","Aage—kya ek khud ke aur doosron ke baraabar aur asamaan (unequal) hai?"],["","Tumhara kya matlab hai?"],["","Agar ek doosron se bada ya chhota hota, ya doosre ek se bade ya chhote, to woh ek aur doosre hone ke kaaran ek doosre se bade ya chhote nahi hote; par, agar jo woh hain uske alawa unmein baraabari hoti, to woh ek doosre ke baraabar hote, ya agar ek mein chhotapan aur doosron mein badappan hota, ya ek mein badappan aur doosron mein chhotapan—jis prakaar mein badappan hota woh bada hota, aur jismein chhotapan hota woh chhota?"],["","Certainly."],["","To badappan aur chhotapan jaise do ideas hain; kyunki agar woh na hote to woh ek doosre ke vipreet na hote aur us mein upasthit na hote jo hai."],["","Kaise ho sakte?"],["","Agar, to, chhotapan ek mein upasthit hai to woh ya to sampoorn mein upasthit hoga ya sampoorn ke ek hisse mein?"],["","Certainly."],["","Pehla maan lo; woh ya to poore ek ke sam-maan aur sam-vistaar hoga, ya ek ko samaayega?"],["","Spasht roop se."],["","Agar woh ek ke sam-vistaar hai to woh ek ke sam-maan hoga, ya agar ek ko samaata hai to woh ek se bada hoga?"],["","Of course."],["","Par kya chhotapan kisi cheez ke baraabar ya kisi cheez se bada ho sakta hai, aur badappan aur baraabari ke kaam kar sakta hai aur apne kaam nahi?"],["","Asambhav."],["","To chhotapan ek ke sampoorn mein nahi ho sakta, balki, agar ho, to sirf ek hisse mein?"],["","Haan."],["","Aur nishchit roop se hisse ke sab mein nahi, kyunki tab sampoorn ki kathinaai lautegi; woh kisi bhi hisse ke baraabar ya usse bada hoga jismein woh hai."],["","Certainly."],["","To chhotapan kisi cheez mein nahi hoga, chaahe sampoorn mein ho ya hisse mein; na vaastavik chhotepan ke alawa koi cheez chhoti hogi."],["","True."],["","Na hi badappan ek mein hoga, kyunki agar badappan kisi cheez mein ho to badappan ke alawa aur usse alag kuch bada hoga, arthaat, woh jismein badappan hai; aur yeh bhi jab chhota khud wahan nahi, jisse ek ko, agar woh bada hai, badhkar hona chahiye; par yeh asambhav hai, yeh dekhte hue ki chhotapan poori tarah anupasthit hai."],["","True."],["","Par nirpeksh badappan sirf nirpeksh chhotepan se bada hai, aur chhotapan sirf nirpeksh badappan se chhota hai."],["","Bahut true."],["","To doosri cheezein ek se badi ya chhoti nahi, agar unmein na badappan hai na chhotapan; na hi badappan ya chhotepan mein ek ke sambandh mein badhne ya pichhadne ki koi shakti hai, balki sirf ek doosre ke sambandh mein; na hi ek unse ya doosron se bada ya chhota hoga, agar usmein na badappan hai na chhotapan."],["","Spasht roop se nahi."],["","To agar ek doosron se na bada hai na chhota, to woh na unse badh sakta hai na unse pichhad sakta hai?"],["","Certainly nahi."],["","Aur jo na badhta hai na pichhadta hai, use baraabari par hona chahiye; aur baraabari par hone se, baraabar hona chahiye."],["","Of course."],["","Aur yeh ek ke khud se sambandh ke baare mein bhi true hoga; khud mein na badappan na chhotapan rakhte hue, woh na khud se badhega na pichhadega, balki khud ke saath baraabari par aur khud ke baraabar hoga."],["","Certainly."],["","To ek khud ke aur doosron ke dono ke baraabar hoga?"],["","Spasht roop se aisa."],["","Aur phir bhi ek, khud khud mein hote hue, khud ko gherega bhi aur khud se baahar bhi hoga; aur, khud ko samaate hue, khud se bada hoga; aur, khud mein samaaye hone ke roop mein, chhota hoga; aur is tarah khud se bada aur chhota hoga."],["","Hoga."],["","Ab aisi koi cheez sambhav nahi jo ek aur doosron mein shaamil na ho?"],["","Of course nahi."],["","Par, nishchit roop se, jo hai use hamesha kahin hona chahiye?"],["","Haan."],["","Par jo kisi cheez mein hai woh chhota hoga, aur jismein woh hai woh bada hoga; kisi aur tarah ek cheez doosri mein nahi ho sakti."],["","True."],["","Aur kyunki ek aur doosron ke alawa ya unse alag kuch nahi, aur unhe kisi cheez mein hona chahiye, to kya unhe ek doosre mein nahi hona chahiye, ek doosron mein aur doosre ek mein, agar unhe kahin hona hai?"],["","Yeh spasht hai."],["","Par jahan tak ek doosron mein hai, doosre ek se bade honge, kyunki woh ek ko samaate hain, jo doosron se chhota hoga, kyunki woh unmein samaaya hai; aur jahan tak doosre ek mein hain, ek usi siddhaant par doosron se bada hoga, aur doosre ek se chhote."],["","True."],["","Ek, to, khud ke aur doosron ke baraabar aur unse bada aur chhota hoga?"],["","Spasht roop se."],["","Aur agar woh bada aur chhota aur baraabar hai, to woh khud aur doosron se baraabar aur adhik aur kam maapon ya vibhaagon ka hoga, aur agar maapon ka, to hisson ka bhi?"],["","Of course."],["","Aur agar baraabar aur adhik aur kam maapon ya vibhaagon ka, to woh sankhya mein khud aur doosron se adhik ya kam hoga, aur isi tarah sankhya mein khud aur doosron ke baraabar?"],["","Woh kaise?"],["","Woh un cheezon se adhik maapon ka hoga jinse woh badhkar hai, aur utne hisson ka jitne maap; aur isi tarah us ke saath jiske woh baraabar hai, aur us ke saath jisse woh chhota hai."],["","True."],["","Aur khud se bada aur chhota, aur khud ke baraabar hone se, woh khud ke saath baraabar maapon ka aur khud se adhik aur kam maapon ka hoga; aur agar maapon ka to hisson ka bhi?"],["","Hoga."],["","Aur khud ke saath baraabar hisson ka hone se, woh sankhya mein khud ke baraabar hoga; aur adhik hisson ka hone se, adhik, aur kam ka hone se, khud se kam?"],["","Certainly."],["","Aur yahi doosri cheezon se uske sambandh par laagu hoga; jahan tak woh unse bada hai, woh sankhya mein unse adhik hoga; aur jahan tak woh chhota hai, woh sankhya mein kam hoga; aur jahan tak woh aakaar mein doosri cheezon ke baraabar hai, woh sankhya mein unke baraabar hoga."],["","Certainly."],["","Ek baar phir, to, jaisa dikhta hai, ek sankhya mein khud aur sab doosri cheezon dono ke baraabar aur unse adhik aur kam hoga."],["","Hoga."]]},{"tag":"151e","title":"Ek aur samay","paras":[["","Kya ek samay mein bhi hissa leta hai? Aur kya woh samay mein sahbhaagita ke kaaran khud aur doosron se bada aur chhota hai aur hota hai, aur phir, khud aur doosron se na chhota na bada?"],["","Tumhara kya matlab hai?"],["","Agar ek hai, to us par being laagu hona chahiye?"],["","Haan."],["","Par hona (einai) sirf vartamaan samay mein being ki sahbhaagita hai, aur ho chuka hona beete samay mein being ki sahbhaagita hai, aur hone wala hona bhavishya samay mein being ki sahbhaagita hai?"],["","Bahut true."],["","To ek, kyunki woh being mein hissa leta hai, samay mein hissa leta hai?"],["","Certainly."],["","Aur kya samay hamesha aage nahi badhta rehta?"],["","Haan."],["","To ek hamesha khud se bada (older) hota ja raha hai, kyunki woh samay mein aage badhta hai?"],["","Certainly."],["","Aur kya tumhe yaad hai ki bada (older) us se bada hota hai jo chhota hota ja raha hai?"],["","Mujhe yaad hai."],["","To kyunki ek khud se bada hota hai, woh saath hi chhota bhi hota hai?"],["","Certainly."],["","Is tarah, to, ek khud se bada aur chhota dono hota hai?"],["","Haan."],["","Aur woh bada hai (hai na?) jab hote-hote, woh 'tha' aur 'hoga' ke beech samay ke us bindu par pahunchta hai, jo 'ab' hai: kyunki nishchit roop se ateet se bhavishya ki or jaate hue, woh vartamaan ko laangh nahi sakta?"],["","Nahi."],["","Aur jab woh vartamaan par pahunchta hai to bada hona band kar deta hai, aur ab hota nahi, balki bada hai, kyunki agar woh aage badhta rehta to vartamaan kabhi usse nahi pahunchta, kyunki jo aage badhta hai uski nature hai ki woh vartamaan aur bhavishya dono ko chhue, vartamaan ko chhodte hue aur bhavishya ko pakadte hue, jab woh unke beech hone ki prakriya mein ho."],["","True."],["","Par jo ho raha hai woh vartamaan ko laangh nahi sakta; jab woh vartamaan par pahunchta hai to hona band kar deta hai, aur tab wahi hai jo woh ho raha ho."],["","Spasht roop se."],["","Aur is tarah ek, jab bada hote hue vartamaan par pahunchta hai, hona band kar deta hai, aur tab bada hai."],["","Certainly."],["","Aur woh us se bada hai jisse woh bada ho raha tha, aur woh khud se bada ho raha tha."],["","Haan."],["","Aur jo bada hai woh chhote se bada hai?"],["","True."],["","To ek khud se chhota hai, jab bada hote hue woh vartamaan par pahunchta hai?"],["","Certainly."],["","Par vartamaan ek ke saath uske poore being ke dauraan hamesha upasthit hai; kyunki jab bhi woh hai woh hamesha ab hai."],["","Certainly."],["","To ek hamesha khud se bada aur chhota hai bhi aur hota bhi hai?"],["","Sach mein."],["","Aur kya woh khud se adhik samay tak hai ya hota hai ya khud ke baraabar samay tak?"],["","Baraabar samay tak."],["","Par agar woh khud ke baraabar samay tak hota hai ya hai, to woh khud ke same umra ka hai?"],["","Of course."],["","Aur jo same umra ka hai, woh na bada hai na chhota?"],["","Nahi."],["","Ek, to, khud ke saath same samay hote aur rehte hue, na khud se bada ya chhota hai na hota hai?"],["","Main kahunga ki nahi."],["","Aur doosri cheezon ke saath uske sambandh kya hain? Kya woh unse bada ya chhota hai ya hota hai?"],["","Main tumhe nahi bata sakta."],["","Tum kam se kam mujhe yeh bata sakte ho ki ek se anya ek se adhik hain—anya ek hota, par doosron mein bahulta hai, aur woh ek se adhik hain?"],["","Unmein bahulta hogi."],["","Aur bahulta ek se badi sankhya ko imply karti hai?"],["","Of course."],["","Aur kya hum kahein ki chhota ya bada astitva mein pehle aata hai ya aaya hai?"],["","Chhota."],["","To sabse chhota pehla hai? Aur woh ek hai?"],["","Haan."],["","To sankhya wali sab cheezon mein ek pehla astitva mein aata hai; par baaki sab cheezon ki bhi sankhya hai, bahuvachan hone se aur ekvachan nahi."],["","Hai."],["","Aur kyunki woh pehle astitva mein aaya, to maanna hoga ki woh doosron se pehle astitva mein aaya, aur doosre baad mein; aur jo cheezein baad mein astitva mein aayi, woh us se chhoti hain jo unse pehle aaya? Aur is tarah doosri cheezein ek se chhoti hongi, aur ek doosri cheezon se bada?"],["","True."],["","Ek aur question ke baare mein tum kya kahoge? Kya ek apni nature ke viruddh astitva mein aa sakta hai, ya yeh asambhav hai?"],["","Asambhav."],["","Aur phir bhi, nishchit roop se, ek ke hisse dikhaaye gaye the; aur agar hisse, to aarambh, madhya aur ant?"],["","Haan."],["","Aur aarambh, ek khud ka aur sab doosri cheezon ka bhi, sabse pehle astitva mein aata hai; aur aarambh ke baad, doosre aate hain, jab tak tum ant tak na pahuncho?"],["","Certainly."],["","Aur in sab doosron ko hum sampoorn ke aur ek ke hisse kahenge, jo, jaise hi ant pahunchta hai, sampoorn aur ek ho chuka hai?"],["","Haan; hum yahi kahenge."],["","Par ant sabse aakhir mein aata hai, aur ek aisi nature ka hai ki woh antim ke saath astitva mein aata hai; aur, kyunki ek apni nature ke anusaar hi astitva mein aa sakta hai, uski nature yeh maangegi ki woh doosron ke baad, ant ke saath-saath, astitva mein aaye."],["","Spasht roop se."],["","To ek doosron se chhota hai aur doosre ek se bade."],["","Woh bhi mere nirnay mein spasht hai."],["","Achha, aur kya ek ka ya kisi cheez ka aarambh ya koi aur hissa, agar woh hissa hai aur hisse nahi, hissa hote hue, avashya ek bhi nahi hona chahiye?"],["","Certainly."],["","Aur kya ek har hisse ke saath astitva mein nahi aayega—pehle hisse ke saath jab woh astitva mein aata hai, aur doosre hisse aur baaki sab ke saath, aur kisi hisse mein kam nahi padega, jo kisi doosre hisse mein joda jaata hai jab tak woh antim tak pahunch kar ek sampoorn na ban jaaye; woh na madhya mein, na pehle mein, na antim mein, na unmein se kisi mein kam padega, jab tak hone ki prakriya chal rahi hai?"],["","True."],["","To ek baaki sab ke same umra ka hai, taaki agar ek khud apni nature ka khandan na kare, to woh na doosron se pehle hoga na baad mein, balki saath-saath; aur is argument ke anusaar ek na doosron se bada hoga na chhota, na doosre ek se, par pichhle argument ke anusaar ek doosron se bada aur chhota hoga aur doosre ek se."],["","Certainly."],["","Is dhang se to ek hai aur ho chuka hai. Par uske doosron se bada aur chhota hone, aur doosron ke ek se, aur na bada na chhota hone ke baare mein, hum kya kahein? Kya hum being ki tarah hone ke baare mein bhi kahein, ya alag?"],["","Main jawaab nahi de sakta."],["","Par main yeh kehne ka saahas kar sakta hoon, ki agar ek cheez doosri se badi ya chhoti bhi ho, to woh pehle se adhik maatra mein badi ya chhoti nahi ho sakti; kyunki asamaanon mein baraabar jodne se, chaahe samay-avadhiyon mein ya kisi aur cheez mein, unke beech ka antar pehle jaisa hi rehta hai."],["","Of course."],["","To jo hai, woh us se bada ya chhota nahi ho sakta jo hai, kyunki umra ka antar hamesha same rehta hai; ek bada hai aur ho chuka hai aur doosra chhota; par woh ab aise ho nahi rahe."],["","True."],["","Aur jo ek hai woh isliye un doosron se na bada hota hai na chhota jo hain."],["","Nahi."],["","Par vichaar karo ki kya woh kisi aur tarah bade aur chhote nahi ho sakte."],["","Kis tarah?"],["","Bilkul jaise ek doosron se bada aur doosre ek se bade siddh kiye gaye the."],["","Aur usmein kya?"],["","Agar ek doosron se bada hai, to woh doosron se adhik samay se astitva mein hai."],["","Haan."],["","Par phir vichaar karo; agar hum ek bade aur ek chhote samay mein baraabar samay jodein, to kya bada chhote samay se baraabar ya pehle se chhote hisse se alag hoga?"],["","Chhote hisse se."],["","To ek ki umra aur doosron ki umra ke beech antar baad mein utna bada nahi hoga jitna pehle, balki agar dono mein baraabar samay joda jaaye to woh umra mein kam se kam alag honge?"],["","Haan."],["","Aur jo umra mein kisi doosre se pehle se kam alag hai, woh bada hone se, us doosre ke sambandh mein chhota ho jaayega jisse woh bada tha?"],["","Haan, chhota."],["","Aur agar ek chhota hota hai to ukt doosre ek ke sambandh mein pehle se bade ho jaayenge."],["","Certainly."],["","To jo chhota ho gaya tha woh us ke saapeksh bada hota hai jo pehle ho chuka tha aur bada tha; woh vaastav mein kabhi bada nahi hai, balki hamesha ho raha hai, kyunki ek hamesha yauvan ki or badh raha hai aur doosra budhaape ki or. Aur isi tarah bada hamesha chhote se chhota hone ki prakriya mein hai; kyunki kyunki woh hamesha vipreet dishaaon mein ja rahe hain woh ek doosre ke vipreet tarikon se hote hain, chhota bade se bada, aur bada chhote se chhota. Par woh ho chuke nahi ho sakte; kyunki agar woh pehle hi ho chuke hote to woh hote aur sirf ho nahi rahe hote. Par yeh asambhav hai; kyunki woh hamesha ek doosre se bade aur chhote dono ho rahe hain: ek doosron se chhota hota hai kyunki woh bada aur pehle dikha tha, aur doosre ek se bade hote hain kyunki woh baad mein astitva mein aaye; aur isi tarah doosre ek ke saath same sambandh mein hain, kyunki woh bade, aur ek se pehle dikhe the."],["","Yeh spasht hai."],["","Jahan tak, to, ek cheez doosri se badi ya chhoti nahi hoti, kyunki woh hamesha ek doosre se baraabar sankhya se alag hoti hain, ek doosron se bada ya chhota nahi ho sakta, na doosre ek se; par jahan tak jo pehle astitva mein aaya aur jo baad mein astitva mein aaya unhe lagaataar ek doosre se alag hisse se alag hona chahiye—is drishti se doosron ko ek se bada aur chhota hona chahiye, aur ek ko doosron se."],["","Certainly."],["","In sab kaaranon se, to, ek khud aur doosron se bada aur chhota hai aur hota hai, aur na khud ya doosron se bada ya chhota hai na hota hai."],["","Certainly."],["","Par kyunki ek samay mein hissa leta hai, aur bada aur chhota hone mein hissa leta hai, to kya use ateet, vartamaan, aur bhavishya mein bhi hissa nahi lena chahiye?"],["","Of course lena chahiye."],["","To ek tha aur hai aur hoga, aur ho raha tha aur ho raha hai aur hoga?"],["","Certainly."],["","Aur kuch hai aur tha aur hoga jo uske sambandh mein hai aur uska hai?"],["","True."],["","Aur kyunki is kshan hamare paas ek ki raay aur knowledge aur perception hai, to uski raay aur knowledge aur perception hai?"],["","Bilkul sahi."],["","To uske liye naam aur abhivyakti hai, aur woh naamit aur vyakt hai, aur is prakaar ki har cheez jo doosri cheezon se sambandhit hai ek se sambandhit hai."],["","Certainly, yeh true hai."]]},{"tag":"155e","title":"Being lena aur chhodna","paras":[["","Phir bhi ek baar aur aur teesri baar, aao vichaar karein: Agar ek ek aur anek dono hai, jaisa humne varnan kiya, aur na ek na anek, aur samay mein hissa leta hai, to kya use, jahan tak woh ek hai, kabhi-kabhi being mein hissa nahi lena chahiye, aur jahan tak woh ek nahi, kabhi-kabhi being mein hissa nahi lena chahiye?"],["","Certainly."],["","Par kya woh being mein hissa na lete hue being mein hissa le sakta hai, ya being mein hissa lete hue being mein hissa na le?"],["","Asambhav."],["","To ek alag-alag samay par being mein hissa leta hai aur nahi leta, kyunki yahi ekmaatra tarika hai jisse woh same mein hissa le bhi aur na bhi le."],["","True."],["","Aur kya koi samay bhi nahi jab woh being dhaaran karta hai aur being chhodta hai—kyunki woh same cheez ko kaise rakh bhi aur na rakh bhi sakta hai jab tak woh kisi samay use grahan aur tyaag na kare?"],["","Asambhav."],["","Aur being dhaaran karne ko tum utpatti (becoming) kahoge?"],["","Kahunga."],["","Aur being chhodne ko tum vinaash kahoge?"],["","Kahunga."],["","Ek to, jaisa dikhta hai, being lekar aur chhod kar utpann hota hai aur nasht hota hai."],["","Certainly."],["","Aur ek aur anek hote hue aur utpann aur nasht hone ki prakriya mein, jab woh ek hota hai to anek hona band kar deta hai, aur jab anek, to ek hona band kar deta hai?"],["","Certainly."],["","Aur jaise woh ek aur anek hota hai, kya use anivaarya roop se alagaav aur ekatrikaran ka anubhav nahi karna chahiye?"],["","Anivaarya roop se."],["","Aur jab bhi woh samaan aur asamaan hota hai to use samaan aur asamaan banna hoga?"],["","Haan."],["","Aur jab woh bada ya chhota ya baraabar hota hai to use badhna ya ghatna ya baraabar hona hoga?"],["","True."],["","Aur jab gati mein hote hue woh rukta hai, aur sthir hote hue gati mein badalta hai, to woh nishchit roop se kisi samay mein nahi ho sakta?"],["","Kaise ho sakta hai?"],["","Par yeh ki jo cheez pehle sthir ho woh baad mein gati mein ho, ya pehle gati mein aur baad mein sthir, bina parivartan ka anubhav kiye, asambhav hai."],["","Asambhav."],["","Aur nishchit roop se aisa koi samay nahi ho sakta jismein koi cheez ek saath na gati mein ho na sthir?"],["","Nahi ho sakta."],["","Par na hi woh badle bina badal sakti hai."],["","True."],["","To woh kab badalti hai; kyunki woh na sthir hote hue badal sakti hai, na gati mein hote hue, na samay mein hote hue?"],["","Nahi badal sakti."]]},{"tag":"156d","title":"Kshan (the instant)","paras":[["","Aur kya yeh ajeeb cheez jismein woh badalne ke samay hoti hai vaastav mein maujood hai?"],["","Kaun-si cheez?"],["","Kshan (the moment). Kyunki kshan kuch aisa imply karta lagta hai jisse parivartan do avasthaaon mein se kisi mein hota hai; kyunki parivartan na sthirta ki avastha se hota hai, na gati ki avastha se; balki yeh vichitra nature hai jise hum kshan kehte hain jo sthirta aur gati ke beech padi hai, kisi samay mein na hote hue; aur isme aur isse baahar jo gati mein hai woh sthirta mein badalta hai, aur jo sthir hai woh gati mein."],["","Aisa dikhta hai."],["","Aur ek to, kyunki woh sthir hai aur gati mein bhi, dono mein se kisi mein badlega, kyunki sirf isi tarah woh dono mein ho sakta hai. Aur badalte hue woh kshan mein badalta hai, aur jab woh badal raha hai to woh kisi samay mein nahi hoga, aur tab na gati mein hoga na sthir."],["","Nahi hoga."],["","Aur doosre parivartanon ke sambandh mein bhi woh same sthiti mein hoga, jab woh being se being ke ant mein, ya not-being se utpatti mein jaata hai—tab woh gati aur sthirta ki kuch avasthaaon ke beech se guzarta hai, aur na hai na nahi hai, na utpann hota hai na nasht hota hai."],["","Bahut true."],["","Aur isi siddhaant par, ek se anek aur anek se ek mein jaane mein, ek na ek hai na anek, na alag na ekatrit; aur samaan se asamaan, aur asamaan se samaan mein jaane mein, woh na samaan hai na asamaan, na samaan banne ki avastha mein na asamaan banne ki; aur chhote se bade aur baraabar aur waapas jaane mein, woh na chhota hoga na bada, na baraabar, na vriddhi, ya hraas, ya sam-karan ki avastha mein."],["","True."],["","To yeh sab, ek ke gun hain, agar ek ka being hai."],["","Of course."]]},{"tag":"157b","title":"Agar ek hai: doosre","paras":[["","1.aa. Par agar ek hai, to doosron ka kya hoga—kya is par bhi vichaar nahi karna chahiye?"],["","Haan."],["","To aao dikhaayein, agar ek hai, to ek se anya doosron ke gun kya honge."],["","Aao aisa karein."],["","Kyunki ek se anya cheezein hain, doosre ek nahi hain; kyunki agar hote to woh ek se anya nahi ho sakte the."],["","Bahut true."],["","Na hi doosre ek se poori tarah rahit hain, balki ek tarah se woh ek mein hissa lete hain."],["","Kis tarah?"],["","Kyunki doosre ek se anya isliye hain ki unke hisse hain; kyunki agar unke hisse na hote to woh bas ek hote."],["","Sahi."],["","Aur hisse, jaisa hum kehte hain, sampoorn se sambandh rakhte hain?"],["","Hum aisa kehte hain."],["","Aur sampoorn avashya anek se bana ek hona chahiye; aur hisse ek ke hisse honge, kyunki har hissa anek ka hissa nahi, balki ek sampoorn ka hai."],["","Tumhara kya matlab hai?"],["","Agar koi cheez anek ka hissa hoti, khud unmein se ek hote hue, to woh nishchit roop se khud ka hissa hogi, jo asambhav hai, aur woh doosre hisson mein se har ek ka hissa hogi, agar sab ka; kyunki agar kisi ek ka hissa nahi, to woh is ek ke alawa baaki sab ka hissa hogi, aur is tarah har ek ka hissa nahi hogi; aur agar har ek ka hissa nahi, to woh anek mein se kisi ek ka hissa nahi hogi; aur kisi ek ka hissa na hone se, woh un sab cheezon ka hissa ya kuch aur nahi ho sakti jinmein se kisi ki woh kuch nahi."],["","Spasht roop se nahi."],["","To hissa na anek ka hissa hai, na sab ka, balki ek nishchit akele roop ka hai, jise hum sampoorn kehte hain, jo sab se bani ek poorn ekta hai—iska hissa hissa hoga."],["","Certainly."],["","Agar, to, doosron ke hisse hain, to woh sampoorn mein aur ek mein hissa lenge."],["","True."],["","To ek se anya doosre ek poorn sampoorn hone chahiye, hisse rakhte hue."],["","Certainly."],["","Aur yahi argument har hisse par laagu hota hai, kyunki hisse ko ek mein hissa lena chahiye; kyunki agar hisson mein se har ek hissa hai, to iska matlab hai, mujhe lagta hai, ki woh baaki se alag aur swa-sambandhit ek hai; varna woh har ek nahi."],["","True."],["","Par jab hum hisse ke ek mein hissa lene ki baat karte hain, to use spasht roop se ek se anya hona chahiye; kyunki agar nahi, to usne sirf hissa nahi liya hota, balki woh ek hota; jabki sirf khud (ek) hi ek ho sakta hai."],["","Bahut true."],["","Sampoorn aur hissa dono ko ek mein hissa lena chahiye; kyunki sampoorn ek sampoorn hoga, jiske hisse hisse honge; aur har hissa sampoorn ka ek hissa hoga jo hisse ka sampoorn hai."],["","True."],["","Aur kya jo cheezein ek mein hissa leti hain, usse anya nahi hongi?"],["","Of course."],["","Aur jo cheezein ek se anya hain woh anek hongi; kyunki agar jo cheezein ek se anya hain woh na ek hoti na ek se adhik, to woh kuch nahi hoti."],["","True."],["","Par, yeh dekhte hue ki jo cheezein hisse ke roop mein ek mein, aur sampoorn ke roop mein ek mein hissa leti hain, ek se adhik hain, kya wahi cheezein jo ek mein hissa leti hain sankhya mein anant nahi honi chahiye?"],["","Kaise?"],["","Aao maamle ko is tarah dekhein:—Kya yeh tathya nahi ki ek mein hissa lete hue woh ek nahi hain, aur jis samay woh usmein hissa le rahi hain usi samay ek mein hissa nahi leti?"],["","Spasht roop se."],["","To woh aisa bheedon (multitudes) ke roop mein karti hain jinmein ek upasthit nahi?"],["","Bahut true."],["","Aur agar hum vichaar mein unse sabse chhota ansh alag karein, to kya woh sabse chhota ansh, agar woh ek mein hissa nahi leta, bheed nahi hona chahiye aur ek nahi?"],["","Hona chahiye."],["","Aur agar hum unki nature ke doosre pehlu ko dekhte rahein, saral roop se, aur swayam mein dekha jaaye, to kya woh, jahan tak hum unhe dekhte hain, sankhya mein aseemit nahi hongi?"],["","Certainly."],["","Aur phir bhi, jab har alag hissa hissa banta hai, to hisson ki sampoorn aur ek doosre ke sambandh mein seema hoti hai, aur sampoorn ki hisson ke sambandh mein."],["","Bilkul aisa hi."],["","Ek se anya doosron ke liye parinaam yeh hai ki unka aur ek ka mel unmein ek naya tattva paida karta dikhta hai jo unhe ek doosre ke sambandh mein seema deta hai; jabki apni nature mein unki koi seema nahi."],["","Yeh spasht hai."],["","To ek se anya doosre, sampoorn aur hisson dono ke roop mein, anant hain, aur seema mein bhi hissa lete hain."],["","Certainly."],["","To woh ek doosre ke aur khud ke samaan aur asamaan dono hain."],["","Woh kaise?"],["","Jahan tak woh apni nature mein aseemit hain, woh sab same tarah prabhaavit hain."],["","True."],["","Aur jahan tak woh sab seema mein hissa lete hain, woh sab same tarah prabhaavit hain."],["","Of course."],["","Par jahan tak unki avastha seemit aur aseemit dono hai, woh vipreet tarikon se prabhaavit hain."],["","Haan."],["","Aur vipreet cheezon mein sabse asamaan hain."],["","Certainly."],["","To, unke gunon mein se kisi ek ke sandarbh mein dekhe jaane par, woh khud ke aur ek doosre ke samaan honge; dono ke ek saath sandarbh mein, sabse vipreet aur sabse asamaan."],["","Yeh true dikhta hai."],["","To doosre khud ke aur ek doosre ke samaan aur asamaan dono hain?"],["","True."],["","Aur woh ek doosre ke same aur alag bhi hain, aur gati mein aur sthir, aur har prakaar ke vipreet gun ka anubhav karte hain, jaisa bina kathinaai ke unke baare mein siddh kiya ja sakta hai, kyunki unhe ukt gunon ka anubhav karte dikhaaya ja chuka hai?"],["","True."]]},{"tag":"159b","title":"Ek se kate hue doosre","paras":[["","1.bb. Maan lo, ab, ki hum in maamlon ki aage ki charcha ko spasht maan kar chhod dein, aur is hypothesis par phir vichaar karein ki ek hai, ki kya is sab ka vipreet doosron ke baare mein utna hi true hai ya nahi."],["","Zaroor."],["","To aao phir se shuru karein, aur poochhein, Agar ek hai, to doosron ke gun kya hone chahiye?"],["","Aao woh question poochhein."],["","Kya ek ko doosron se alag nahi hona chahiye, aur doosron ko ek se?"],["","Kyun?"],["","Kyun, kyunki unke alawa aur kuch nahi jo dono se alag ho; kyunki 'ek aur doosre' abhivyakti mein sab cheezein shaamil hain."],["","Haan, sab cheezein."],["","To hum yeh nahi maan sakte ki unse alag kuch hai jismein ek aur doosre dono maujood ho sakein?"],["","Kuch nahi hai."],["","To ek aur doosre kabhi same mein nahi?"],["","True."],["","To woh ek doosre se alag hain?"],["","Haan."],["","Aur hum nishchit roop se nahi keh sakte ki jo vaastav mein ek hai uske hisse hain?"],["","Asambhav."],["","To ek doosron mein na sampoorn ke roop mein hoga, na hisse ke roop mein, agar woh doosron se alag hai, aur uske hisse nahi?"],["","Asambhav."],["","To aisa koi tarika nahi jisse doosre ek mein hissa le sakein, agar woh na sampoorn mein na hisse mein hissa lete hain?"],["","Aisa lagta hai ki nahi."],["","To aisa koi tarika nahi jisse doosre ek hon, ya khud mein koi ekta rakhein?"],["","Nahi hai."],["","Na hi doosre anek hain; kyunki agar woh anek hote, to unka har hissa sampoorn ka hissa hota; par ab doosre, kisi tarah ek mein hissa na lete hue, na ek hain na anek, na sampoorn, na hissa."],["","True."],["","To doosre na do ya teen hain na unhe samaate hain, agar ek se poori tarah vanchit hain?"],["","True."],["","To doosre na ek ke samaan hain na asamaan, na unmein samaanta aur asamaanta hai; kyunki agar woh samaan aur asamaan hote, ya unmein samaanta aur asamaanta hoti, to unmein ek doosre ki vipreet do natures hoti."],["","Yeh spasht hai."],["","Par jo kisi cheez mein hissa nahi leta uska do cheezon mein hissa lena hamare dwara asambhav maana gaya tha?"],["","Asambhav."],["","To doosre na samaan hain na asamaan na dono, kyunki agar woh samaan ya asamaan hote to woh un do natures mein se ek mein hissa lete, jo ek cheez hoti, aur agar woh dono hote to woh vipreeton mein hissa lete jo do cheezein hoti, aur yeh asambhav dikhaaya ja chuka hai."],["","True."],["","Isliye woh na same hain, na anya, na gati mein, na sthir, na utpatti ki avastha mein, na vinaash ki, na bade, na chhote, na baraabar, na unhone is prakaar ka kuch aur anubhav kiya hai; kyunki, agar woh aisa koi gun anubhav karne mein saksham hain, to woh ek aur do aur teen, aur vishamm aur samm mein hissa lenge, aur inmein, jaisa siddh kiya ja chuka hai, woh hissa nahi lete, yeh dekhte hue ki woh poori tarah aur har tarah ek se rahit hain."],["","Bahut true."],["","Isliye agar ek hai, to ek sab cheezein hai, aur kuch bhi nahi, khud ke sambandh mein bhi aur doosri cheezon ke sambandh mein bhi."],["","Certainly."]]},{"tag":"160b","title":"Nigaman: agar ek nahi hai","paras":[["","2.a. Achha, aur kya hamein agla yeh vichaar nahi karna chahiye ki agar ek nahi hai to parinaam kya hoga?"],["","Haan; karna chahiye."],["","Is hypothesis ka arth kya hai—Agar ek nahi hai; kya ismein aur is hypothesis mein koi antar hai—Agar na-ek nahi hai?"],["","Antar hai, certainly."],["","Kya sirf antar hai, ya balki kya do abhivyaktiyaan—agar ek nahi hai, aur agar na-ek nahi hai, poori tarah vipreet nahi?"],["","Woh poori tarah vipreet hain."],["","Aur maan lo koi kahe:—Agar badappan nahi hai, agar chhotapan nahi hai, ya is tarah ki koi cheez, to kya uska matlab, jab bhi woh aisi abhivyakti ka prayog karta hai, yeh nahi ki 'jo nahi hai' doosri cheezon se anya hai?"],["","Zaroor."],["","Aur isliye jab woh kehta hai 'Agar ek nahi hai' to uska spasht matlab hai, ki jo 'nahi hai' woh baaki sab se anya hai; hum jaante hain ki uska kya matlab hai—jaante hain na?"],["","Haan, jaante hain."],["","Jab woh 'ek' kehta hai, to woh kuch aisa kehta hai jo gyaat hai; aur doosre, kuch aisa jo baaki sab cheezon se anya hai; isse koi antar nahi padta ki woh ek par being laagu kare ya not-being, kyunki jise 'nahi hai' kaha jaata hai woh phir bhi kuch gyaat maana jaata hai, aur doosri cheezon se alag kiya jaata hai."],["","Certainly."],["","To main phir se shuru karunga, aur poochhunga: Agar ek nahi hai, to parinaam kya hain? Pehle sthaan par, jaisa dikhta hai, uska knowledge hai, varna 'agar ek nahi hai' words ka arth hi gyaat nahi hota."],["","True."],["","Doosre, doosre usse alag hain, varna use doosron se alag varnit nahi kiya ja sakta tha?"],["","Certainly."],["","Bhinnata, to, knowledge ki tarah uski bhi hai; kyunki ek ko doosron se alag kehte hue, hum doosron mein bhinnata ki baat nahi karte, balki ek mein."],["","Spasht roop se aisa."],["","Iske alawa, jo ek nahi hai woh kuch hai aur 'woh,' aur 'yeh,' aur 'ye,' aur aise se sambandh mein hissa leta hai, aur 'is' ka gun hai; kyunki ek, ya ek se anya doosron ki baat nahi ki ja sakti thi, na us ek ka jo nahi hai koi gun ya sambandhi ho sakta tha ya kaha ja sakta tha, na use kuch hona kaha ja sakta tha, agar woh 'kuch' mein, ya abhi bataaye gaye doosre sambandhon mein hissa na leta."],["","True."],["","Being, to, ek par laagu nahi kiya ja sakta, kyunki woh nahi hai; par jo ek nahi hai woh anek cheezon mein hissa le sakta hai ya balki use lena hi chahiye, agar woh aur kuch aur nahi hai; par agar, na ek na woh ek jo nahi hai, ka na hona maana jaaye, aur hum kisi alag nature ki cheez ki baat kar rahe hain, to hum uske baare mein kuch nahi keh sakte. Par maan lo ki woh ek jo nahi hai aur kuch aur nahi hai, to use 'woh' vidheya (predicate) mein, aur anek doosron mein hissa lena hoga."],["","Certainly."],["","Aur doosron ke sambandh mein usmein asamaanta hogi, kyunki doosre ek se alag hone se alag prakaar ke honge."],["","Certainly."],["","Aur kya alag prakaar ki cheezein prakaar mein anya bhi nahi?"],["","Of course."],["","Aur kya prakaar mein anya cheezein asamaan nahi?"],["","Woh asamaan hain."],["","Aur agar woh ek se asamaan hain, to jisse woh asamaan hain woh spasht roop se unse asamaan hoga?"],["","Spasht roop se aisa."],["","To ek mein asamaanta hogi jiske sandarbh mein doosre usse asamaan hain?"],["","Yeh true lagta hai."],["","Aur agar doosri cheezon se asamaanta usse judi hai, to usmein khud se samaanta honi chahiye."],["","Kaise?"],["","Agar ek mein ek se asamaanta ho, to kuch aur arth hoga; na hi hypothesis ek se sambandhit hogi; balki woh ek se anya kisi cheez se sambandhit hogi?"],["","Bilkul aisa."],["","Par aisa nahi ho sakta."],["","Nahi."],["","To ek mein khud se samaanta honi chahiye?"],["","Honi chahiye."],["","Phir, woh doosron ke baraabar nahi; kyunki agar woh baraabar hota, to woh baraabari ke kaaran turant hota aur unke samaan hota; par agar ek ka koi being nahi, to woh na ho sakta hai na samaan ho sakta hai?"],["","Nahi ho sakta."],["","Par kyunki woh doosron ke baraabar nahi, to na hi doosre uske baraabar ho sakte hain?"],["","Certainly nahi."],["","Aur jo cheezein baraabar nahi woh asamaan (unequal) hain?"],["","True."],["","Aur woh ek asamaan ke asamaan hain?"],["","Of course."],["","To ek asamaanta mein hissa leta hai, aur iske sandarbh mein doosre usse asamaan hain?"],["","Bahut true."],["","Aur asamaanta badappan aur chhotepan ko imply karti hai?"],["","Haan."],["","To ek, agar aisi nature ka hai, to usmein badappan aur chhotapan hai?"],["","Yeh true dikhta hai."],["","Aur badappan aur chhotapan hamesha alag khade rehte hain?"],["","True."],["","To unke beech hamesha kuch hota hai?"],["","Hota hai."],["","Aur kya tum baraabari ke alawa kisi aur cheez ka soch sakte ho jo unke beech ho?"],["","Nahi, baraabari hi hai jo unke beech padi hai."],["","To jismein badappan aur chhotapan hai usmein baraabari bhi hai, jo unke beech padi hai?"],["","Yeh spasht hai."],["","To ek, jo nahi hai, jaisa dikhta hai, badappan aur chhotepan aur baraabari mein hissa leta hai?"],["","Spasht roop se."]]},{"tag":"161e","title":"Jo ek nahi hai woh being mein hissa leta hai","paras":[["","Aage, use nishchit roop se kisi tarah being mein hissa lena chahiye?"],["","Kaise?"],["","Aisa hona chahiye, kyunki agar nahi, to yeh kehne mein ki ek nahi hai hum sach nahi bolenge. Par agar hum sach bolte hain, to spasht roop se hamein woh kehna chahiye jo hai. Kya main sahi nahi?"],["","Haan."],["","Aur kyunki hum daava karte hain ki hum sach bolte hain, to hamein yeh bhi daava karna chahiye ki hum woh kehte hain jo hai?"],["","Certainly."],["","To, jaisa dikhta hai, ek, jab woh nahi hai, hai; kyunki agar woh nahi hone par na hota, balki (Ya, 'not-being ke sambandh mein astitva ka kuch hissa chhod de.') being ka kuch hissa chhod deta, taaki not-being ban jaaye, to woh turant hota."],["","Bilkul true."],["","To ek jo nahi hai, agar use khud ko banaaye rakhna hai, to not-being ke bandhan ke roop mein not-being ka being rakhna chahiye, bilkul jaise being ko apna being poorn karne ke liye bandhan ke roop mein not-being ka not-being rakhna chahiye; kyunki being ke being aur not-being ke not-being ka sabse sachcha daava tab hai jab being being ke being mein hissa leta hai, aur not-being ke being mein nahi—yahi being ki poornata hai; aur jab not-being not-being ke not-being mein hissa nahi leta balki not-being ke being mein—yahi not-being ki poornata hai."],["","Bilkul true."],["","To kyunki jo hai woh not-being mein hissa leta hai, aur jo nahi hai woh being mein, to kya ek ko bhi na hone ke liye being mein hissa nahi lena chahiye?"],["","Certainly."],["","To ek, agar woh nahi hai, to spasht roop se uska being hai?"],["","Spasht roop se."],["","Aur not-being bhi hai, agar woh nahi hai?"],["","Of course."],["","Par kya koi cheez jo ek nishchit avastha mein hai bina badle us avastha mein na ho sakti hai?"],["","Asambhav."],["","To har cheez jo ek nishchit avastha mein hai aur nahi hai, parivartan ko imply karti hai?"],["","Certainly."],["","Aur parivartan gati hai—hum yeh keh sakte hain?"],["","Haan, gati."],["","Aur ek ko hona aur na hona dono siddh kiya ja chuka hai?"],["","Haan."],["","Aur isliye same avastha mein hai aur nahi hai?"],["","Haan."],["","Is tarah jo ek nahi hai uski gati bhi dikhaayi ja chuki hai, kyunki woh being se not-being mein badalta hai?"],["","Yeh true dikhta hai."],["","Par nishchit roop se agar woh jo hai unke beech kahin nahi, jaisa ki tathya hai, kyunki woh nahi hai, to woh ek jagah se doosri jagah nahi badal sakta?"],["","Asambhav."],["","To woh jagah badal kar gati nahi kar sakta?"],["","Nahi."],["","Na hi woh same sthaan par ghoom sakta hai, kyunki woh kahin same ko nahi chhoota, kyunki same hai, aur jo nahi hai use un cheezon mein nahi gina ja sakta jo hain?"],["","Nahi gina ja sakta."],["","To ek, agar woh nahi hai, us mein nahi ghoom sakta jismein woh nahi hai?"],["","Nahi."],["","Na hi ek, chaahe woh hai ya nahi hai, khud se anya mein badla ja sakta hai, kyunki agar woh badalta aur khud se alag ho jaata, to hum ab bhi ek ki baat nahi kar rahe hote, balki kisi aur cheez ki?"],["","True."],["","Par agar ek na badlaav sahta hai, na same jagah par ghoomta hai, na jagah badalta hai, to kya woh ab bhi gati mein saksham ho sakta hai?"],["","Asambhav."],["","Ab jo achal hai use nishchit roop se sthir hona chahiye, aur jo sthir hai use thehra rehna chahiye?"],["","Certainly."],["","To ek jo nahi hai, thehra rehta hai, aur gati mein bhi hai?"],["","Yeh true lagta hai."],["","Par agar woh gati mein hai to use avashya badlaav se guzarna hoga, kyunki jo kuch gati karta hai, jahan tak woh gati karta hai, woh ab same avastha mein nahi, balki doosri mein hai?"],["","Haan."],["","To ek, gati karte hue, badla jaata hai?"],["","Haan."],["","Aur, aage, agar kisi tarah gati nahi karta, to woh kisi tarah badla nahi jaayega?"],["","Nahi."],["","To, jahan tak jo ek nahi hai gati karta hai, woh badla jaata hai, par jahan tak woh gati nahi karta, woh badla nahi jaata?"],["","Sahi."],["","To jo ek nahi hai woh badla jaata hai aur nahi badla jaata?"],["","Yeh spasht hai."],["","Aur kya jo badla jaata hai use pehle se anya nahi hona chahiye, aur apni pichhli avastha khoni aur nasht hona chahiye; par jo badla nahi jaata woh na astitva mein aa sakta hai na nasht ho sakta hai?"],["","Bahut true."],["","Aur jo ek nahi hai, badla jaate hue, utpann aur nasht hota hai; aur na badla jaate hue, na utpann hota hai na nasht; aur is tarah jo ek nahi hai woh utpann aur nasht hota hai, aur na utpann hota hai na nasht?"],["","True."]]},{"tag":"163b","title":"Jo ek nahi hai, nirpeksh roop se","paras":[["","2.b. Aur ab, aao ek baar phir shuruaat par lautein, aur dekhein ki kya yeh ya koi aur parinaam nikalenge."],["","Aao waisa karein jaisa tum kehte ho."],["","Agar ek nahi hai, to hum poochhte hain ki ek ke sambandh mein kya hoga? Yahi question hai."],["","Haan."],["","Kya 'nahi hai' words us mein being ki anupasthiti ko nahi darshaate jis par hum unhe laagu karte hain?"],["","Bilkul aisa hi."],["","Aur jab hum kehte hain ki koi cheez nahi hai, to kya hamara matlab hai ki woh ek tarah se nahi hai par doosri tarah hai? ya kya hamara matlab, nirpeksh roop se, yeh hai ki jo nahi hai uski kisi prakaar ya tarah ya kism mein being mein sahbhaagita nahi?"],["","Bilkul nirpeksh roop se."],["","To, jo nahi hai woh ho nahi sakta, ya kisi tarah being mein hissa nahi le sakta?"],["","Nahi le sakta."],["","Aur kya utpatti, aur nasht hone se hamara matlab being ko dhaaran karna aur being ko khona nahi tha?"],["","Aur kuch nahi."],["","Aur kya jiski being mein koi sahbhaagita nahi, woh being ko dhaaran kar sakta ya kho sakta hai?"],["","Asambhav."],["","Ek to, kyunki woh kisi tarah nahi hai, kisi tarah being ko rakh ya kho ya dhaaran nahi kar sakta?"],["","True."],["","To jo ek nahi hai, kyunki woh kisi tarah being mein hissa nahi leta, na nasht hota hai na utpann?"],["","Nahi."],["","To woh bilkul badla nahi jaata; kyunki agar badla jaata to woh utpann aur nasht hota?"],["","True."],["","Par agar woh badla nahi jaata to woh gati nahi kar sakta?"],["","Certainly nahi."],["","Na hi hum keh sakte hain ki woh thehra hai, agar woh kahin nahi; kyunki jo thehra hai use hamesha ek hi aur same jagah mein hona chahiye?"],["","Of course."],["","To hamein kehna hoga ki jo ek nahi hai woh kabhi thehra nahi rehta aur kabhi gati nahi karta?"],["","Dono nahi."],["","Na hi koi maujood cheez hai jo usse jodi ja sake; kyunki agar hoti, to woh being mein hissa leta?"],["","Yeh spasht hai."],["","Aur isliye na chhotapan, na badappan, na baraabari, usse jodi ja sakti hai?"],["","Nahi."],["","Na hi samaanta na bhinnata, na khud ke sambandh mein na doosron ke?"],["","Spasht roop se nahi."],["","Achha, aur agar usse kuch nahi joda jaana chahiye, to kya doosri cheezein usse jodi ja sakti hain?"],["","Certainly nahi."],["","Aur isliye doosri cheezein uske sambandh mein na samaan ho sakti hain na asamaan, na same, na alag?"],["","Nahi ho sakti."],["","Na hi jo nahi hai woh kuch ho sakta hai, ya yeh cheez ho sakta hai, ya is ya us ya anya se sambandhit ya uska gun ho sakta hai, ya ateet, vartamaan, ya bhavishya ho sakta hai. Na hi knowledge, ya raay, ya perception, ya abhivyakti, ya naam, ya koi aur cheez jo hai, usse koi sambandh rakh sakti hai?"],["","Nahi."],["","To jo ek nahi hai uski kisi prakaar ki koi avastha nahi?"],["","Aisa hi nishkarsh dikhta hai."]]},{"tag":"164b","title":"Agar ek nahi hai: aabhaas ke roop mein doosre","paras":[["","2.aa. Phir bhi ek baar aur; agar ek nahi hai, to doosron ka kya hota hai? Aao yeh tay karein."],["","Haan; aao yeh tay karein."],["","Doosre nishchit roop se hone chahiye; kyunki agar woh, ek ki tarah, na hote, to hum ab unki baat nahi kar rahe hote."],["","True."],["","Par doosron ki baat karna bhinnata ko imply karta hai—'anya' aur 'bhinn' terms paryaayvaachi hain?"],["","True."],["","Anya ka matlab anya se anya hai, aur bhinn, bhinn se bhinn?"],["","Haan."],["","To, agar doosre hone hain, to kuch hai jisse woh anya honge?"],["","Certainly."],["","Aur woh kya ho sakta hai?—kyunki agar ek nahi hai, to woh ek se anya nahi honge."],["","Nahi honge."],["","To woh ek doosre se anya honge; kyunki ekmaatra bacha vikalp yeh hai ki woh kuch nahi se anya hain."],["","True."],["","Aur woh har ek ek doosre se anya hain, bahuvachan hone se aur ekvachan nahi; kyunki agar ek nahi hai, to woh ekvachan nahi ho sakte, balki unka har kan sankhya mein anant hai; aur agar koi woh le jo sabse chhota ansh dikhta hai, to yeh, jo ek dikhta tha, ek kshan mein anek mein ud jaata hai, jaise sapne mein, aur sabse chhota hone se bahut bada ho jaata hai, un anshon ki tulna mein jinmein woh toot jaata hai?"],["","Bahut true."],["","Aur aise kanon mein doosre ek doosre se anya honge, agar doosre hain, aur ek nahi hai?"],["","Bilkul."],["","Aur kya anek kan nahi honge, har ek ek dikhte hue, par ek na hote hue, agar ek nahi hai?"],["","True."],["","Aur aisa lagta hai ki unke baare mein sankhya kahi ja sakti hai agar unmein se har ek ek dikhta hai, haalaanki woh vaastav mein anek hai?"],["","Kahi ja sakti hai."],["","Aur unmein vishamm aur samm dikhenge, jinki bhi koi vaastavikta nahi hogi, agar ek nahi hai?"],["","Haan."],["","Aur unmein ek sabse chhota dikhega; aur yeh bhi un anek chhote anshon ki tulna mein bada aur bahuvidh dikhega jo usmein samaaye hain?"],["","Certainly."],["","Aur har kan ko anek aur thode ke baraabar kalpit kiya jaayega; kyunki woh bade se chhote mein jaata nahi dikh sakta tha bina madhya tak pahunchta dikhe; aur is tarah baraabari ka aabhaas paida hoga."],["","Haan."],["","Aur na aarambh, na madhya, na ant rakhte hue, har alag kan phir bhi khud ke aur doosre ke sambandh mein seema rakhta dikhta hai."],["","Kaise?"],["","Kyunki, jab koi inmein se kisi ek ki aisi kalpana karta hai, to aarambh se pehle ek aur aarambh dikhta hai, aur ant ke baad bacha ek aur ant hai, aur madhya mein andar adhik sachche par chhote madhya, kyunki unmein se kisi ki koi ekta kalpit nahi ki ja sakti, kyunki ek nahi hai."],["","Bahut true."],["","Aur is tarah saara being, jo bhi hum sochein, anshon mein toot jaana chahiye, kyunki kan ki kalpana ekta ke bina karni hogi?"],["","Certainly."],["","Aur aisa being jab dhundhla aur door se dekha jaaye, to ek dikhta hai; par jab paas se aur teekshn buddhi se dekha jaaye, to har ek cheez anant dikhti hai, kyunki woh ek se vanchit hai, jo nahi hai?"],["","Isse adhik nishchit kuch nahi."],["","To doosron mein se har ek ko anant aur seemit, aur ek aur anek dikhna chahiye, agar ek se anya doosre maujood hain aur ek nahi."],["","Dikhna chahiye."],["","To kya woh samaan aur asamaan nahi dikhenge?"],["","Kis tarah?"],["","Bilkul jaise ek chitra mein door khade vyakti ko cheezein sab ek, aur same avastha mein aur samaan dikhti hain?"],["","True."],["","Par jab tum unke paas jaate ho, to woh anek aur alag dikhti hain; aur bhinnata ke aabhaas ke kaaran, prakaar mein alag, aur khud se asamaan?"],["","True."],["","Aur isi tarah kanon ko khud ke aur ek doosre ke samaan aur asamaan dikhna chahiye."],["","Certainly."],["","Aur kya unhe same aur phir bhi ek doosre se alag, aur khud ke sampark mein, haalaanki woh alag hain, aur har prakaar ki gati, aur har prakaar ki sthirta rakhte hue, aur utpann aur nasht hote hue, aur dono avasthaaon mein se kisi mein nahi, aur aise, nahi hona chahiye, jin sab cheezon ki aasaani se ganana ki ja sakti hai, agar ek nahi hai aur anek hain?"],["","Bilkul true."]]},{"tag":"165e","title":"Agar ek nahi hai, to kuch nahi hai","paras":[["","2.bb. Ek baar phir, aao shuruaat par lautein, aur poochhein ki agar ek nahi hai, aur ek ke doosre hain, to kya nikalega."],["","Aao woh question poochhein."],["","Pehle sthaan par, doosre ek nahi honge?"],["","Asambhav."],["","Na hi woh anek honge; kyunki agar woh anek hote to unmein ek samaaya hota. Par agar unmein se koi ek ek nahi, to woh sab shoonya hain, aur isliye woh anek nahi honge."],["","True."],["","Agar doosron mein koi ek nahi, to doosre na anek hain na ek."],["","Nahi hain."],["","Na hi woh ek ya anek ke roop mein dikhte hain."],["","Kyun nahi?"],["","Kyunki doosron ka kisi prakaar ke not-being ke saath kisi prakaar ya dhang ya tarike ka sahbhaagita nahi, na hi jo nahi hai woh doosron mein se kisi se juda ho sakta hai; kyunki jo nahi hai uske hisse nahi."],["","True."],["","Na hi doosron ke sambandh mein not-being ki koi raay ya koi aabhaas hai, na not-being kabhi kisi tarah doosron se joda jaata hai."],["","Nahi."],["","To agar ek nahi hai, to doosron mein se kisi ki na ek ke roop mein na anek ke roop mein koi dhaarna hai; kyunki tum ek ke bina anek ki dhaarna nahi kar sakte."],["","Nahi kar sakte."],["","To agar ek nahi hai, to doosre na hain, na ek ya anek hone ki kalpana ki ja sakti hai?"],["","Aisa lagta hai ki nahi."],["","Na samaan ya asamaan ke roop mein?"],["","Nahi."],["","Na same ya alag ke roop mein, na sampark ya alagaav mein, na un avasthaaon mein se kisi mein jinki ganana humne dikhne ke roop mein ki;—doosre inmein se na kuch hain na kuch dikhte hain, agar ek nahi hai?"],["","True."],["","To kya hum argument ko ek word mein samet kar sach nahi keh sakte: Agar ek nahi hai, to kuch nahi hai?"],["","Certainly."],["","Itna kaha jaaye; aur aage aao woh daava karein jo sach lagta hai, ki, chaahe ek hai ya nahi hai, ek aur doosre khud ke aur ek doosre ke sambandh mein, sab ke sab, har tarah se, hain aur nahi hain, aur hone ka aabhaas dete hain aur na hone ka aabhaas dete hain."],["","Bilkul true."]]}],"hi":[{"tag":"126a","title":"प्रस्तावना: सेफ़ेलस, एंटीफ़ोन और पार्मेनाइडीज़ का आगमन","paras":[["","सेफ़ेलस एक संवाद दोहराता है जो माना जाता है कि उसकी उपस्थिति में एंटीफ़ोन ने, जो एडीमैंटस और ग्लॉकन का सौतेला भाई है, कुछ क्लाज़ोमेनी लोगों को सुनाया था।","n"],["","हम क्लाज़ोमेने में अपने घर से एथेंस आए थे, और अगोरा में एडीमैंटस और ग्लॉकन से मिले। स्वागत है, सेफ़ेलस, एडीमैंटस ने मेरा हाथ पकड़ते हुए कहा; क्या एथेंस में हम तुम्हारे लिए कुछ कर सकते हैं?"],["","हाँ; इसीलिए तो मैं यहाँ हूँ; मैं तुमसे एक उपकार माँगना चाहता हूँ।"],["","वह क्या हो सकता है? उसने कहा।"],["","मैं चाहता हूँ कि तुम मुझे अपने सौतेले भाई का नाम बताओ, जो मैं भूल गया हूँ; जब मैं पिछली बार क्लाज़ोमेने से यहाँ आया था तब वह नन्हा बच्चा था, पर वह बहुत पहले की बात है; उसके पिता का नाम, यदि मुझे सही याद है, पाइरिलैम्पीज़ था?"],["","हाँ, उसने कहा, और हमारे भाई का नाम, एंटीफ़ोन; पर तुम क्यों पूछते हो?"],["","मुझे अपने कुछ देशवासियों का परिचय कराने दो, मैंने कहा; वे दर्शन के प्रेमी हैं, और उन्होंने सुना है कि एंटीफ़ोन एक पाइथोडोरस का गहरा मित्र था, जो ज़ेनो का मित्र था, और उसे एक बातचीत याद है जो कई वर्ष पहले सुकरात, ज़ेनो, और पार्मेनाइडीज़ के बीच हुई थी, क्योंकि पाइथोडोरस ने उसे प्रायः वह सुनाई थी।"],["","बिल्कुल सत्य।"],["","और क्या हम उसे सुन सकते हैं? मैंने पूछा।"],["","इससे आसान कुछ नहीं, उसने उत्तर दिया; जब वह युवक था तो उसने इस अंश का ध्यान से अध्ययन किया था; अब उसके विचार दूसरी दिशा में चलते हैं; अपने दादा एंटीफ़ोन की तरह वह घोड़ों का दीवाना है। पर, यदि तुम यही चाहते हो, तो चलो उसे ढूँढते हैं; वह मेलिटा में रहता है, जो बिल्कुल पास है, और वह अभी-अभी हमारे पास से घर गया है।"],["","इसलिए हम उसे ढूँढने गए; वह घर पर था, और एक लोहार को लगाम ठीक करने के लिए दे रहा था। जब वह लोहार से निपट गया, तो उसके भाइयों ने उसे हमारे आने का उद्देश्य बताया; और उसने मुझे एक परिचित की तरह अभिवादन किया जिसे वह मेरी पिछली यात्रा से याद रखता था, और हमने उससे संवाद दोहराने को कहा। पहले वह बहुत इच्छुक नहीं था, और परेशानी की शिकायत की, पर अंत में मान गया। उसने हमें बताया कि पाइथोडोरस ने उसे पार्मेनाइडीज़ और ज़ेनो का रूप-रंग बताया था; वे एथेंस आए थे, जैसा उसने कहा, महान पैनाथीनिया पर; पहला, अपनी यात्रा के समय, लगभग 65 वर्ष का था, आयु से बहुत सफ़ेद, पर सुंदर। ज़ेनो लगभग 40 वर्ष का था, लंबा और देखने में सुंदर; अपनी जवानी के दिनों में कहा जाता था कि वह पार्मेनाइडीज़ का प्रिय था। उसने कहा कि वे सेरामिकस में, दीवार के बाहर, पाइथोडोरस के साथ ठहरे थे, जहाँ सुकरात, तब बहुत युवक, उनसे मिलने आया, और उसके साथ कई और भी; वे ज़ेनो की रचनाएँ सुनना चाहते थे, जो उनकी यात्रा के अवसर पर पहली बार एथेंस लाई गई थीं। इन्हें ज़ेनो ने स्वयं पार्मेनाइडीज़ की अनुपस्थिति में उन्हें पढ़कर सुनाया, और लगभग समाप्त कर चुका था जब पाइथोडोरस भीतर आया, और उसके साथ पार्मेनाइडीज़ और अरिस्टोटेलीज़ जो बाद में तीस (शासकों) में से एक बना, और जो थोड़ा बचा था वह सुना। पाइथोडोरस ने ज़ेनो को उन्हें पहले दोहराते सुना था।"]]},{"tag":"127d","title":"ज़ेनो का तर्क और सुकरात का प्रत्यय-सिद्धांत","paras":[["","जब पाठ पूरा हुआ, तो सुकरात ने अनुरोध किया कि पहले तर्क की पहली प्रतिज्ञा फिर से पढ़ी जाए, और ऐसा हो जाने पर, उसने कहा: तुम्हारा क्या अर्थ है, ज़ेनो? क्या तुम यह मानते हो कि यदि सत् अनेक है, तो उसे समान और असमान दोनों होना होगा, और कि यह असंभव है, क्योंकि न समान असमान हो सकता है, न असमान समान—क्या यही तुम्हारी स्थिति है?"],["","बिल्कुल ऐसा ही, ज़ेनो ने कहा।"],["","और यदि असमान समान नहीं हो सकता, या समान असमान, तो तुम्हारे अनुसार, सत् अनेक नहीं हो सकता; क्योंकि इसमें एक असंभवता शामिल होगी। जो कुछ तुम कहते हो क्या उसमें तुम्हारा अनेक के अस्तित्व को खंडित करने के अलावा कोई और उद्देश्य है? और क्या तुम्हारे ग्रंथ का हर विभाग इसका एक अलग प्रमाण देने के लिए नहीं, कुल मिलाकर अनेक के अनस्तित्व के उतने प्रमाण जितने तर्क तुमने रचे हैं? क्या यही तुम्हारा अर्थ है, या मैंने तुम्हें गलत समझा?"],["","नहीं, ज़ेनो ने कहा; तुमने मेरा सामान्य उद्देश्य सही समझा है।"],["","मैं देखता हूँ, पार्मेनाइडीज़, सुकरात ने कहा, कि ज़ेनो न केवल मित्रता में तुम्हारे साथ एक होना चाहता है बल्कि अपनी रचनाओं में भी तुम्हारा दूसरा रूप; वह जो तुम कहते हो उसे दूसरे ढंग से रखता है, और यह दिखावा करना चाहता है कि वह हमें कुछ नया बता रहा है। क्योंकि तुम, अपनी कविताओं में, कहते हो सब एक है, और इसके उत्कृष्ट प्रमाण देते हो; और वह दूसरी ओर कहता है अनेक नहीं है; और इसके पक्ष में भारी साक्ष्य देता है। तुम एकता को स्वीकार करते हो, वह बहुलता को नकारता है। और इस तरह तुम संसार को यह मानने का धोखा देते हो कि तुम अलग-अलग बातें कह रहे हो जबकि वास्तव में तुम लगभग समान बात कह रहे हो। यह कला का ऐसा कमाल है जो हममें से अधिकतर की पहुँच से बाहर है।"],["","हाँ, सुकरात, ज़ेनो ने कहा। पर यद्यपि तुम निशान का पीछा करने में स्पार्टा के शिकारी कुत्ते जितने तेज़ हो, तुम रचना के सच्चे उद्देश्य को पूरी तरह नहीं समझते, जो वास्तव में उतनी कृत्रिम कृति नहीं जितनी तुम कल्पना करते हो; क्योंकि जिसकी तुम बात करते हो वह संयोग था; किसी बड़े उद्देश्य का दिखावा नहीं था; न संसार को धोखा देने का कोई गंभीर इरादा। सच यह है, कि मेरी ये रचनाएँ पार्मेनाइडीज़ के तर्कों को उन लोगों से बचाने के लिए थीं जो उसका मज़ाक उड़ाते हैं और उन अनेक हास्यास्पद और विरोधी परिणामों को दिखाने का प्रयास करते हैं जो उनके अनुसार एक की स्वीकृति से निकलते हैं। मेरा उत्तर अनेक के समर्थकों को संबोधित है, जिनके हमले को मैं ब्याज सहित लौटाता हूँ, उन्हें यह पलटवार करके कि उनकी अनेक के अस्तित्व की परिकल्पना, यदि आगे बढ़ाई जाए, तो एक के अस्तित्व की परिकल्पना से भी अधिक हास्यास्पद लगती है। अपने गुरु के प्रति उत्साह ने मुझे अपनी जवानी के दिनों में यह पुस्तक लिखने को प्रेरित किया, पर किसी ने प्रति चुरा ली; और इसलिए मेरे पास कोई विकल्प नहीं था कि वह प्रकाशित हो या नहीं; लिखने का उद्देश्य, फिर भी, किसी बड़े मनुष्य की महत्वाकांक्षा नहीं, बल्कि एक युवक की लड़ाकू प्रवृत्ति थी। यह तुम देखते नहीं लगते, सुकरात; यद्यपि दूसरे मामलों में, जैसा मैं कह रहा था, तुम्हारी धारणा बहुत उचित है।"],["","मैं समझता हूँ, सुकरात ने कहा, और तुम्हारे विवरण को पूरी तरह स्वीकार करता हूँ। पर मुझे बताओ, ज़ेनो, क्या तुम आगे यह नहीं सोचते कि समानता का स्वयं में एक प्रत्यय है, और असमानता का एक और प्रत्यय, जो समानता का विपरीत है, और कि इन दो में, तुम और मैं और सब दूसरी वस्तुएँ जिन पर हम अनेक पद लागू करते हैं, भाग लेते हैं—जो वस्तुएँ समानता में भाग लेती हैं वे उस मात्रा और ढंग में समान हो जाती हैं; और जहाँ तक वे असमानता में भाग लेती हैं उस मात्रा में असमान हो जाती हैं, या समान और असमान दोनों उस मात्रा में जिसमें वे दोनों में भाग लेती हैं? और क्या सब वस्तुएँ दोनों विपरीतों में भाग लेकर, इस सहभागिता के कारण, समान और असमान दोनों नहीं हो सकतीं?—इसमें आश्चर्य क्या है? अब यदि कोई यह सिद्ध कर सके कि निरपेक्ष समान असमान हो जाता है, या निरपेक्ष असमान समान हो जाता है, तो वह, मेरी राय में, सचमुच आश्चर्य होगा; पर इसमें कुछ असाधारण नहीं, ज़ेनो, यह दिखाने में कि जो वस्तुएँ केवल समानता और असमानता में भाग लेती हैं वे दोनों का अनुभव करती हैं। न ही, फिर, यदि कोई यह दिखाए कि सब कुछ एक में भाग लेकर एक है, और साथ ही अनेक में भाग लेकर अनेक, तो क्या वह बहुत चौंकाने वाला होगा। पर यदि वह मुझे दिखाए कि निरपेक्ष एक अनेक था, या निरपेक्ष अनेक एक, तो मैं सचमुच चकित होऊँगा। और बाकी सब के साथ भी ऐसा ही: मुझे यह सुनकर आश्चर्य होगा कि स्वभावों या प्रत्ययों में स्वयं ये विपरीत गुण थे; पर तब नहीं यदि कोई मेरे बारे में सिद्ध करना चाहे कि मैं अनेक था और एक भी। जब वह दिखाना चाहेगा कि मैं अनेक था तो वह कहेगा कि मेरा दार्यीं और बायाँ भाग है, और आगे और पीछा, और ऊपरी और निचला आधा, क्योंकि मैं नकार नहीं सकता कि मैं बहुलता में भाग लेता हूँ; जब, दूसरी ओर, वह सिद्ध करना चाहता है कि मैं एक हूँ, तो वह कहेगा, कि हम जो यहाँ इकट्ठा हैं सात हैं, और कि मैं एक हूँ और एक में भाग लेता हूँ। दोनों उदाहरणों में वह अपनी बात सिद्ध करता है। इसी तरह फिर, यदि कोई यह दिखाता है कि लकड़ी, पत्थर, और ऐसी वस्तुएँ, अनेक होते हुए एक भी हैं, तो हम मानते हैं कि वह एक और अनेक का सह-अस्तित्व दिखाता है, पर वह यह नहीं दिखाता कि अनेक एक हैं या एक अनेक; वह विरोधाभास नहीं बल्कि एक साधारण सत्य बोल रहा है। पर यदि, जैसा मैंने अभी सुझाया, कोई समान, असमान, एक, अनेक, स्थिरता, गति, और ऐसे प्रत्ययों की सरल धारणाओं को अलग करे, और फिर दिखाए कि इनमें स्वयं में मिश्रण और अलगाव संभव है, तो मैं बहुत चकित होऊँगा। तर्क का यह भाग, ज़ेनो, तुमने बहुत जोश के साथ सँभाला लगता है; पर, जैसा मैं कह रहा था, मैं कहीं अधिक चकित होऊँगा यदि कोई उन प्रत्ययों में स्वयं, जो तर्क से ग्रहण किए जाते हैं, वही पहेली और उलझन पाए जो तुमने दृश्य वस्तुओं में दिखाई है।"],["","जब सुकरात बोल रहा था, पाइथोडोरस ने सोचा कि पार्मेनाइडीज़ और ज़ेनो तर्क के लगातार कदमों से पूरी तरह प्रसन्न नहीं थे; पर फिर भी उन्होंने पूरा ध्यान दिया, और प्रायः एक-दूसरे की ओर देखा, और मुस्कराए मानो उसकी प्रशंसा में। जब वह समाप्त कर चुका, तो पार्मेनाइडीज़ ने निम्नलिखित शब्दों में उनकी भावनाएँ व्यक्त कीं:—"]]},{"tag":"130a","title":"किन वस्तुओं के प्रत्यय हैं?","paras":[["","सुकरात, उसने कहा, मैं दर्शन की ओर तुम्हारे मन के झुकाव की प्रशंसा करता हूँ; अब मुझे बताओ, क्या स्वयं में प्रत्ययों और उन वस्तुओं के बीच जो उनमें भाग लेती हैं यह भेद तुम्हारा अपना था? और क्या तुम सोचते हो कि समानता का एक प्रत्यय है जो उस समानता से अलग है जो हमारे पास है, और एक और अनेक का, और उन दूसरी वस्तुओं का जिनका ज़ेनो ने उल्लेख किया?"],["","मैं सोचता हूँ कि ऐसे प्रत्यय हैं, सुकरात ने कहा।"],["","पार्मेनाइडीज़ ने आगे कहा: और क्या तुम न्यायपूर्ण और सुंदर और अच्छे के, और उस पूरे वर्ग के निरपेक्ष प्रत्यय भी बनाओगे?"],["","हाँ, उसने कहा, बनाऊँगा।"],["","और क्या तुम मनुष्य का एक प्रत्यय बनाओगे जो हमसे और सब दूसरे मानव प्राणियों से अलग हो, या अग्नि और जल का?"],["","मैं प्रायः अनिश्चित रहता हूँ, पार्मेनाइडीज़, कि मुझे उन्हें शामिल करना चाहिए या नहीं।"],["","और क्या तुम उतने ही अनिश्चित होगे, सुकरात, उन वस्तुओं के बारे में जिनका उल्लेख मुस्कान ला सकता है?—मेरा अर्थ है बाल, कीचड़, गंदगी, या कोई और वस्तु जो नीच और तुच्छ हो; क्या तुम मानोगे कि इनमें से हर एक का उन वास्तविक वस्तुओं से अलग प्रत्यय है जिनके हम संपर्क में आते हैं, या नहीं?"],["","निश्चित रूप से नहीं, सुकरात ने कहा; ऐसी दृश्य वस्तुएँ वैसी ही हैं जैसी हमें दिखती हैं, और मुझे डर है कि उनका कोई प्रत्यय मानने में बेतुकापन होगा, यद्यपि मैं कभी-कभी परेशान हो जाता हूँ, और सोचने लगता हूँ कि प्रत्यय के बिना कुछ भी नहीं; पर फिर, जब मैं यह स्थिति अपना लेता हूँ, तो भाग जाता हूँ, क्योंकि मुझे डर है कि मैं बकवास के अथाह गड्ढे में गिरकर नष्ट न हो जाऊँ; और इसलिए मैं उन प्रत्ययों पर लौट आता हूँ जिनकी मैं अभी बात कर रहा था, और उन्हीं में व्यस्त रहता हूँ।"],["","हाँ, सुकरात, पार्मेनाइडीज़ ने कहा; यह इसलिए है कि तुम अभी युवक हो; समय आएगा, यदि मैं गलत नहीं, जब दर्शन की तुम पर अधिक मज़बूत पकड़ होगी, और तब तुम सबसे तुच्छ वस्तुओं को भी तुच्छ नहीं समझोगे; तुम्हारी आयु में, तुम लोगों की रायों का बहुत अधिक लिहाज़ करने की ओर झुकते हो। पर मैं जानना चाहूँगा कि क्या तुम्हारा अर्थ है कि कुछ प्रत्यय हैं जिनमें बाकी सब वस्तुएँ भाग लेती हैं, और जिनसे उन्हें अपने नाम मिलते हैं; कि समान वस्तुएँ, उदाहरण के लिए, समान हो जाती हैं, क्योंकि वे समानता में भाग लेती हैं; और बड़ी वस्तुएँ बड़ी हो जाती हैं, क्योंकि वे बड़प्पन में भाग लेती हैं; और कि न्यायपूर्ण और सुंदर वस्तुएँ न्यायपूर्ण और सुंदर हो जाती हैं, क्योंकि वे न्याय और सौंदर्य में भाग लेती हैं?"],["","हाँ, अवश्य, सुकरात ने कहा, मेरा यही अर्थ है।"]]},{"tag":"131a","title":"सहभागिता: संपूर्ण या भाग? पाल","paras":[["","तो हर व्यक्ति या तो पूरे प्रत्यय में भाग लेता है या फिर प्रत्यय के एक भाग में? क्या सहभागिता का कोई और तरीका हो सकता है?"],["","नहीं हो सकता, उसने कहा।"],["","तो क्या तुम सोचते हो कि पूरा प्रत्यय एक है, और फिर भी, एक होते हुए, अनेक में से हर एक में है?"],["","क्यों नहीं, पार्मेनाइडीज़? सुकरात ने कहा।"],["","क्योंकि एक ही और समान वस्तु एक ही समय में अनेक अलग व्यक्तियों में संपूर्ण रूप से विद्यमान होगी, और इसलिए स्वयं से अलगाव की अवस्था में होगी।"],["","नहीं, पर प्रत्यय दिन की तरह हो सकता है जो एक साथ अनेक जगहों में एक ही और समान है, और फिर भी स्वयं से निरंतर है; इस तरह हर प्रत्यय एक ही समय में सब में एक ही और समान हो सकता है।"],["","मुझे तुम्हारा तरीका पसंद है, सुकरात, एक को एक साथ अनेक जगहों में बनाने का। तुम्हारा कहना है, कि यदि मैं एक पाल फैलाकर कई लोगों को ढक दूँ, तो एक संपूर्ण होगा जो अनेक को शामिल करेगा—क्या यही तुम्हारा अर्थ नहीं?"],["","मुझे ऐसा लगता है।"],["","और क्या तुम कहोगे कि पूरा पाल हर व्यक्ति को शामिल करता है, या केवल उसका एक भाग, और अलग-अलग भाग अलग-अलग लोगों को?"],["","बाद वाला।"],["","तो, सुकरात, प्रत्यय स्वयं विभाज्य होंगे, और जो वस्तुएँ उनमें भाग लेती हैं उनके पास उनका केवल एक भाग होगा और हर एक में पूरा प्रत्यय विद्यमान नहीं होगा?"],["","ऐसा ही निकलता लगता है।"],["","तो क्या तुम कहना चाहोगे, सुकरात, कि एक प्रत्यय वास्तव में विभाज्य है और फिर भी एक बना रहता है?"],["","निश्चित रूप से नहीं, उसने कहा।"],["","मान लो कि तुम निरपेक्ष बड़प्पन को बाँटो, और कि अनेक बड़ी वस्तुओं में से, हर एक निरपेक्ष बड़प्पन से कम बड़प्पन के एक भाग के कारण बड़ी है—क्या यह कल्पनीय है?"],["","नहीं।"],["","या क्या हर बराबर वस्तु, यदि निरपेक्ष बराबरी से कम बराबरी का कोई छोटा भाग रखती है, तो केवल उस भाग के कारण किसी दूसरी वस्तु के बराबर होगी?"],["","असंभव।"],["","या मान लो कि हममें से किसी के पास छोटेपन का एक भाग है; यह छोटे का केवल एक भाग है, और इसलिए निरपेक्ष छोटा बड़ा है; यदि निरपेक्ष छोटा बड़ा हो, तो जिस वस्तु में छोटे का भाग जोड़ा जाता है वह पहले से छोटी होगी और बड़ी नहीं।"],["","कितना बेतुका!"],["","तो किस तरह, सुकरात, सब वस्तुएँ प्रत्ययों में भाग लेंगी, यदि वे उनमें न भागों के रूप में न संपूर्णों के रूप में भाग ले सकती हैं?"],["","सचमुच, उसने कहा, तुमने ऐसा प्रश्न पूछा है जिसका आसानी से उत्तर नहीं दिया जा सकता।"],["","अच्छा, पार्मेनाइडीज़ ने कहा, और एक और प्रश्न के बारे में तुम क्या कहते हो?"],["","कौन-सा प्रश्न?"]]},{"tag":"132a","title":"'तीसरा मनुष्य': बड़प्पन की अनवस्था","paras":[["","मैं कल्पना करता हूँ कि जिस तरह तुम हर प्रकार का एक प्रत्यय मानने की ओर ले जाए जाते हो वह इस प्रकार है:—तुम कई बड़ी वस्तुएँ देखते हो, और जब तुम उन्हें देखते हो तो तुम्हें उन सब में एक ही और समान प्रत्यय (या स्वभाव) दिखता है; इसलिए तुम बड़प्पन को एक के रूप में समझते हो।"],["","बहुत सत्य, सुकरात ने कहा।"],["","और यदि तुम आगे बढ़ो और अपने मन को इसी तरह बड़प्पन के प्रत्यय और उन बड़ी वस्तुओं को जो प्रत्यय नहीं हैं एक दृष्टि में समेट लेने दो, और उनकी तुलना करो, तो क्या एक और बड़प्पन उत्पन्न नहीं होगा, जो इन सब का स्रोत दिखेगा?"],["","ऐसा लगता है।"],["","तो अब निरपेक्ष बड़प्पन, और उसमें भाग लेने वाले व्यक्तियों के ऊपर एक और बड़प्पन का प्रत्यय दिखाई देता है; और फिर एक और, इन सब के ऊपर, जिसके कारण वे सब बड़े होंगे, और इस तरह हर प्रत्यय एक होने के बजाय अनंत गुना हो जाएगा।"]]},{"tag":"132b","title":"विचार के रूप में प्रत्यय","paras":[["","पर क्या प्रत्यय, सुकरात ने पूछा, केवल विचार नहीं हो सकते, और हमारे मनों के अलावा उनका कोई उचित अस्तित्व न हो, पार्मेनाइडीज़? क्योंकि उस स्थिति में हर प्रत्यय फिर भी एक रह सकता है, और इस अनंत गुना-वृद्धि का अनुभव नहीं करेगा।"],["","और क्या ऐसे व्यक्तिगत विचार हो सकते हैं जो किसी वस्तु के विचार न हों?"],["","असंभव, उसने कहा।"],["","विचार किसी वस्तु का होना चाहिए?"],["","हाँ।"],["","किसी ऐसी वस्तु का जो है या जो नहीं है?"],["","किसी ऐसी वस्तु का जो है।"],["","क्या वह किसी एक वस्तु का नहीं होना चाहिए, जिसे विचार सब से जुड़ा हुआ पहचानता है, एक अकेला रूप या स्वभाव होते हुए?"],["","हाँ।"],["","और क्या वह वस्तु जो सब में एक ही और समान के रूप में ग्रहण की जाती है, प्रत्यय नहीं होगी?"],["","उससे भी, फिर, बचने का कोई रास्ता नहीं।"],["","तो, पार्मेनाइडीज़ ने कहा, यदि तुम कहते हो कि बाकी सब वस्तुएँ प्रत्ययों में भाग लेती हैं, तो क्या तुम्हें यह नहीं कहना पड़ेगा कि या तो हर वस्तु विचारों से बनी है, और सब वस्तुएँ सोचती हैं; या कि वे विचार हैं पर उनमें कोई विचार नहीं?"]]},{"tag":"132d","title":"आदर्श के रूप में प्रत्यय: सादृश्य की अनवस्था","paras":[["","बाद वाला मत, पार्मेनाइडीज़, पिछले वाले से अधिक तर्कसंगत नहीं। मेरी राय में, प्रत्यय, मानो, प्रकृति में स्थिर आदर्श (प्रतिमान) हैं, और दूसरी वस्तुएँ उनके जैसी हैं, और उनकी प्रतिच्छायाएँ हैं—दूसरी वस्तुओं की प्रत्ययों में सहभागिता का जो अर्थ है, वह वास्तव में उनके साथ सादृश्य है।"],["","पर यदि, उसने कहा, व्यक्ति प्रत्यय जैसा है, तो क्या प्रत्यय भी व्यक्ति जैसा नहीं होना चाहिए, जहाँ तक व्यक्ति प्रत्यय की प्रतिच्छाया है? जो समान है, उसकी कल्पना समान के समान के अलावा कुछ और नहीं की जा सकती।"],["","असंभव।"],["","और जब दो वस्तुएँ समान हैं, तो क्या उन्हें समान प्रत्यय में भाग नहीं लेना चाहिए?"],["","लेना चाहिए।"],["","और जिसमें दोनों भाग लेती हैं, और जो उन्हें समान बनाता है, क्या वह स्वयं प्रत्यय नहीं होगा?"],["","अवश्य।"],["","तो प्रत्यय व्यक्ति जैसा नहीं हो सकता, या व्यक्ति प्रत्यय जैसा; क्योंकि यदि वे समान हैं, तो समानता का कोई और प्रत्यय सदा सामने आता रहेगा, और यदि वह किसी और वस्तु जैसा हो, तो एक और; और नए प्रत्यय सदा उत्पन्न होते रहेंगे, यदि प्रत्यय उस वस्तु से मेल खाता है जो उसमें भाग लेती है?"],["","बिल्कुल सत्य।"],["","तो यह सिद्धांत, कि दूसरी वस्तुएँ सादृश्य से प्रत्ययों में भाग लेती हैं, छोड़ना होगा, और सहभागिता का कोई और तरीका खोजना होगा?"],["","ऐसा लगता है।"],["","तो क्या तुम देखते हो, सुकरात, कि प्रत्ययों को निरपेक्ष कहने में कितनी बड़ी कठिनाई है?"],["","हाँ, सचमुच।"],["","और, आगे, मुझे कहने दो कि अभी तक तुम उस कठिनाई का केवल एक छोटा भाग समझते हो जो शामिल है यदि तुम हर वस्तु का एक अकेला प्रत्यय बनाओ, उसे दूसरी वस्तुओं से अलग करते हुए।"],["","कौन-सी कठिनाई? उसने कहा।"]]},{"tag":"133b","title":"सबसे बड़ी कठिनाई: प्रत्यय अज्ञात","paras":[["","कई हैं, पर सबसे बड़ी यह है:—यदि कोई विरोधी तर्क करे कि ये प्रत्यय, वैसे होते हुए जैसा हम कहते हैं कि उन्हें होना चाहिए, अज्ञात ही रहेंगे, तो कोई उसे गलत सिद्ध नहीं कर सकता, जब तक कि उनके अस्तित्व को नकारने वाला बहुत योग्यता और ज्ञान वाला मनुष्य न हो, और एक लंबे और परिश्रमी प्रदर्शन का अनुसरण करने को तैयार न हो; वह असंतुष्ट रहेगा, और फिर भी ज़िद करेगा कि उन्हें जाना नहीं जा सकता।"],["","तुम्हारा क्या अर्थ है, पार्मेनाइडीज़? सुकरात ने कहा।"],["","पहले स्थान पर, मुझे लगता है, सुकरात, कि तुम, या कोई भी जो निरपेक्ष सारों का अस्तित्व मानता है, स्वीकार करेगा कि वे हमारे भीतर विद्यमान नहीं हो सकते।"],["","नहीं, सुकरात ने कहा; क्योंकि तब वे निरपेक्ष नहीं रहेंगे।"],["","सत्य, उसने कहा; और इसलिए जब प्रत्यय जो हैं वह एक-दूसरे के संबंध में हैं, तो उनका सार उनके आपसी संबंध से तय होता है, और उसका उन प्रतिच्छायाओं से, या उन्हें जो भी कहा जाए, कोई लेना-देना नहीं जो हमारे क्षेत्र में हैं, और जिनसे हम जब उनमें भाग लेते हैं तो यह या वह नाम पाते हैं। और जो वस्तुएँ हमारे क्षेत्र में हैं और उनके समान नाम रखती हैं, वे भी केवल एक-दूसरे के सापेक्ष हैं, और उन प्रत्ययों के नहीं जिनके समान नाम हैं, बल्कि अपनी हैं और उनकी नहीं।"],["","तुम्हारा क्या अर्थ है? सुकरात ने कहा।"],["","मैं अपना अर्थ इस तरह समझा सकता हूँ, पार्मेनाइडीज़ ने कहा:—एक स्वामी का एक दास है; अब उनके बीच के संबंध में कुछ निरपेक्ष नहीं, जो बस एक मनुष्य का दूसरे से संबंध है। पर अमूर्त में स्वामित्व का एक प्रत्यय भी है, जो अमूर्त में दासता के प्रत्यय के सापेक्ष है। इन स्वभावों का हमसे कोई लेना-देना नहीं, न हमारा उनसे; वे केवल अपने आप से संबंधित हैं, और हम अपने आप से। क्या तुम मेरा अर्थ देखते हो?"],["","हाँ, सुकरात ने कहा, मैं तुम्हारा अर्थ पूरी तरह देखता हूँ।"],["","और क्या ज्ञान—मेरा अर्थ निरपेक्ष ज्ञान—निरपेक्ष सत्य के अनुरूप नहीं होगा?"],["","अवश्य।"],["","और निरपेक्ष ज्ञान का हर प्रकार निरपेक्ष सत् के हर प्रकार के अनुरूप होगा?"],["","हाँ।"],["","पर जो ज्ञान हमारे पास है, वह उस सत्य के अनुरूप होगा जो हमारे पास है; और फिर, हमारे ज्ञान का हर प्रकार, हमारे सत् के हर प्रकार का ज्ञान होगा?"],["","अवश्य।"],["","पर प्रत्यय स्वयं, जैसा तुम मानते हो, हमारे पास नहीं, और नहीं हो सकते?"],["","नहीं, नहीं हो सकते।"],["","और निरपेक्ष स्वभाव या जातियाँ अलग-अलग ज्ञान के निरपेक्ष प्रत्यय द्वारा जानी जाती हैं?"],["","हाँ।"],["","और हमारे पास ज्ञान का प्रत्यय नहीं है?"],["","नहीं।"],["","तो कोई भी प्रत्यय हमें ज्ञात नहीं, क्योंकि निरपेक्ष ज्ञान में हमारा कोई भाग नहीं?"],["","मुझे लगता है नहीं।"],["","तो स्वयं में सुंदर का, और स्वयं में अच्छे का स्वभाव, और बाकी सब प्रत्यय जिन्हें हम निरपेक्ष रूप से विद्यमान मानते हैं, हमें अज्ञात हैं?"],["","ऐसा लगता है।"],["","मुझे लगता है कि एक और भी अजीब परिणाम है।"],["","वह क्या है?"],["","क्या तुम कहोगे, या नहीं कहोगे, कि निरपेक्ष ज्ञान, यदि ऐसी कोई वस्तु है, हमारे ज्ञान से कहीं अधिक सटीक ज्ञान होना चाहिए; और सौंदर्य और बाकी के बारे में भी यही?"],["","हाँ।"],["","और यदि निरपेक्ष ज्ञान में सहभागिता जैसी कोई वस्तु हो, तो ईश्वर से अधिक किसी के पास यह सबसे सटीक ज्ञान होने की संभावना नहीं?"],["","अवश्य।"],["","पर फिर, क्या ईश्वर, निरपेक्ष ज्ञान रखते हुए, मानवीय वस्तुओं का ज्ञान रखेगा?"],["","क्यों नहीं?"],["","क्योंकि, सुकरात, पार्मेनाइडीज़ ने कहा, हमने मान लिया है कि प्रत्यय मानवीय वस्तुओं के संबंध में मान्य नहीं; न मानवीय वस्तुएँ उनके संबंध में; दोनों के संबंध अपने-अपने क्षेत्रों तक सीमित हैं।"],["","हाँ, यह माना जा चुका है।"],["","और यदि ईश्वर के पास यह पूर्ण अधिकार, और पूर्ण ज्ञान है, तो उसका अधिकार हम पर शासन नहीं कर सकता, न उसका ज्ञान हमें, या किसी मानवीय वस्तु को जान सकता है; जैसे हमारा अधिकार देवताओं तक नहीं पहुँचता, न हमारा ज्ञान कुछ दिव्य जानता है, वैसे ही उसी तर्क से वे, देवता होते हुए, हमारे स्वामी नहीं, न ही वे मनुष्यों की वस्तुएँ जानते हैं।"],["","फिर भी, निश्चित रूप से, सुकरात ने कहा, ईश्वर को ज्ञान से वंचित करना भयानक है।"],["","ये, सुकरात, पार्मेनाइडीज़ ने कहा, उन कठिनाइयों में से कुछ हैं, और केवल कुछ, जिनमें हम उलझ जाते हैं यदि प्रत्यय वास्तव में हैं और हम उनमें से हर एक को निरपेक्ष एकता तय करते हैं। जो उनके विरुद्ध कही जा सकने वाली बातें सुनता है वह उनके अस्तित्व को ही नकार देगा—और यदि वे विद्यमान भी हों, तो वह कहेगा कि वे अवश्य मनुष्य के लिए अज्ञात होंगे; और तर्क उसके पक्ष में लगेगा, और जैसा हम अभी कह रहे थे, उसे मनाना बहुत कठिन होगा; मनुष्य को काफ़ी बड़ी योग्यता से संपन्न होना चाहिए तब वह सीख सकता है कि हर वस्तु का एक वर्ग और एक निरपेक्ष सार है; और वह और भी उल्लेखनीय होगा जो ये सब वस्तुएँ स्वयं खोजे, और उनकी पूरी जाँच करके उन्हें दूसरों को सिखा सके।"],["","मैं तुमसे सहमत हूँ, पार्मेनाइडीज़, सुकरात ने कहा; और जो तुम कहते हो वह मेरे मन के बहुत अनुकूल है।"],["","और फिर भी, सुकरात, पार्मेनाइडीज़ ने कहा, यदि कोई मनुष्य, इन और ऐसी कठिनाइयों पर ध्यान टिकाकर, वस्तुओं के प्रत्ययों को समाप्त कर दे और यह न माने कि हर व्यक्तिगत वस्तु का अपना निश्चित प्रत्यय है जो सदा एक ही और समान है, तो उसके पास कुछ नहीं होगा जिस पर उसका मन टिक सके; और इस तरह वह तर्क करने की शक्ति को पूरी तरह नष्ट कर देगा, जैसा तुमने, मुझे लगता है, विशेष रूप से ध्यान दिया है।"],["","बहुत सत्य, उसने कहा।"],["","पर, फिर, दर्शन का क्या होगा? हम कहाँ मुड़ें, यदि प्रत्यय अज्ञात हैं?"],["","अभी तो मुझे निश्चित रूप से अपना रास्ता नहीं दिखता।"]]},{"tag":"135c","title":"द्ंद्रवात्सक प्रशिक्षण की आवश्यकता","paras":[["","हाँ, पार्मेनाइडीज़ ने कहा; और मुझे लगता है कि यह, सुकरात, इसलिए होता है कि तुम पर्याप्त पूर्व प्रशिक्षण के बिना सुंदर, न्यायपूर्ण, अच्छे, और सामान्य रूप से प्रत्ययों को परिभाषित करने का प्रयास करते हो। मैंने तुम्हारी कमी देखी थी, जब मैंने तुम्हें परसों यहाँ अपने मित्र अरिस्टोटेलीज़ के साथ बात करते सुना। जो प्रेरणा तुम्हें दर्शन की ओर ले जाती है वह निश्चित रूप से श्रेष्ठ और दिव्य है; पर एक कला है जिसे आम लोग बेकार की बातचीत कहते हैं, और जिसे प्रायः व्यर्थ समझा जाता है; उसमें तुम्हें स्वयं को प्रशिक्षित और अभ्यस्त करना चाहिए, अब जब तुम युवक हो, वरना सत्य तुम्हारी पकड़ से फिसल जाएगा।"],["","और इस अभ्यास का स्वभाव क्या है, पार्मेनाइडीज़, जिसकी तुम सिफ़ारिश करोगे?"],["","वह जो तुमने ज़ेनो को करते सुना; साथ ही, मैं तुम्हें इस बात का श्रेय देता हूँ कि तुमने उससे कहा कि तुम दृश्य वस्तुओं के संदर्भ में उलझन की जाँच करना, या प्रश्न को उस तरह देखना पसंद नहीं करते; बल्कि केवल विचार के विषयों के संदर्भ में, और जिन्हें प्रत्यय कहा जा सकता है।"],["","क्यों, हाँ, उसने कहा, मुझे इस पद्धति से यह दिखाने में कोई कठिनाई नहीं लगती कि दृश्य वस्तुएँ समान और असमान हैं और कुछ भी अनुभव कर सकती हैं।"],["","बिल्कुल सत्य, पार्मेनाइडीज़ ने कहा; पर मुझे लगता है कि तुम्हें एक कदम आगे जाना चाहिए, और न केवल उन परिणामों पर विचार करना चाहिए जो किसी दी गई परिकल्पना से निकलते हैं, बल्कि उन परिणामों पर भी जो परिकल्पना को नकारने से निकलते हैं; और वह तुम्हारे लिए और भी बेहतर प्रशिक्षण होगा।"],["","तुम्हारा क्या अर्थ है? उसने कहा।"],["","मेरा अर्थ है, उदाहरण के लिए, कि अनेक के बारे में ज़ेनो की इसी परिकल्पना के मामले में, तुम्हें न केवल यह जाँचना चाहिए कि अनेक के अस्तित्व की परिकल्पना पर, अनेक के लिए अपने और एक के संबंध में, और एक के लिए अपने और अनेक के संबंध में क्या परिणाम होंगे, बल्कि यह भी कि विपरीत परिकल्पना पर, एक और अनेक के लिए अपने और एक-दूसरे के संबंध में क्या परिणाम होंगे। या, फिर, यदि समानता है या नहीं है, तो इन दोनों मामलों में परिकल्पना के विषयों के लिए, और दूसरी वस्तुओं के लिए, अपने और एक-दूसरे दोनों के संबंध में क्या परिणाम होंगे, और इसी तरह असमानता के; और यही गति और स्थिरता, उत्पत्ति और विनाश, और सत् और असत् पर भी लागू होता है। एक शब्द में, जब तुम किसी वस्तु को होना या न होना, या किसी भी तरह प्रभावित होना मानो, तो तुम्हें स्वयं उस वस्तु के संबंध में, और किसी भी दूसरी वस्तु के संबंध में जिसे तुम चुनो, परिणामों को देखना चाहिए,—उनमें से हर एक को अकेले, एक से अधिक को, और सब को; और इसी तरह दूसरी वस्तुओं को, तुम्हें उन्हें अपने आप के और किसी भी और वस्तु के संबंध में देखना चाहिए जिसे तुम होना या न होना मानो, यदि तुम स्वयं को पूरी तरह प्रशिक्षित करना और वास्तविक सत्य देखना चाहते हो।"],["","वह, पार्मेनाइडीज़, एक विशाल काम है जिसकी तुम बात करते हो, और मैं तुम्हें पूरी तरह नहीं समझता; क्या तुम कोई परिकल्पना लेकर कदमों से गुज़रोगे?—तब मैं तुम्हें बेहतर समझूँगा।"],["","वह, सुकरात, मेरी आयु के मनुष्य पर डालने के लिए एक गंभीर काम है।"],["","तो क्या तुम करोगे, ज़ेनो? सुकरात ने कहा।"],["","ज़ेनो ने मुस्कराकर उत्तर दिया:—आओ स्वयं पार्मेनाइडीज़ से अपनी प्रार्थना करें, जो यह कहने में बिल्कुल सही है कि तुम उस काम की विशालता से शायद ही परिचित हो जो तुम उस पर डाल रहे हो; और यदि हम और लोग होते तो मैं उससे न कहता, क्योंकि ये ऐसे विषय नहीं जिनके बारे में कोई, ख़ासकर उसकी आयु में, बड़ी सभा के सामने अच्छी तरह बोल सके; अधिकतर लोग यह नहीं जानते कि सब वस्तुओं से होकर यह घुमावदार यात्रा ही वह एकमात्र तरीका है जिससे मन सत्य और प्रज्ञा प्राप्त कर सकता है। और इसलिए, पार्मेनाइडीज़, मैं सुकरात के अनुरोध में शामिल होता हूँ, ताकि मैं वह प्रक्रिया फिर से सुन सकूँ जो मैंने बहुत समय से नहीं सुनी।"]]},{"tag":"136e","title":"पार्मेनाइडीज़ मान जाता है; अरिस्टोटेलीज़ उत्तर देगा","paras":[["","जब ज़ेनो ने ऐसा कहा, तो पाइथोडोरस ने, एंटीफ़ोन के बताए अनुसार, कहा, कि उसने स्वयं और अरिस्टोटेलीज़ और पूरी मंडली ने पार्मेनाइडीज़ से प्रक्रिया का उदाहरण देने की विनती की। मैं मना नहीं कर सकता, पार्मेनाइडीज़ ने कहा; और फिर भी मैं कुछ इबाइकस जैसा महसूस करता हूँ, जिसने, जब बुढ़ापे में, अपनी इच्छा के विरुद्ध, उसे प्रेम हुआ, तो अपनी तुलना एक बूढ़े दौड़ के घोड़े से की, जो रथ-दौड़ में दौड़ने वाला था, उस मार्ग के डर से काँपता हुआ जिसे वह इतनी अच्छी तरह जानता था—यह उसकी अपनी उपमा थी। और मुझे भी कँपकँपी महसूस होती है जब मैं याद करता हूँ कि अपनी आयु के इस पड़ाव पर मुझे शब्दों के कैसे सागर से गुज़रना है। पर मुझे तुम्हारी बात माननी होगी, क्योंकि ज़ेनो कहता है कि माननी चाहिए, और हम अकेले हैं। मैं कहाँ से आरंभ करूँ? और हमारी पहली परिकल्पना क्या हो, यदि मुझे यह परिश्रमी मनोरंजन करना है? क्या मैं अपने से आरंभ करूँ, और अपनी परिकल्पना एक को लूँ? और उन परिणामों पर विचार करूँ जो एक के अस्तित्व या अनस्तित्व की मान्यता पर निकलते हैं?"],["","अवश्य, ज़ेनो ने कहा।"],["","और मुझे उत्तर कौन देगा? उसने कहा। क्या मैं सबसे युवक का प्रस्ताव करूँ? वह कठिनाइयाँ नहीं खड़ी करेगा और जो सोचता है वह कहने की सबसे अधिक संभावना है; और उसके उत्तर मुझे साँस लेने का समय देंगे।"],["","मैं ही वह हूँ जिसका तुम अर्थ रखते हो, पार्मेनाइडीज़, अरिस्टोटेलीज़ ने कहा; क्योंकि मैं सबसे युवक हूँ और तुम्हारी सेवा में हूँ। पूछो, और मैं उत्तर दूँगा।"]]},{"tag":"137c","title":"पहला निगमन: यदि एक है, तो अनेक नहीं","paras":[["","पार्मेनाइडीज़ ने आगे कहा: 1.a. यदि एक है, उसने कहा, तो एक अनेक नहीं हो सकता?"],["","असंभव।"],["","तो एक के भाग नहीं हो सकते, और वह संपूर्ण नहीं हो सकता?"],["","क्यों नहीं?"],["","क्योंकि हर भाग एक संपूर्ण का भाग है; है न?"],["","हाँ।"],["","और संपूर्ण क्या है? क्या वह जिसका कोई भाग कम न हो संपूर्ण नहीं होगा?"],["","अवश्य।"],["","तो, दोनों मामलों में, एक भागों से बना होगा; संपूर्ण होने के रूप में भी, और भाग रखने के रूप में भी?"],["","अवश्य।"],["","और दोनों मामलों में, एक अनेक होगा, और एक नहीं?"],["","सत्य।"],["","पर, निश्चित रूप से, उसे एक होना चाहिए और अनेक नहीं?"],["","होना चाहिए।"],["","तो, यदि एक को एक बने रहना है, तो वह संपूर्ण नहीं होगा, और उसके भाग नहीं होंगे?"],["","नहीं।"],["","पर यदि उसके भाग नहीं, तो उसका न आरंभ होगा, न मध्य, न अंत; क्योंकि ये निस्संदेह उसके भाग होंगे।"],["","सही।"],["","पर फिर, आरंभ और अंत हर वस्तु की सीमाएँ हैं?"],["","अवश्य।"],["","तो एक, जिसका न आरंभ है न अंत, असीमित है?"],["","हाँ, असीमित।"],["","और इसलिए निराकार; क्योंकि वह न गोल में भाग ले सकता है न सीधे में।"],["","पर क्यों?"],["","क्यों, क्योंकि गोल वह है जिसके सब अंतिम बिंदु केंद्र से समान दूरी पर हैं?"],["","हाँ।"],["","और सीधा वह है जिसका केंद्र सिरों के दृश्य को रोकता है?"],["","सत्य।"],["","तो एक के भाग होंगे और वह अनेक होगा, यदि वह सीधे या गोल रूप में भाग ले?"],["","निश्चित रूप से।"],["","पर भाग न होने से, वह न सीधा होगा न गोल?"],["","सही।"],["","और, ऐसे स्वभाव का होने से, वह किसी स्थान में नहीं हो सकता, क्योंकि वह न किसी दूसरे में हो सकता है न स्वयं में।"],["","कैसे?"],["","क्योंकि यदि वह किसी दूसरे में होता, तो जिसमें वह था उससे घिरा होता, और उसे कई जगहों पर और कई भागों से छूता; पर जो एक और अविभाज्य है, और गोल स्वभाव में भाग नहीं लेता, उसे चारों ओर कई जगहों पर छुआ नहीं जा सकता।"],["","निश्चित रूप से नहीं।"],["","पर यदि, दूसरी ओर, एक स्वयं में होता, तो वह भी स्वयं के अलावा किसी और से समाया नहीं होता; अर्थात्, यदि वह वास्तव में स्वयं में होता; क्योंकि कोई वस्तु किसी ऐसी वस्तु में नहीं हो सकती जो उसे समाए न।"],["","असंभव।"],["","पर फिर, जो समाता है उसे उससे भिन्न होना चाहिए जो समाया हुआ है? क्योंकि समान संपूर्ण एक साथ कर्ता और भोक्ता दोनों नहीं हो सकता; और यदि ऐसा है, तो एक एक नहीं रहेगा, बल्कि दो?"],["","सत्य।"],["","तो एक कहीं नहीं हो सकता, न स्वयं में न किसी दूसरे में?"],["","नहीं।"]]},{"tag":"138b","title":"न गति में न स्थिर","paras":[["","आगे विचार करो, कि क्या ऐसे स्वभाव वाली वस्तु में स्थिरता या गति हो सकती है।"],["","क्यों नहीं?"],["","क्यों, क्योंकि एक, यदि गति करता, तो या तो स्थान में गति करता या स्वभाव में बदलता; क्योंकि गति के बस यही प्रकार हैं।"],["","हाँ।"],["","और एक, जब बदलता है और स्वयं नहीं रहता, तो एक नहीं रह सकता।"],["","नहीं रह सकता।"],["","तो वह उस प्रकार की गति का अनुभव नहीं कर सकता जो स्वभाव का बदलाव है?"],["","स्पष्ट रूप से नहीं।"],["","तो क्या एक की गति स्थान में हो सकती है?"],["","शायद।"],["","पर यदि एक स्थान में गति करे, तो क्या उसे या तो समान जगह में गोल-गोल घूमना होगा, या एक जगह से दूसरी जगह?"],["","होना होगा।"],["","और जो वृत्त में घूमता है उसे एक केंद्र पर टिकना होगा; और जो केंद्र पर घूमता है उसके ऐसे भाग होने चाहिए जो केंद्र से भिन्न हों; पर जिसका न केंद्र है न भाग उसे केंद्र पर घुमाया नहीं जा सकता?"],["","असंभव।"],["","पर शायद एक की गति स्थान-परिवर्तन में है?"],["","शायद ऐसा, यदि वह गति करता ही है।"],["","और क्या हम पहले ही नहीं दिखा चुके कि वह किसी वस्तु में नहीं हो सकता?"],["","हाँ।"],["","तो उसका किसी वस्तु में अस्तित्व में आना और भी असंभव है; है न?"],["","मैं नहीं देखता क्यों।"],["","क्यों, क्योंकि जो कुछ किसी वस्तु में अस्तित्व में आता है, वह अस्तित्व में आते हुए अभी उस दूसरी वस्तु में नहीं हो सकता, न पूरी तरह उससे बाहर, यदि पहले से उसमें अस्तित्व में आ रहा है।"],["","निश्चित रूप से नहीं।"],["","और इसलिए जो कुछ दूसरे में अस्तित्व में आता है उसके भाग होने चाहिए, और तब एक भाग उस दूसरे के भीतर हो सकता है, और दूसरा बाहर; पर जिसके भाग नहीं वह कभी एक ही समय में किसी वस्तु के न पूरी तरह भीतर हो सकता है न पूरी तरह बाहर।"],["","सत्य।"],["","और क्या उस वस्तु में जिसके भाग नहीं, और जो संपूर्ण नहीं, कहीं भी अस्तित्व में आने की और भी बड़ी असंभवता नहीं, क्योंकि वह न भाग के रूप में न संपूर्ण के रूप में अस्तित्व में आ सकती है?"],["","स्पष्ट रूप से।"],["","तो वह न समान जगह पर घूमकर स्थान बदलता है, न कहीं जाकर और किसी वस्तु में अस्तित्व में आकर; न फिर, स्वयं में बदलाव से?"],["","बहुत सत्य।"],["","तो किसी भी प्रकार की गति के संदर्भ में एक अचल है?"],["","अचल।"],["","पर न ही एक किसी वस्तु में हो सकता है, जैसा हम कहते हैं?"],["","हाँ, हमने ऐसा कहा था।"],["","तो वह कभी समान में नहीं?"],["","क्यों नहीं?"],["","क्योंकि यदि वह समान में होता तो वह किसी वस्तु में होता।"],["","अवश्य।"],["","और हमने कहा था कि वह न स्वयं में हो सकता है, न दूसरे में?"],["","सत्य।"],["","तो एक कभी समान जगह में नहीं?"],["","ऐसा लगता है कि नहीं।"],["","पर जो कभी समान जगह में नहीं वह कभी शांत या स्थिर नहीं?"],["","कभी नहीं।"],["","तो एक, जैसा लगता है, न स्थिर है न गति में?"],["","निश्चित रूप से ऐसा दिखता है।"]]},{"tag":"139b","title":"न समान न अन्य, न सदृश न असदूश","paras":[["","न ही वह स्वयं के या दूसरे के समान होगा; न फिर, स्वयं से या दूसरे से अन्य।"],["","वह कैसे?"],["","यदि स्वयं से अन्य हो तो वह एक से अन्य होगा, और एक नहीं होगा।"],["","सत्य।"],["","और यदि दूसरे के समान हो, तो वह वह दूसरा होगा, और स्वयं नहीं; तो इस मान्यता पर भी, उसका स्वभाव एक का नहीं होगा, बल्कि वह एक से अन्य होगा?"],["","होगा।"],["","तो वह न दूसरे के समान होगा, न स्वयं से अन्य?"],["","नहीं होगा।"],["","न ही वह दूसरे से अन्य होगा, जब तक वह एक बना रहता है; क्योंकि एक नहीं, बल्कि केवल अन्य ही, अन्य से अन्य हो सकता है, और कुछ नहीं।"],["","सत्य।"],["","तो एक होने के कारण वह अन्य नहीं होगा?"],["","निश्चित रूप से नहीं।"],["","पर यदि एक होने के कारण नहीं, तो स्वयं के कारण नहीं; और यदि स्वयं के कारण नहीं, तो स्वयं नहीं, और स्वयं बिल्कुल अन्य न होते हुए, किसी वस्तु से अन्य नहीं होगा?"],["","सही।"],["","न ही एक स्वयं के समान होगा।"],["","कैसे नहीं?"],["","निश्चित रूप से एक का स्वभाव समान का स्वभाव नहीं।"],["","क्यों नहीं?"],["","ऐसा नहीं कि जब कोई वस्तु किसी वस्तु के समान हो जाती है तो वह एक हो जाती है।"],["","तो क्या?"],["","जो कुछ अनेक के समान हो जाता है, वह अवश्य अनेक हो जाता है और एक नहीं।"],["","सत्य।"],["","पर, यदि एक और समान में कोई अंतर न होता, तो जब कोई वस्तु समान होती, वह सदा एक हो जाती; और जब एक होती, तो समान?"],["","अवश्य।"],["","और, इसलिए, यदि एक स्वयं के समान हो, तो वह स्वयं के साथ एक नहीं, और इसलिए एक भी होगा और एक नहीं भी।"],["","निश्चित रूप से यह असंभव है।"],["","और इसलिए एक न अन्य से अन्य हो सकता है, न स्वयं के समान।"],["","असंभव।"],["","और इस तरह एक न समान हो सकता है, न अन्य, न स्वयं के संबंध में न दूसरे के?"],["","नहीं।"],["","न ही एक किसी वस्तु के सदृश होगा या स्वयं या दूसरे से असदूश।"],["","क्यों नहीं?"],["","क्योंकि सादृश्य गुणों की एकरूपता है।"],["","हाँ।"],["","और एकरूपता एकता से भिन्न स्वभाव की दिखाई जा चुकी है?"],["","वह दिखाया जा चुका है।"],["","पर यदि एक में एक होने के अलावा कोई और गुण होता, तो वह इस तरह प्रभावित होता कि एक से अधिक हो जाता; जो असंभव है।"],["","सत्य।"],["","तो एक कभी इस तरह प्रभावित नहीं हो सकता कि दूसरे के या स्वयं के समान हो?"],["","स्पष्ट रूप से नहीं।"],["","तो वह दूसरे के सदृश, या स्वयं के सदृश नहीं हो सकता?"],["","नहीं।"],["","न ही वह इस तरह प्रभावित हो सकता है कि अन्य हो, क्योंकि तब वह इस तरह प्रभावित होगा कि एक से अधिक हो।"],["","होगा।"],["","जो स्वयं से या दूसरे से भिन्न ढंग से प्रभावित होता है, वह स्वयं से या दूसरे से असदूश होगा, क्योंकि गुणों की एकरूपता सादृश्य है।"],["","सत्य।"],["","पर एक, जैसा दिखता है, कभी भिन्न ढंग से प्रभावित न होने से, कभी स्वयं से या दूसरे से असदूश नहीं?"],["","कभी नहीं।"],["","तो एक कभी न स्वयं के या दूसरे के सदृश होगा न असदूश?"],["","स्पष्ट रूप से नहीं।"]]},{"tag":"140b","title":"न बराबर न असमान, न बड़ा न छोटा","paras":[["","फिर, इस स्वभाव का होने से, वह न स्वयं के न दूसरे के बराबर हो सकता है न असमान।"],["","वह कैसे?"],["","क्यों, क्योंकि एक यदि बराबर हो तो उसे उन्हीं मापों का होना चाहिए जिनका वह है जिसके वह बराबर है।"],["","सत्य।"],["","और यदि उन वस्तुओं से बड़ा या छोटा हो जो उसके साथ सममेय हैं, तो एक के पास छोटी वस्तु से अधिक माप होंगे, और बड़ी से कम?"],["","हाँ।"],["","और इसी तरह उन वस्तुओं के साथ जो उसके साथ सममेय नहीं, एक के पास छोटी वस्तु से बड़े माप होंगे और बड़ी से छोटे।"],["","अवश्य।"],["","पर जो एकरूपता में भाग नहीं लेता, उसके समान माप या कोई और वस्तु समान कैसे हो सकती है?"],["","असंभव।"],["","और समान माप न होने से, एक न स्वयं के बराबर हो सकता है न दूसरे के?"],["","ऐसा दिखता है।"],["","पर फिर, चाहे उसके कम माप हों या अधिक, उसके उतने भाग होंगे जितने माप; और इस तरह फिर एक एक नहीं रहेगा बल्कि उसके उतने भाग होंगे जितने माप।"],["","सही।"],["","और यदि वह एक माप का होता, तो उस माप के बराबर होता; फिर भी वह बराबरी में असमर्थ दिखाया जा चुका है।"],["","दिखाया जा चुका है।"],["","तो वह न एक माप में भाग लेगा, न अनेक में, न कम में, न बिल्कुल समान में, न स्वयं या दूसरे के बराबर होगा; न स्वयं या दूसरे से बड़ा या छोटा?"],["","अवश्य।"],["","अच्छा, और क्या हम मानते हैं कि एक किसी वस्तु से आयु में बड़ा या छोटा, या उसकी समान आयु का हो सकता है?"],["","क्यों नहीं?"],["","क्यों, क्योंकि जो स्वयं या दूसरे की समान आयु का है, उसे समय की बराबरी या सादृश्य में भाग लेना चाहिए; और हमने कहा था कि एक न बराबरी में भाग लेता है न सादृश्य में?"],["","हमने ऐसा कहा था।"],["","और हमने यह भी कहा था, कि वह असमानता या असादृश्य में भाग नहीं लेता।"],["","बहुत सत्य।"],["","तो एक, इस स्वभाव का होते हुए, किसी वस्तु से आयु में बड़ा या छोटा कैसे हो सकता है, या उसकी समान आयु का?"],["","किसी तरह नहीं।"],["","तो एक न बड़ा हो सकता है न छोटा, न समान आयु का, न स्वयं के साथ न दूसरे के?"],["","स्पष्ट रूप से नहीं।"]]},{"tag":"141a","title":"काल में नहीं, और बिल्कुल नहीं","paras":[["","तो एक, इस स्वभाव का होते हुए, काल में बिल्कुल नहीं हो सकता; क्योंकि क्या जो काल में है उसे सदा स्वयं से बड़ा (आयु में) होते नहीं जाना चाहिए?"],["","अवश्य।"],["","और जो बड़ा है, उसे सदा किसी छोटी वस्तु से बड़ा होना चाहिए?"],["","सत्य।"],["","तो, जो स्वयं से बड़ा होता है, वह साथ ही स्वयं से छोटा भी होता है, यदि उसके पास कुछ होना है जिससे वह बड़ा हो।"],["","तुम्हारा क्या अर्थ है?"],["","मेरा अर्थ यह है:—किसी वस्तु को किसी ऐसी दूसरी वस्तु से भिन्न होने की आवश्यकता नहीं जो पहले से भिन्न है; वह भिन्न है, और यदि उसका भिन्न हो चुका है, तो वह भिन्न हो चुकी है; यदि उसका भिन्न होगा, तो वह भिन्न होगी; पर जो भिन्न हो रही है, उसका कोई भिन्न न हो चुका हो सकता है, न होने वाला, न अभी हो—एकमात्र संभव भिन्न वह है जो हो रहा है।"],["","यह अनिवार्य है।"],["","पर, निश्चित रूप से, बड़ा (आयु में) छोटे के सापेक्ष एक अंतर है, और किसी और के नहीं।"],["","सत्य।"],["","तो जो स्वयं से बड़ा होता है उसे, साथ ही, स्वयं से छोटा भी होना चाहिए?"],["","हाँ।"],["","पर फिर, यह सत्य है कि वह स्वयं से अधिक या कम समय के लिए नहीं हो सकता, बल्कि उसे स्वयं के समान समय के लिए होना, और होना, और हो चुका होना, और होने वाला होना चाहिए?"],["","वह भी अनिवार्य है।"],["","तो जो वस्तुएँ काल में हैं, और काल में भाग लेती हैं, उन्हें हर मामले में, मुझे लगता है, स्वयं की समान आयु का होना चाहिए; और एक साथ स्वयं से बड़ी और छोटी भी होना चाहिए?"],["","हाँ।"],["","पर एक उन गुणों में भाग नहीं लेता था?"],["","बिल्कुल नहीं।"],["","तो वह काल में भाग नहीं लेता, और किसी काल में नहीं है?"],["","तर्क यही दिखाता है।"],["","अच्छा, पर क्या 'था,' और 'हो चुका है,' और 'हो रहा था,' अभिव्यक्तियाँ बीते काल में सहभागिता नहीं दर्शातीं?"],["","अवश्य।"],["","और क्या 'होगा,' 'हो जाएगा,' 'हो चुका होगा,' भविष्य काल में सहभागिता नहीं दर्शाते?"],["","हाँ।"],["","और 'है,' या 'होता है,' वर्तमान काल में सहभागिता दर्शाता है?"],["","अवश्य।"],["","और यदि एक काल में सहभागिता से निरपेक्ष रूप से रहित है, तो वह कभी न हुआ था, न हो रहा था, न कभी किसी समय था, न अब हो चुका है न हो रहा है, न है, न होगा, न हो चुका होगा, न आगे होगा।"],["","बिल्कुल सत्य।"],["","पर क्या सत् में भाग लेने के इनके अलावा कोई और तरीके हैं?"],["","कोई नहीं हैं।"],["","तो एक किसी तरह सत् में भाग नहीं ले सकता?"],["","यही निष्कर्ष है।"],["","तो एक बिल्कुल नहीं है?"],["","स्पष्ट रूप से नहीं।"],["","तो एक इस तरह विद्यमान नहीं कि एक हो; क्योंकि यदि वह होता और सत् में भाग लेता, तो वह पहले से होता; पर यदि तर्क पर विश्वास किया जाए, तो एक न है न एक है?"],["","सत्य।"],["","पर जो नहीं है उसमें कोई गुण या संबंध संभव नहीं?"],["","अवश्य नहीं।"],["","तो उसका न कोई नाम है, न अभिव्यक्ति, न प्रत्यक्ष, न मत, न ज्ञान?"],["","स्पष्ट रूप से नहीं।"],["","तो वह न नामित है, न व्यक्त, न मत का विषय, न ज्ञात, न कोई वस्तु जो है उसे प्रत्यक्ष करती है।"],["","हमें यही निष्कर्ष निकालना होगा।"],["","पर क्या यह सब एक के बारे में सत्य हो सकता है?"],["","मुझे लगता है नहीं।"]]},{"tag":"142b","title":"दूसरा निगमन: वह एक जो है","paras":[["","1.b. मान लो, अब, कि हम एक बार फिर मूल परिकल्पना पर लौटें; आओ देखें कि क्या, आगे की समीक्षा पर, प्रश्न का कोई नया पहलू दिखता है।"],["","मुझे ऐसा करके बहुत खुशी होगी।"],["","हम कहते हैं कि हमें मिलकर वे सब परिणाम निकालने हैं, जो भी वे हों, जो निकलते हैं, यदि एक है?"],["","हाँ।"],["","तो हम आरंभ से आरंभ करेंगे:—यदि एक है, तो क्या एक हो सकता है, और सत् में भाग न ले?"],["","असंभव।"],["","तो एक का सत् होगा, पर उसका सत् एक के समान नहीं होगा; क्योंकि यदि समान होता, तो वह एक का सत् नहीं होता; न ही एक ने सत् में भाग लिया होता, क्योंकि यह प्रतिज्ञप्ति कि एक है इस प्रतिज्ञप्ति के समान होती कि एक एक है; पर हमारी परिकल्पना यह नहीं कि यदि एक एक है तो क्या निकलेगा, बल्कि यदि एक है:—क्या मैं सही नहीं?"],["","बिल्कुल सही।"],["","हमारा कहना है, कि सत् का अर्थ एक के समान नहीं?"],["","अवश्य।"],["","और जब हम उन्हें संक्षेप में जोड़ते हैं, और कहते हैं 'एक है,' तो यह कहने के बराबर है, 'सत् में भाग लेता है'?"],["","बिल्कुल सत्य।"],["","तो एक बार फिर पूछें, यदि एक है तो क्या निकलेगा। क्या यह परिकल्पना अवश्य यह संकेत नहीं करती कि एक ऐसे स्वभाव का है कि उसके भाग हैं?"],["","कैसे?"],["","इस तरह:—यदि सत् एक पर लागू होता है, यदि एक है, और एक सत् पर, यदि सत् एक है; और यदि सत् और एक समान नहीं; और क्योंकि एक, जिसे हमने माना है, है, तो क्या संपूर्ण, यदि वह एक है, स्वयं नहीं होगा, और उसके भाग, एक और सत्, नहीं होंगे?"],["","अवश्य।"],["","और क्या इन भागों में से हर एक—एक और सत्—को बस भाग कहा जाए, या 'भाग' शब्द 'संपूर्ण' शब्द के सापेक्ष होना चाहिए?"],["","बाद वाला।"],["","तो जो एक है वह संपूर्ण भी है और उसका भाग भी है?"],["","अवश्य।"],["","फिर, एक के भागों में, यदि वह है—मेरा अर्थ सत् और एक—क्या कोई दूसरे को संकेतित करने में असफल है? क्या एक सत् से, या सत् एक से खाली है?"],["","असंभव।"],["","इस तरह, हर भाग में भी बारी-बारी से एक और सत् दोनों हैं, और वह कम से कम दो भागों से बना है; और यही सिद्धांत सदा चलता रहता है, और हर भाग में सदा ये दो भाग होते हैं; क्योंकि सत् में सदा एक शामिल है, और एक में सत्; तो एक सदा गायब होता और दो बनता रहता है।"],["","अवश्य।"],["","और इस तरह एक, यदि है, तो बहुलता में अनंत होना चाहिए?"],["","स्पष्ट रूप से।"]]},{"tag":"143a","title":"एक से संख्या उत्पन्न होती है","paras":[["","आओ एक और दिशा लें।"],["","कौन-सी दिशा?"],["","हम कहते हैं कि एक सत् में भाग लेता है और इसलिए वह है?"],["","हाँ।"],["","और इस तरह, एक, यदि उसका सत् है, अनेक निकला है?"],["","सत्य।"],["","पर अब, आओ उस एक को अलग करें जो, जैसा हम कहते हैं, सत् में भाग लेता है, और उसे उससे अलग कल्पना करने का प्रयास करें जिसमें, जैसा हम कहते हैं, वह भाग लेता है—क्या यह अमूर्त एक केवल एक होगा या अनेक?"],["","एक, मुझे लगता है।"],["","आओ देखें:—क्या एक का सत् एक से अन्य नहीं होना चाहिए? क्योंकि एक सत् नहीं, बल्कि, एक के रूप में देखा जाए, तो केवल सत् में भाग लेता था?"],["","अवश्य।"],["","यदि सत् और एक दो अलग वस्तुएँ हैं, तो ऐसा नहीं कि एक एक होने के कारण सत् से अन्य है; न सत् सत् होने के कारण एक से अन्य है; बल्कि वे अन्यता और भिन्नता के कारण एक-दूसरे से भिन्न हैं।"],["","अवश्य।"],["","तो अन्य समान नहीं है—न एक के साथ न सत् के साथ?"],["","निश्चित रूप से नहीं।"],["","और इसलिए चाहे हम सत् और अन्य को लें, या सत् और एक को, या एक और अन्य को, हर ऐसे मामले में हम दो वस्तुएँ लेते हैं, जिन्हें सही रूप से दोनों कहा जा सकता है।"],["","कैसे।"],["","इस तरह—तुम सत् की बात कर सकते हो?"],["","हाँ।"],["","और एक की भी?"],["","हाँ।"],["","तो अब हमने दोनों में से हर एक की बात की है?"],["","हाँ।"],["","अच्छा, और जब मैं सत् और एक की बात करता हूँ, तो मैं उन दोनों की बात करता हूँ?"],["","अवश्य।"],["","और यदि मैं सत् और अन्य की, या एक और अन्य की बात करूँ,—क्या ऐसे किसी भी मामले में मैं दोनों की बात नहीं करता?"],["","हाँ।"],["","और जिसे सही रूप से दोनों कहा जाता है, क्या उसे दो भी नहीं होना चाहिए?"],["","निस्संदेह।"],["","और दो वस्तुओं में से कोई भी किसी भी संभावना से एक कैसे नहीं हो सकती?"],["","नहीं हो सकती।"],["","तो, यदि जोड़े के सदस्य मिलकर दो हैं, तो उन्हें अलग-अलग एक होना चाहिए?"],["","स्पष्ट रूप से।"],["","और यदि उनमें से हर एक एक है, तो किसी भी जोड़े में किसी एक को जोड़ने से, संपूर्ण तीन हो जाता है?"],["","हाँ।"],["","और तीन विषम है, और दो सम?"],["","अवश्य।"],["","और यदि दो हैं तो दुगना भी होना चाहिए, और यदि तीन हैं तो तिगुना होना चाहिए; अर्थात्, यदि दो गुना एक दो बनाता है, और तीन गुना एक तीन?"],["","अवश्य।"],["","दो हैं, और दुगना, और इसलिए दो गुना दो होना चाहिए; और तीन हैं, और तिगुना है, और इसलिए तीन गुना तीन होना चाहिए?"],["","अवश्य।"],["","यदि तीन और दुगना हैं, तो दो गुना तीन है; और यदि दो और तिगुना हैं, तो तीन गुना दो है?"],["","निस्संदेह।"],["","यहाँ, तो, हमने सम को सम बार, और विषम को विषम बार, और सम को विषम बार, और विषम को सम बार लिया है।"],["","सत्य।"],["","और यदि ऐसा है, तो क्या कोई संख्या बचती है जिसका होना आवश्यक नहीं?"],["","बिल्कुल कोई नहीं।"],["","तो यदि एक है, तो संख्या भी होनी चाहिए?"],["","होनी चाहिए।"],["","पर यदि संख्या है, तो अनेक भी होना चाहिए, और सत् की अनंत बहुलता; क्योंकि संख्या बहुलता में अनंत है, और सत् में भी भाग लेती है: क्या मैं सही नहीं?"],["","अवश्य।"],["","और यदि सारी संख्या सत् में भाग लेती है, तो संख्या का हर भाग भी भाग लेगा?"],["","हाँ।"],["","तो सत् वस्तुओं की पूरी भीड़ पर बाँटा गया है, और जो कुछ है, चाहे कितना छोटा या कितना बड़ा, उससे रहित नहीं? और, वास्तव में, इसकी मान्यता ही बेतुकी है, क्योंकि जो है वह सत् से रहित कैसे हो सकता है?"],["","किसी तरह नहीं।"],["","और वह सबसे बड़े और सबसे छोटे में, और हर आकार के सत् में बाँटा गया है, और सब वस्तुओं से अधिक टूटा है; उसके विभाजनों की कोई सीमा नहीं।"],["","सत्य।"],["","तो उसके सबसे अधिक संख्या में भाग हैं?"],["","हाँ, सबसे अधिक संख्या।"],["","क्या इनमें से कोई है जो सत् का भाग है, और फिर भी कोई भाग नहीं?"],["","असंभव।"],["","पर यदि वह है ही और जब तक है, तो उसे एक होना चाहिए, और कोई नहीं नहीं हो सकता?"],["","अवश्य।"],["","तो एक सत् के हर एक भाग से जुड़ा है, और किसी भाग में कम नहीं पड़ता, चाहे बड़ा हो या छोटा, या उसका आकार जो भी हो?"],["","सत्य।"],["","पर सोचो:—क्या एक, अपनी संपूर्णता में, एक ही समय में अनेक जगहों में हो सकता है?"],["","नहीं; मैं उसकी असंभवता देखता हूँ।"],["","और यदि अपनी संपूर्णता में नहीं, तो वह बाँटा गया है; क्योंकि वह सत् के सब भागों के साथ उपस्थित नहीं हो सकता, जब तक बाँटा न जाए।"],["","सत्य।"],["","और जिसके भाग हैं वह उतने होंगे जितने भाग हैं?"],["","अवश्य।"],["","तो हम अभी यह कहने में गलत थे, कि सत् सबसे अधिक संख्या में भागों में बाँटा गया था। क्योंकि वह एक से अधिक भागों में नहीं बाँटा गया, एक के बराबर भागों में; एक कभी सत् से खाली नहीं, न सत् एक से, बल्कि दो होते हुए वे सम-मान और सम-विस्तार हैं।"],["","निश्चित रूप से यह सत्य है।"],["","एक स्वयं, तो, सत् द्वारा भागों में तोड़ा जाकर, अनेक और अनंत है?"],["","सत्य।"],["","तो न केवल वह एक जिसका सत् है अनेक है, बल्कि सत् द्वारा बाँटा गया एक स्वयं भी अनेक होना चाहिए?"],["","अवश्य।"],["","आगे, क्योंकि भाग एक संपूर्ण के भाग हैं, एक, संपूर्ण के रूप में, सीमित होगा; क्योंकि क्या भाग संपूर्ण से समाए नहीं होते?"],["","अवश्य।"],["","और जो समाता है, वह सीमा है?"],["","अवश्य।"],["","तो एक यदि उसका सत् है तो एक और अनेक, संपूर्ण और भाग, सीमाएँ रखते हुए और फिर भी संख्या में असीमित है?"],["","स्पष्ट रूप से।"],["","और सीमाएँ होने के कारण, सिरे भी रखते हुए?"],["","अवश्य।"],["","और यदि संपूर्ण है, तो आरंभ और मध्य और अंत रखते हुए। क्योंकि क्या कोई वस्तु इन तीन के बिना संपूर्ण हो सकती है? और यदि इनमें से कोई किसी वस्तु में कम हो, तो क्या वह फिर संपूर्ण होगी?"],["","नहीं।"],["","तो एक, जैसा दिखता है, आरंभ, मध्य, और अंत रखेगा।"],["","रखेगा।"],["","पर, फिर, मध्य सिरों से समान दूरी पर होगा; वरना वह मध्य में नहीं होगा?"],["","हाँ।"],["","तो एक आकृति में भाग लेगा, या तो सीधी रेखा वाली या गोल, या दोनों का मेल?"],["","सत्य।"],["","और यदि ऐसा है, तो वह स्वयं में भी होगा और दूसरे में भी।"],["","कैसे?"],["","हर भाग संपूर्ण में है, और कोई संपूर्ण के बाहर नहीं।"],["","सत्य।"],["","और सब भाग संपूर्ण से समाए हैं?"],["","हाँ।"],["","और एक अपने सब भाग है, और सब से न अधिक न कम?"],["","नहीं।"],["","और एक संपूर्ण है?"],["","अवश्य।"],["","पर यदि सब भाग संपूर्ण में हैं, और एक उन सब और संपूर्ण है, और वे सब संपूर्ण से समाए हैं, तो एक एक से समाया होगा; और इस तरह एक स्वयं में होगा।"],["","यह सत्य है।"],["","पर फिर, संपूर्ण भागों में नहीं—न सब भागों में, न उनमें से किसी एक में। क्योंकि यदि वह सब में है, तो उसे एक में होना चाहिए; क्योंकि यदि कोई एक होता जिसमें वह नहीं था, तो वह सब भागों में नहीं हो सकता; क्योंकि जिस भाग में वह नहीं वह सब में से एक है, और यदि संपूर्ण इसमें नहीं, तो वह उन सब में कैसे हो सकता है?"],["","नहीं हो सकता।"],["","न ही संपूर्ण कुछ भागों में हो सकता है; क्योंकि यदि संपूर्ण कुछ भागों में होता, तो बड़ा छोटे में होता, जो असंभव है।"],["","हाँ, असंभव।"],["","पर यदि संपूर्ण न एक में, न एक से अधिक में, न सब भागों में है, तो उसे किसी और वस्तु में होना चाहिए, या कहीं भी होना बंद कर देना चाहिए?"],["","अवश्य।"],["","यदि वह कहीं नहीं होता, तो वह कुछ नहीं होता; पर संपूर्ण होते हुए, और स्वयं में न होते हुए, उसे दूसरे में होना चाहिए।"],["","बहुत सत्य।"],["","एक, तो, संपूर्ण के रूप में देखा जाए, तो दूसरे में है, पर अपने सब भाग होने के रूप में देखा जाए, तो स्वयं में है; और इसलिए एक को स्वयं स्वयं में और दूसरे में भी होना चाहिए।"],["","अवश्य।"],["","एक, तो, इस स्वभाव का होते हुए, अवश्य स्थिर और गति में दोनों है?"],["","कैसे?"],["","एक स्थिर है क्योंकि वह स्वयं में है, क्योंकि एक में होते हुए, और इससे बाहर न जाते हुए, वह समान में है, जो वह स्वयं है।"],["","सत्य।"],["","और जो सदा समान में है, उसे सदा स्थिर होना चाहिए?"],["","अवश्य।"],["","अच्छा, और क्या, इसके विपरीत, जो सदा दूसरे में है, उसे कभी समान में नहीं होना चाहिए; और यदि कभी समान में नहीं, तो कभी स्थिर नहीं, और यदि स्थिर नहीं, तो गति में?"],["","सत्य।"],["","तो एक सदा स्वयं स्वयं में और दूसरे में होते हुए, सदा स्थिर और गति में दोनों होना चाहिए?"],["","स्पष्ट रूप से।"],["","और उसे स्वयं के समान, और स्वयं से अन्य होना चाहिए; और दूसरों के समान भी, और दूसरों से अन्य भी; यह उसके पिछले गुणों से निकलता है।"],["","कैसे?"],["","हर वस्तु हर दूसरी वस्तु के संबंध में, या तो समान है या अन्य; या यदि न समान न अन्य, तो भाग का संपूर्ण से, या संपूर्ण का भाग से संबंध में।"],["","स्पष्ट रूप से।"],["","और क्या एक स्वयं का भाग है?"],["","निश्चित रूप से नहीं।"],["","क्योंकि वह स्वयं के संबंध में भाग नहीं, वह स्वयं से संपूर्ण और भाग की तरह संबंधित नहीं हो सकता?"],["","नहीं हो सकता।"],["","पर क्या एक एक से अन्य है?"],["","नहीं।"],["","और इसलिए स्वयं से अन्य नहीं?"],["","निश्चित रूप से नहीं।"],["","तो यदि वह स्वयं के संबंध में न अन्य है, न संपूर्ण, न भाग, तो क्या उसे स्वयं के समान नहीं होना चाहिए?"],["","अवश्य।"],["","पर फिर, एक वस्तु जो 'स्वयं' से दूसरी जगह में है, यदि यह 'स्वयं' स्वयं के साथ समान जगह में रहता है, तो उसे 'स्वयं' से अन्य होना चाहिए, क्योंकि वह दूसरी जगह में होगी?"],["","सत्य।"],["","तो एक एक साथ स्वयं में और दूसरे में दिखाया जा चुका है?"],["","हाँ।"],["","इस तरह, तो, जैसा दिखता है, एक स्वयं से अन्य होगा?"],["","सत्य।"],["","अच्छा, तो, यदि कोई वस्तु किसी वस्तु से अन्य हो, तो क्या वह उससे अन्य नहीं होगी जो अन्य है?"],["","अवश्य।"],["","और क्या सब वस्तुएँ जो एक नहीं हैं, एक से अन्य नहीं होंगी, और एक न-एक से अन्य?"],["","अवश्य।"],["","तो एक दूसरों से अन्य होगा?"],["","सत्य।"],["","पर, विचार करो:—क्या निरपेक्ष समान, और निरपेक्ष अन्य, एक-दूसरे के विपरीत नहीं?"],["","अवश्य।"],["","तो क्या समान कभी अन्य में होगा, या अन्य समान में?"],["","नहीं होंगे।"],["","तो यदि अन्य कभी समान में नहीं, तो ऐसा कुछ नहीं जिसमें अन्य किसी भी समय-अवधि के दौरान हो; क्योंकि उस समय-अवधि के दौरान, चाहे कितनी छोटी, अन्य समान में होगा। क्या यह सत्य नहीं?"],["","हाँ।"],["","और क्योंकि अन्य कभी समान में नहीं, वह कभी किसी ऐसी वस्तु में नहीं हो सकता जो है।"],["","सत्य।"],["","तो अन्य कभी न न-एक में होगा, न एक में?"],["","निश्चित रूप से नहीं।"],["","तो अन्यता के कारण एक न-एक से अन्य नहीं, न न-एक एक से अन्य।"],["","नहीं।"],["","न ही अपने कारण वे एक-दूसरे से अन्य होंगे, यदि अन्य में भाग नहीं लेते।"],["","कैसे हो सकते हैं?"],["","पर यदि वे अन्य नहीं हैं, न अपने कारण न अन्य के कारण, तो क्या वे एक-दूसरे से अन्य होने से पूरी तरह बच नहीं जाएँगे?"],["","बच जाएँगे।"],["","फिर, न-एक एक में भाग नहीं ले सकता; वरना वह न-एक नहीं होता, बल्कि किसी तरह एक होता।"],["","सत्य।"],["","न ही न-एक संख्या हो सकता है; क्योंकि संख्या रखते हुए, वह बिल्कुल न-एक नहीं होता।"],["","नहीं होता।"],["","फिर, क्या न-एक एक का भाग है; या बल्कि, क्या उस स्थिति में वह एक में भाग नहीं लेगा?"],["","लेगा।"],["","तो यदि, हर दृष्टि से, एक और न-एक अलग हैं, तो न एक न-एक का भाग या संपूर्ण है, न न-एक एक का भाग या संपूर्ण?"],["","नहीं।"],["","पर हमने कहा था कि जो वस्तुएँ न एक-दूसरे के भाग हैं न संपूर्ण, न एक-दूसरे से अन्य, वे एक-दूसरे के समान होंगी:—हमने ऐसा कहा था?"],["","हाँ।"],["","तो क्या हम कहें कि एक, न-एक के साथ इस संबंध में होते हुए, उसके समान है?"],["","आओ ऐसा कहें।"],["","तो वह स्वयं के और दूसरों के समान है, और स्वयं से और दूसरों से अन्य भी।"],["","यही निष्कर्ष दिखता है।"],["","और वह स्वयं के और दूसरों के सदृश और असदूश भी होगा?"],["","शायद।"],["","क्योंकि एक दूसरों से अन्य दिखाया गया था, तो दूसरे भी एक से अन्य होंगे।"],["","हाँ।"],["","और एक दूसरों से उसी मात्रा में अन्य है जितना दूसरे उससे अन्य हैं, और न अधिक न कम?"],["","सत्य।"],["","और यदि न अधिक न कम, तो सदृश मात्रा में?"],["","हाँ।"],["","उस गुण के कारण जिससे एक दूसरों से अन्य है और दूसरे इसी तरह उससे अन्य, एक दूसरों जैसा प्रभावित होगा और दूसरे एक जैसे।"],["","तुम्हारा क्या अर्थ है?"],["","मैं नामों का मामला उदाहरण के रूप में ले सकता हूँ: तुम किसी वस्तु को नाम देते हो?"],["","हाँ।"],["","और तुम नाम एक बार या अधिक बार कह सकते हो?"],["","हाँ।"],["","और जब तुम उसे एक बार कहते हो, तो तुम उसका उल्लेख करते हो जिसका वह नाम है? और जब एक से अधिक बार, तो क्या तुम किसी और वस्तु का उल्लेख करते हो? या क्या वह सदा समान वस्तु होनी चाहिए जिसकी तुम बात करते हो, चाहे तुम नाम एक बार बोलो या एक से अधिक बार?"],["","अवश्य वह समान है।"],["","और क्या 'अन्य' किसी वस्तु को दिया गया नाम नहीं?"],["","अवश्य।"],["","जब भी, तो, तुम 'अन्य' शब्द का प्रयोग करते हो, चाहे एक बार या अधिक बार, तुम उसे नाम देते हो जिसका वह नाम है, और किसी और को नाम नहीं देते?"],["","सत्य।"],["","तो जब हम कहते हैं कि दूसरे एक से अन्य हैं, और एक दूसरों से अन्य, तो 'अन्य' शब्द दोहराते हुए हम उस स्वभाव की बात करते हैं जिस पर नाम लागू होता है, और किसी और की नहीं?"],["","बिल्कुल सत्य।"],["","तो एक जो दूसरों से अन्य है, और अन्य जो एक से अन्य है, क्योंकि 'अन्य' शब्द दोनों पर लागू होता है, समान स्थिति में होंगे; और जो समान स्थिति में है वह सदृश है?"],["","हाँ।"],["","तो उस गुण के कारण जिससे एक दूसरों से अन्य है, हर वस्तु हर वस्तु के सदृश होगी, क्योंकि हर वस्तु हर वस्तु से अन्य है।"],["","सत्य।"],["","फिर, सदृश असदूश का विपरीत है?"],["","हाँ।"],["","और अन्य समान का?"],["","फिर सत्य।"],["","और एक दूसरों के समान भी दिखाया गया था?"],["","हाँ।"],["","और दूसरों के समान होना दूसरों से अन्य होने का विपरीत है?"],["","अवश्य।"],["","और जहाँ तक वह अन्य था, उसे सदृश दिखाया गया था?"],["","हाँ।"],["","पर जहाँ तक वह समान था, वह उस गुण के विपरीत गुण के कारण असदूश होगा जिसने उसे सदृश बनाया; और वह अन्यता का गुण था।"],["","हाँ।"],["","तो समान उसे असदूश बनाएगा; वरना वह अन्य का विपरीत नहीं होगा।"],["","सत्य।"],["","तो एक दूसरों के सदृश और असदूश दोनों होगा; सदृश जहाँ तक वह अन्य है, और असदूश जहाँ तक वह समान है।"],["","हाँ, यह तर्क प्रयोग किया जा सकता है।"],["","और एक और तर्क है।"],["","क्या?"],["","जहाँ तक वह समान तरह प्रभावित है वह भिन्न तरह प्रभावित नहीं, और भिन्न तरह प्रभावित न होने से असदूश नहीं, और असदूश न होने से, सदृश है; पर जहाँ तक वह अन्य से प्रभावित है वह भिन्न है, और भिन्न तरह प्रभावित होने से असदूश है।"],["","सत्य।"],["","तो क्योंकि एक दूसरों के समान है और दूसरों से अन्य, इन दो आधारों में से किसी पर भी, या दोनों पर, वह दूसरों के सदृश और असदूश दोनों होगा?"],["","अवश्य।"],["","और इसी तरह स्वयं से अन्य और स्वयं के समान होने से, इन दो आधारों में से किसी पर भी और दोनों पर, वह स्वयं के सदृश और असदूश होगा?"],["","अवश्य।"]]},{"tag":"148d","title":"छूना और न छूना","paras":[["","फिर, एक स्वयं को और दूसरों को कहाँ तक छू सकता है या नहीं छू सकता?—विचार करो।"],["","मैं विचार कर रहा हूँ।"],["","एक को स्वयं में दिखाया गया था जो एक संपूर्ण था?"],["","सत्य।"],["","और दूसरी वस्तुओं में भी?"],["","हाँ।"],["","जहाँ तक वह दूसरी वस्तुओं में है वह दूसरी वस्तुओं को छुएगा, पर जहाँ तक वह स्वयं में है वह उन्हें छूने से रोका जाएगा, और केवल स्वयं को छुएगा।"],["","स्पष्ट रूप से।"],["","तो निष्कर्ष यह है कि वह दोनों को छुएगा?"],["","छुएगा।"],["","पर एक नए दृष्टिकोण पर तुम क्या कहते हो? क्या जो किसी दूसरे को छूने वाला है उसे उसके बगल में नहीं होना चाहिए जिसे उसे छूना है, और उस जगह के सबसे निकट की जगह नहीं घेरनी चाहिए जिसमें वह है जिसे वह छूता है?"],["","सत्य।"],["","तो एक, यदि उसे स्वयं को छूना है, तो स्वयं के बगल में स्थित होना चाहिए, और उस जगह के बगल की जगह घेरनी चाहिए जिसमें वह स्वयं है?"],["","होना चाहिए।"],["","और इसके लिए आवश्यक होगा कि एक दो हो, और एक साथ दो जगहों में हो, और यह, जब तक वह एक है, कभी नहीं होगा।"],["","नहीं।"],["","तो एक स्वयं को उतना ही नहीं छू सकता जितना वह दो नहीं हो सकता?"],["","नहीं छू सकता।"],["","न ही वह दूसरों को छू सकता है।"],["","क्यों नहीं?"],["","कारण यह है, कि जो कुछ किसी दूसरे को छूने वाला है उसे उससे अलग, और उसके बगल में होना चाहिए जिसे उसे छूना है, और उनके बीच कोई तीसरी वस्तु नहीं हो सकती।"],["","सत्य।"],["","तो संपर्क संभव बनाने के लिए कम से कम दो वस्तुएँ आवश्यक हैं?"],["","हैं।"],["","और यदि दो में उचित क्रम में एक तीसरी जोड़ी जाए, तो पदों की संख्या तीन होगी, और संपर्क दो?"],["","हाँ।"],["","और हर अतिरिक्त पद एक अतिरिक्त संपर्क बनाता है, जिससे यह निकलता है कि संपर्क संख्या में पदों से एक कम हैं; पहले दो पद संपर्कों की संख्या से एक अधिक थे, और पदों की पूरी संख्या इसी तरह संपर्कों की पूरी संख्या से एक अधिक है; और हर एक के लिए जो बाद में पदों की संख्या में जोड़ा जाता है, संपर्कों में एक संपर्क जुड़ता है।"],["","सत्य।"],["","वस्तुओं की पूरी संख्या जो भी हो, संपर्क सदा एक कम होंगे।"],["","सत्य।"],["","पर यदि केवल एक हो, और दो नहीं, तो कोई संपर्क नहीं होगा?"],["","कैसे हो सकता है?"],["","और क्या हम नहीं कहते कि दूसरे एक से अन्य होने के कारण एक नहीं हैं और एक में उनका कोई भाग नहीं?"],["","सत्य।"],["","तो उनकी कोई संख्या नहीं, यदि उनमें कोई एक नहीं?"],["","अवश्य नहीं।"],["","तो दूसरे न एक हैं न दो, न वे किसी संख्या के नाम से पुकारे जाते हैं?"],["","नहीं।"],["","एक, तो, अकेला एक है, और दो विद्यमान नहीं?"],["","स्पष्ट रूप से नहीं।"],["","और यदि दो नहीं हैं, तो कोई संपर्क नहीं?"],["","नहीं है।"],["","तो न एक दूसरों को छूता है, न दूसरे एक को, यदि कोई संपर्क नहीं?"],["","निश्चित रूप से नहीं।"],["","इन सब कारणों से एक स्वयं को और दूसरों को छूता भी है और नहीं भी छूता?"],["","सत्य।"]]},{"tag":"149d","title":"बराबर और असमान, बड़ा और छोटा","paras":[["","आगे—क्या एक स्वयं के और दूसरों के बराबर और असमान है?"],["","तुम्हारा क्या अर्थ है?"],["","यदि एक दूसरों से बड़ा या छोटा होता, या दूसरे एक से बड़े या छोटे, तो वे एक और दूसरे होने के कारण एक-दूसरे से बड़े या छोटे नहीं होते; पर, यदि जो वे हैं उसके अलावा उनमें बराबरी होती, तो वे एक-दूसरे के बराबर होते, या यदि एक में छोटापन और दूसरों में बड़प्पन होता, या एक में बड़प्पन और दूसरों में छोटापन—जिस प्रकार में बड़प्पन होता वह बड़ा होता, और जिसमें छोटापन होता वह छोटा?"],["","अवश्य।"],["","तो बड़प्पन और छोटापन जैसे दो प्रत्यय हैं; क्योंकि यदि वे न होते तो वे एक-दूसरे के विपरीत न होते और उसमें उपस्थित न होते जो है।"],["","कैसे हो सकते?"],["","यदि, तो, छोटापन एक में उपस्थित है तो वह या तो संपूर्ण में उपस्थित होगा या संपूर्ण के एक भाग में?"],["","अवश्य।"],["","पहला मान लो; वह या तो पूरे एक के सम-मान और सम-विस्तार होगा, या एक को समाएगा?"],["","स्पष्ट रूप से।"],["","यदि वह एक के सम-विस्तार है तो वह एक के सम-मान होगा, या यदि एक को समाता है तो वह एक से बड़ा होगा?"],["","अवश्य।"],["","पर क्या छोटापन किसी वस्तु के बराबर या किसी वस्तु से बड़ा हो सकता है, और बड़प्पन और बराबरी के काम कर सकता है और अपने काम नहीं?"],["","असंभव।"],["","तो छोटापन एक के संपूर्ण में नहीं हो सकता, बल्कि, यदि हो, तो केवल एक भाग में?"],["","हाँ।"],["","और निश्चित रूप से भाग के सब में नहीं, क्योंकि तब संपूर्ण की कठिनाई लौटेगी; वह किसी भी भाग के बराबर या उससे बड़ा होगा जिसमें वह है।"],["","अवश्य।"],["","तो छोटापन किसी वस्तु में नहीं होगा, चाहे संपूर्ण में हो या भाग में; न वास्तविक छोटेपन के अलावा कोई वस्तु छोटी होगी।"],["","सत्य।"],["","न ही बड़प्पन एक में होगा, क्योंकि यदि बड़प्पन किसी वस्तु में हो तो बड़प्पन के अलावा और उससे अलग कुछ बड़ा होगा, अर्थात्, वह जिसमें बड़प्पन है; और यह भी जब छोटा स्वयं वहाँ नहीं, जिससे एक को, यदि वह बड़ा है, बढ़कर होना चाहिए; पर यह असंभव है, यह देखते हुए कि छोटापन पूरी तरह अनुपस्थित है।"],["","सत्य।"],["","पर निरपेक्ष बड़प्पन केवल निरपेक्ष छोटेपन से बड़ा है, और छोटापन केवल निरपेक्ष बड़प्पन से छोटा है।"],["","बहुत सत्य।"],["","तो दूसरी वस्तुएँ एक से बड़ी या छोटी नहीं, यदि उनमें न बड़प्पन है न छोटापन; न ही बड़प्पन या छोटेपन में एक के संबंध में बढ़ने या पिछड़ने की कोई शक्ति है, बल्कि केवल एक-दूसरे के संबंध में; न ही एक उनसे या दूसरों से बड़ा या छोटा होगा, यदि उसमें न बड़प्पन है न छोटापन।"],["","स्पष्ट रूप से नहीं।"],["","तो यदि एक दूसरों से न बड़ा है न छोटा, तो वह न उनसे बढ़ सकता है न उनसे पिछड़ सकता है?"],["","निश्चित रूप से नहीं।"],["","और जो न बढ़ता है न पिछड़ता है, उसे बराबरी पर होना चाहिए; और बराबरी पर होने से, बराबर होना चाहिए।"],["","अवश्य।"],["","और यह एक के स्वयं से संबंध के बारे में भी सत्य होगा; स्वयं में न बड़प्पन न छोटापन रखते हुए, वह न स्वयं से बढ़ेगा न पिछड़ेगा, बल्कि स्वयं के साथ बराबरी पर और स्वयं के बराबर होगा।"],["","अवश्य।"],["","तो एक स्वयं के और दूसरों के दोनों के बराबर होगा?"],["","स्पष्ट रूप से ऐसा।"],["","और फिर भी एक, स्वयं स्वयं में होते हुए, स्वयं को घेरेगा भी और स्वयं से बाहर भी होगा; और, स्वयं को समाते हुए, स्वयं से बड़ा होगा; और, स्वयं में समाए होने के रूप में, छोटा होगा; और इस तरह स्वयं से बड़ा और छोटा होगा।"],["","होगा।"],["","अब ऐसी कोई वस्तु संभव नहीं जो एक और दूसरों में शामिल न हो?"],["","अवश्य नहीं।"],["","पर, निश्चित रूप से, जो है उसे सदा कहीं होना चाहिए?"],["","हाँ।"],["","पर जो किसी वस्तु में है वह छोटा होगा, और जिसमें वह है वह बड़ा होगा; किसी और तरह एक वस्तु दूसरी में नहीं हो सकती।"],["","सत्य।"],["","और क्योंकि एक और दूसरों के अलावा या उनसे अलग कुछ नहीं, और उन्हें किसी वस्तु में होना चाहिए, तो क्या उन्हें एक-दूसरे में नहीं होना चाहिए, एक दूसरों में और दूसरे एक में, यदि उन्हें कहीं होना है?"],["","यह स्पष्ट है।"],["","पर जहाँ तक एक दूसरों में है, दूसरे एक से बड़े होंगे, क्योंकि वे एक को समाते हैं, जो दूसरों से छोटा होगा, क्योंकि वह उनमें समाया है; और जहाँ तक दूसरे एक में हैं, एक उसी सिद्धांत पर दूसरों से बड़ा होगा, और दूसरे एक से छोटे।"],["","सत्य।"],["","एक, तो, स्वयं के और दूसरों के बराबर और उनसे बड़ा और छोटा होगा?"],["","स्पष्ट रूप से।"],["","और यदि वह बड़ा और छोटा और बराबर है, तो वह स्वयं और दूसरों से बराबर और अधिक और कम मापों या विभागों का होगा, और यदि मापों का, तो भागों का भी?"],["","अवश्य।"],["","और यदि बराबर और अधिक और कम मापों या विभागों का, तो वह संख्या में स्वयं और दूसरों से अधिक या कम होगा, और इसी तरह संख्या में स्वयं और दूसरों के बराबर?"],["","वह कैसे?"],["","वह उन वस्तुओं से अधिक मापों का होगा जिनसे वह बढ़कर है, और उतने भागों का जितने माप; और इसी तरह उसके साथ जिसके वह बराबर है, और उसके साथ जिससे वह छोटा है।"],["","सत्य।"],["","और स्वयं से बड़ा और छोटा, और स्वयं के बराबर होने से, वह स्वयं के साथ बराबर मापों का और स्वयं से अधिक और कम मापों का होगा; और यदि मापों का तो भागों का भी?"],["","होगा।"],["","और स्वयं के साथ बराबर भागों का होने से, वह संख्या में स्वयं के बराबर होगा; और अधिक भागों का होने से, अधिक, और कम का होने से, स्वयं से कम?"],["","अवश्य।"],["","और यही दूसरी वस्तुओं से उसके संबंध पर लागू होगा; जहाँ तक वह उनसे बड़ा है, वह संख्या में उनसे अधिक होगा; और जहाँ तक वह छोटा है, वह संख्या में कम होगा; और जहाँ तक वह आकार में दूसरी वस्तुओं के बराबर है, वह संख्या में उनके बराबर होगा।"],["","अवश्य।"],["","एक बार फिर, तो, जैसा दिखता है, एक संख्या में स्वयं और सब दूसरी वस्तुओं दोनों के बराबर और उनसे अधिक और कम होगा।"],["","होगा।"]]},{"tag":"151e","title":"एक और काल","paras":[["","क्या एक काल में भी भाग लेता है? और क्या वह काल में सहभागिता के कारण स्वयं और दूसरों से आयु में बड़ा और छोटा है और होता है, और फिर, स्वयं और दूसरों से न छोटा न बड़ा?"],["","तुम्हारा क्या अर्थ है?"],["","यदि एक है, तो उस पर सत् लागू होना चाहिए?"],["","हाँ।"],["","पर होना (einai) केवल वर्तमान काल में सत् की सहभागिता है, और हो चुका होना बीते काल में सत् की सहभागिता है, और होने वाला होना भविष्य काल में सत् की सहभागिता है?"],["","बहुत सत्य।"],["","तो एक, क्योंकि वह सत् में भाग लेता है, काल में भाग लेता है?"],["","अवश्य।"],["","और क्या काल सदा आगे नहीं बढ़ता रहता?"],["","हाँ।"],["","तो एक सदा स्वयं से आयु में बड़ा होता जा रहा है, क्योंकि वह काल में आगे बढ़ता है?"],["","अवश्य।"],["","और क्या तुम्हें याद है कि आयु में बड़ा उससे बड़ा होता है जो छोटा होता जा रहा है?"],["","मुझे याद है।"],["","तो क्योंकि एक स्वयं से बड़ा होता है, वह साथ ही छोटा भी होता है?"],["","अवश्य।"],["","इस तरह, तो, एक स्वयं से बड़ा और छोटा दोनों होता है?"],["","हाँ।"],["","और वह बड़ा है (है न?) जब होते-होते, वह 'था' और 'होगा' के बीच काल के उस बिंदु पर पहुँचता है, जो 'अब' है: क्योंकि निश्चित रूप से अतीत से भविष्य की ओर जाते हुए, वह वर्तमान को लाँघ नहीं सकता?"],["","नहीं।"],["","और जब वह वर्तमान पर पहुँचता है तो बड़ा होना बंद कर देता है, और अब होता नहीं, बल्कि बड़ा है, क्योंकि यदि वह आगे बढ़ता रहता तो वर्तमान कभी उस तक नहीं पहुँचता, क्योंकि जो आगे बढ़ता है उसका स्वभाव है कि वह वर्तमान और भविष्य दोनों को छुए, वर्तमान को छोड़ते हुए और भविष्य को पकड़ते हुए, जब वह उनके बीच होने की प्रक्रिया में हो।"],["","सत्य।"],["","पर जो हो रहा है वह वर्तमान को लाँघ नहीं सकता; जब वह वर्तमान पर पहुँचता है तो होना बंद कर देता है, और तब वही है जो वह हो रहा हो।"],["","स्पष्ट रूप से।"],["","और इस तरह एक, जब बड़ा होते हुए वर्तमान पर पहुँचता है, होना बंद कर देता है, और तब बड़ा है।"],["","अवश्य।"],["","और वह उससे बड़ा है जिससे वह बड़ा हो रहा था, और वह स्वयं से बड़ा हो रहा था।"],["","हाँ।"],["","और जो बड़ा है वह छोटे से बड़ा है?"],["","सत्य।"],["","तो एक स्वयं से छोटा है, जब बड़ा होते हुए वह वर्तमान पर पहुँचता है?"],["","अवश्य।"],["","पर वर्तमान एक के साथ उसके पूरे अस्तित्व के दौरान सदा उपस्थित है; क्योंकि जब भी वह है वह सदा अब है।"],["","अवश्य।"],["","तो एक सदा स्वयं से बड़ा और छोटा है भी और होता भी है?"],["","सचमुच।"],["","और क्या वह स्वयं से अधिक समय तक है या होता है या स्वयं के बराबर समय तक?"],["","बराबर समय तक।"],["","पर यदि वह स्वयं के बराबर समय तक होता है या है, तो वह स्वयं की समान आयु का है?"],["","अवश्य।"],["","और जो समान आयु का है, वह न बड़ा है न छोटा?"],["","नहीं।"],["","एक, तो, स्वयं के साथ समान समय होते और रहते हुए, न स्वयं से बड़ा या छोटा है न होता है?"],["","मैं कहूँगा कि नहीं।"],["","और दूसरी वस्तुओं के साथ उसके संबंध क्या हैं? क्या वह उनसे बड़ा या छोटा है या होता है?"],["","मैं तुम्हें नहीं बता सकता।"],["","तुम कम से कम मुझे यह बता सकते हो कि एक से अन्य एक से अधिक हैं—अन्य एक होता, पर दूसरों में बहुलता है, और वे एक से अधिक हैं?"],["","उनमें बहुलता होगी।"],["","और बहुलता एक से बड़ी संख्या को संकेतित करती है?"],["","अवश्य।"],["","और क्या हम कहें कि छोटा या बड़ा अस्तित्व में पहले आता है या आया है?"],["","छोटा।"],["","तो सबसे छोटा पहला है? और वह एक है?"],["","हाँ।"],["","तो संख्या वाली सब वस्तुओं में एक पहला अस्तित्व में आता है; पर बाकी सब वस्तुओं की भी संख्या है, बहुवचन होने से और एकवचन नहीं।"],["","है।"],["","और क्योंकि वह पहले अस्तित्व में आया, तो मानना होगा कि वह दूसरों से पहले अस्तित्व में आया, और दूसरे बाद में; और जो वस्तुएँ बाद में अस्तित्व में आई, वे उससे छोटी हैं जो उनसे पहले आया? और इस तरह दूसरी वस्तुएँ एक से छोटी होंगी, और एक दूसरी वस्तुओं से बड़ा?"],["","सत्य।"],["","एक और प्रश्न के बारे में तुम क्या कहोगे? क्या एक अपने स्वभाव के विरुद्ध अस्तित्व में आ सकता है, या यह असंभव है?"],["","असंभव।"],["","और फिर भी, निश्चित रूप से, एक के भाग दिखाए गए थे; और यदि भाग, तो आरंभ, मध्य और अंत?"],["","हाँ।"],["","और आरंभ, एक स्वयं का और सब दूसरी वस्तुओं का भी, सबसे पहले अस्तित्व में आता है; और आरंभ के बाद, दूसरे आते हैं, जब तक तुम अंत तक न पहुँची?"],["","अवश्य।"],["","और इन सब दूसरों को हम संपूर्ण के और एक के भाग कहेंगे, जो, जैसे ही अंत पहुँचता है, संपूर्ण और एक हो चुका है?"],["","हाँ; हम यही कहेंगे।"],["","पर अंत सबसे आखिर में आता है, और एक ऐसे स्वभाव का है कि वह अंतिम के साथ अस्तित्व में आता है; और, क्योंकि एक अपने स्वभाव के अनुसार ही अस्तित्व में आ सकता है, उसका स्वभाव यह माँंगिगा कि वह दूसरों के बाद, अंत के साथ-साथ, अस्तित्व में आए।"],["","स्पष्ट रूप से।"],["","तो एक दूसरों से छोटा है और दूसरे एक से बड़े।"],["","वह भी मेरे निर्णय में स्पष्ट है।"],["","अच्छा, और क्या एक का या किसी वस्तु का आरंभ या कोई और भाग, यदि वह भाग है और भाग (बहुवचन) नहीं, भाग होते हुए, अवश्य एक भी नहीं होना चाहिए?"],["","अवश्य।"],["","और क्या एक हर भाग के साथ अस्तित्व में नहीं आएगा—पहले भाग के साथ जब वह अस्तित्व में आता है, और दूसरे भाग और बाकी सब के साथ, और किसी भाग में कम नहीं पड़ेगा, जो किसी दूसरे भाग में जोड़ा जाता है जब तक वह अंतिम तक पहुँचकर एक संपूर्ण न बन जाए; वह न मध्य में, न पहले में, न अंतिम में, न उनमें से किसी में कम पड़ेगा, जब तक होने की प्रक्रिया चल रही है?"],["","सत्य।"],["","तो एक बाकी सब की समान आयु का है, ताकि यदि एक स्वयं अपने स्वभाव का खंडन न करे, तो वह न दूसरों से पहले होगा न बाद में, बल्कि साथ-साथ; और इस तर्क के अनुसार एक न दूसरों से बड़ा होगा न छोटा, न दूसरे एक से, पर पिछले तर्क के अनुसार एक दूसरों से बड़ा और छोटा होगा और दूसरे एक से।"],["","अवश्य।"],["","इस ढंग से तो एक है और हो चुका है। पर उसके दूसरों से बड़ा और छोटा होने, और दूसरों के एक से, और न बड़ा न छोटा होने के बारे में, हम क्या कहें? क्या हम सत् की तरह होने के बारे में भी कहें, या भिन्न?"],["","मैं उत्तर नहीं दे सकता।"],["","पर मैं यह कहने का साहस कर सकता हूँ, कि यदि एक वस्तु दूसरी से बड़ी या छोटी भी हो, तो वह पहले से अधिक मात्रा में बड़ी या छोटी नहीं हो सकती; क्योंकि असमानों में बराबर जोड़ने से, चाहे समय-अवधियों में या किसी और वस्तु में, उनके बीच का अंतर पहले जैसा ही रहता है।"],["","अवश्य।"],["","तो जो है, वह उससे बड़ा या छोटा नहीं हो सकता जो है, क्योंकि आयु का अंतर सदा समान रहता है; एक बड़ा है और हो चुका है और दूसरा छोटा; पर वे अब ऐसे हो नहीं रहे।"],["","सत्य।"],["","और जो एक है वह इसलिए उन दूसरों से न बड़ा होता है न छोटा जो हैं।"],["","नहीं।"],["","पर विचार करो कि क्या वे किसी और तरह बड़े और छोटे नहीं हो सकते।"],["","किस तरह?"],["","बिल्कुल जैसे एक दूसरों से बड़ा और दूसरे एक से बड़े सिद्ध किए गए थे।"],["","और उसमें क्या?"],["","यदि एक दूसरों से बड़ा है, तो वह दूसरों से अधिक समय से अस्तित्व में है।"],["","हाँ।"],["","पर फिर विचार करो; यदि हम एक बड़े और एक छोटे समय में बराबर समय जोड़ें, तो क्या बड़ा छोटे समय से बराबर या पहले से छोटे भाग से भिन्न होगा?"],["","छोटे भाग से।"],["","तो एक की आयु और दूसरों की आयु के बीच अंतर बाद में उतना बड़ा नहीं होगा जितना पहले, बल्कि यदि दोनों में बराबर समय जोड़ा जाए तो वे आयु में कम से कम भिन्न होंगे?"],["","हाँ।"],["","और जो आयु में किसी दूसरे से पहले से कम भिन्न है, वह बड़ा होने से, उस दूसरे के संबंध में छोटा हो जाएगा जिससे वह बड़ा था?"],["","हाँ, छोटा।"],["","और यदि एक छोटा होता है तो उक्त दूसरे एक के संबंध में पहले से बड़े हो जाएँगे।"],["","अवश्य।"],["","तो जो छोटा हो गया था वह उसके सापेक्ष बड़ा होता है जो पहले हो चुका था और बड़ा था; वह वास्तव में कभी बड़ा नहीं है, बल्कि सदा हो रहा है, क्योंकि एक सदा यौवन की ओर बढ़ रहा है और दूसरा बुढ़ापे की ओर। और इसी तरह बड़ा सदा छोटे से छोटा होने की प्रक्रिया में है; क्योंकि क्योंकि वे सदा विपरीत दिशाओं में जा रहे हैं वे एक-दूसरे के विपरीत तरीकों से होते हैं, छोटा बड़े से बड़ा, और बड़ा छोटे से छोटा। पर वे हो चुके नहीं हो सकते; क्योंकि यदि वे पहले ही हो चुके होते तो वे होते और केवल हो नहीं रहे होते। पर यह असंभव है; क्योंकि वे सदा एक-दूसरे से बड़े और छोटे दोनों हो रहे हैं: एक दूसरों से छोटा होता है क्योंकि वह बड़ा और पहले दिखा था, और दूसरे एक से बड़े होते हैं क्योंकि वे बाद में अस्तित्व में आए; और इसी तरह दूसरे एक के साथ समान संबंध में हैं, क्योंकि वे बड़े, और एक से पहले दिखे थे।"],["","यह स्पष्ट है।"],["","जहाँ तक, तो, एक वस्तु दूसरी से बड़ी या छोटी नहीं होती, क्योंकि वे सदा एक-दूसरे से बराबर संख्या से भिन्न होती हैं, एक दूसरों से बड़ा या छोटा नहीं हो सकता, न दूसरे एक से; पर जहाँ तक जो पहले अस्तित्व में आया और जो बाद में अस्तित्व में आया उन्हें लगातार एक-दूसरे से भिन्न भाग से भिन्न होना चाहिए—इस दृष्टि से दूसरों को एक से बड़ा और छोटा होना चाहिए, और एक को दूसरों से।"],["","अवश्य।"],["","इन सब कारणों से, तो, एक स्वयं और दूसरों से बड़ा और छोटा है और होता है, और न स्वयं या दूसरों से बड़ा या छोटा है न होता है।"],["","अवश्य।"],["","पर क्योंकि एक काल में भाग लेता है, और बड़ा और छोटा होने में भाग लेता है, तो क्या उसे अतीत, वर्तमान, और भविष्य में भी भाग नहीं लेना चाहिए?"],["","अवश्य लेना चाहिए।"],["","तो एक था और है और होगा, और हो रहा था और हो रहा है और होगा?"],["","अवश्य।"],["","और कुछ है और था और होगा जो उसके संबंध में है और उसका है?"],["","सत्य।"],["","और क्योंकि इस क्षण हमारे पास एक का मत और ज्ञान और प्रत्यक्ष है, तो उसका मत और ज्ञान और प्रत्यक्ष है?"],["","बिल्कुल सही।"],["","तो उसके लिए नाम और अभिव्यक्ति है, और वह नामित और व्यक्त है, और इस प्रकार की हर वस्तु जो दूसरी वस्तुओं से संबंधित है एक से संबंधित है।"],["","अवश्य, यह सत्य है।"]]},{"tag":"155e","title":"सत् लेना और छोड़ना","paras":[["","फिर भी एक बार और और तीसरी बार, आओ विचार करें: यदि एक एक और अनेक दोनों है, जैसा हमने वर्णन किया, और न एक न अनेक, और काल में भाग लेता है, तो क्या उसे, जहाँ तक वह एक है, कभी-कभी सत् में भाग नहीं लेना चाहिए, और जहाँ तक वह एक नहीं, कभी-कभी सत् में भाग नहीं लेना चाहिए?"],["","अवश्य।"],["","पर क्या वह सत् में भाग न लेते हुए सत् में भाग ले सकता है, या सत् में भाग लेते हुए सत् में भाग न ले?"],["","असंभव।"],["","तो एक अलग-अलग समय पर सत् में भाग लेता है और नहीं लेता, क्योंकि यही एकमात्र तरीका है जिससे वह समान में भाग ले भी और न भी ले।"],["","सत्य।"],["","और क्या कोई समय भी नहीं जब वह सत् धारण करता है और सत् छोड़ता है—क्योंकि वह समान वस्तु को कैसे रख भी और न रख भी सकता है जब तक वह किसी समय उसे ग्रहण और त्याग न करे?"],["","असंभव।"],["","और सत् धारण करने को तुम उत्पत्ति कहोगे?"],["","कहूँगा।"],["","और सत् छोड़ने को तुम विनाश कहोगे?"],["","कहूँगा।"],["","एक तो, जैसा दिखता है, सत् लेकर और छोड़कर उत्पन्न होता है और नष्ट होता है।"],["","अवश्य।"],["","और एक और अनेक होते हुए और उत्पन्न और नष्ट होने की प्रक्रिया में, जब वह एक होता है तो अनेक होना बंद कर देता है, और जब अनेक, तो एक होना बंद कर देता है?"],["","अवश्य।"],["","और जैसे वह एक और अनेक होता है, क्या उसे अनिवार्य रूप से अलगाव और एकत्रीकरण का अनुभव नहीं करना चाहिए?"],["","अनिवार्य रूप से।"],["","और जब भी वह सदृश और असदूश होता है तो उसे सदृश और असदूश बनना होगा?"],["","हाँ।"],["","और जब वह बड़ा या छोटा या बराबर होता है तो उसे बढ़ना या घटना या बराबर होना होगा?"],["","सत्य।"],["","और जब गति में होते हुए वह रुकता है, और स्थिर होते हुए गति में बदलता है, तो वह निश्चित रूप से किसी काल में नहीं हो सकता?"],["","कैसे हो सकता है?"],["","पर यह कि जो वस्तु पहले स्थिर हो वह बाद में गति में हो, या पहले गति में और बाद में स्थिर, बिना परिवर्तन का अनुभव किए, असंभव है।"],["","असंभव।"],["","और निश्चित रूप से ऐसा कोई समय नहीं हो सकता जिसमें कोई वस्तु एक साथ न गति में हो न स्थिर?"],["","नहीं हो सकता।"],["","पर न ही वह बदले बिना बदल सकती है।"],["","सत्य।"],["","तो वह कब बदलती है; क्योंकि वह न स्थिर होते हुए बदल सकती है, न गति में होते हुए, न काल में होते हुए?"],["","नहीं बदल सकती।"]]},{"tag":"156d","title":"क्षण","paras":[["","और क्या यह अजीब वस्तु जिसमें वह बदलने के समय होती है वास्तव में विद्यमान है?"],["","कौन-सी वस्तु?"],["","क्षण। क्योंकि क्षण कुछ ऐसा संकेतित करता लगता है जिससे परिवर्तन दो अवस्थाओं में से किसी में होता है; क्योंकि परिवर्तन न स्थिरता की अवस्था से होता है, न गति की अवस्था से; बल्कि यह विचित्र स्वभाव है जिसे हम क्षण कहते हैं जो स्थिरता और गति के बीच पड़ा है, किसी काल में न होते हुए; और इसमें और इससे बाहर जो गति में है वह स्थिरता में बदलता है, और जो स्थिर है वह गति में।"],["","ऐसा दिखता है।"],["","और एक तो, क्योंकि वह स्थिर है और गति में भी, दोनों में से किसी में बदलेगा, क्योंकि केवल इसी तरह वह दोनों में हो सकता है। और बदलते हुए वह क्षण में बदलता है, और जब वह बदल रहा है तो वह किसी काल में नहीं होगा, और तब न गति में होगा न स्थिर।"],["","नहीं होगा।"],["","और दूसरे परिवर्तनों के संबंध में भी वह समान स्थिति में होगा, जब वह सत् से सत् के अंत में, या असत् से उत्पत्ति में जाता है —तब वह गति और स्थिरता की कुछ अवस्थाओं के बीच से गुज़रता है, और न है न नहीं है, न उत्पन्न होता है न नष्ट होता है।"],["","बहुत सत्य।"],["","और इसी सिद्धांत पर, एक से अनेक और अनेक से एक में जाने में, एक न एक है न अनेक, न अलग न एकत्रित; और सदृश से असदूश, और असदूश से सदृश में जाने में, वह न सदृश है न असदूश, न सदृश बनने की अवस्था में न असदूश बनने की; और छोटे से बड़े और बराबर और वापस जाने में, वह न छोटा होगा न बड़ा, न बराबर, न वृद्धि, या हास, या सम-करण की अवस्था में।"],["","सत्य।"],["","तो ये सब, एक के गुण हैं, यदि एक का सत् है।"],["","अवश्य।"]]},{"tag":"157b","title":"यदि एक है: दूसरे","paras":[["","1.aa. पर यदि एक है, तो दूसरों का क्या होगा—क्या इस पर भी विचार नहीं करना चाहिए?"],["","हाँ।"],["","तो आओ दिखाएँ, यदि एक है, तो एक से अन्य दूसरों के गुण क्या होंगे।"],["","आओ ऐसा करें।"],["","क्योंकि एक से अन्य वस्तुएँ हैं, दूसरे एक नहीं हैं; क्योंकि यदि होते तो वे एक से अन्य नहीं हो सकते थे।"],["","बहुत सत्य।"],["","न ही दूसरे एक से पूरी तरह रहित हैं, बल्कि एक तरह से वे एक में भाग लेते हैं।"],["","किस तरह?"],["","क्योंकि दूसरे एक से अन्य इसलिए हैं कि उनके भाग हैं; क्योंकि यदि उनके भाग न होते तो वे बस एक होते।"],["","सही।"],["","और भाग, जैसा हम कहते हैं, संपूर्ण से संबंध रखते हैं?"],["","हम ऐसा कहते हैं।"],["","और संपूर्ण अवश्य अनेक से बना एक होना चाहिए; और भाग एक के भाग होंगे, क्योंकि हर भाग अनेक का भाग नहीं, बल्कि एक संपूर्ण का है।"],["","तुम्हारा क्या अर्थ है?"],["","यदि कोई वस्तु अनेक का भाग होती, स्वयं उनमें से एक होते हुए, तो वह निश्चित रूप से स्वयं का भाग होगी, जो असंभव है, और वह दूसरे भागों में से हर एक का भाग होगी, यदि सब का; क्योंकि यदि किसी एक का भाग नहीं, तो वह इस एक के अलावा बाकी सब का भाग होगी, और इस तरह हर एक का भाग नहीं होगी; और यदि हर एक का भाग नहीं, तो वह अनेक में से किसी एक का भाग नहीं होगी; और किसी एक का भाग न होने से, वह उन सब वस्तुओं का भाग या कुछ और नहीं हो सकती जिनमें से किसी की वह कुछ नहीं।"],["","स्पष्ट रूप से नहीं।"],["","तो भाग न अनेक का भाग है, न सब का, बल्कि एक निश्चित अकेले रूप का है, जिसे हम संपूर्ण कहते हैं, जो सब से बनी एक पूर्ण एकता है—इसका भाग भाग होगा।"],["","अवश्य।"],["","यदि, तो, दूसरों के भाग हैं, तो वे संपूर्ण में और एक में भाग लेंगे।"],["","सत्य।"],["","तो एक से अन्य दूसरे एक पूर्ण संपूर्ण होने चाहिए, भाग रखते हुए।"],["","अवश्य।"],["","और यही तर्क हर भाग पर लागू होता है, क्योंकि भाग को एक में भाग लेना चाहिए; क्योंकि यदि भागों में से हर एक भाग है, तो इसका अर्थ है, मुझे लगता है, कि वह बाकी से अलग और स्व-संबंधित एक है; वरना वह हर एक नहीं।"],["","सत्य।"],["","पर जब हम भाग के एक में भाग लेने की बात करते हैं, तो उसे स्पष्ट रूप से एक से अन्य होना चाहिए; क्योंकि यदि नहीं, तो उसने केवल भाग नहीं लिया होता, बल्कि वह एक होता; जबकि केवल स्वयं (एक) ही एक हो सकता है।"],["","बहुत सत्य।"],["","संपूर्ण और भाग दोनों को एक में भाग लेना चाहिए; क्योंकि संपूर्ण एक संपूर्ण होगा, जिसके भाग भाग होंगे; और हर भाग संपूर्ण का एक भाग होगा जो भाग का संपूर्ण है।"],["","सत्य।"],["","और क्या जो वस्तुएँ एक में भाग लेती हैं, उससे अन्य नहीं होंगी?"],["","अवश्य।"],["","और जो वस्तुएँ एक से अन्य हैं वे अनेक होंगी; क्योंकि यदि जो वस्तुएँ एक से अन्य हैं वे न एक होतीं न एक से अधिक, तो वे कुछ नहीं होतीं।"],["","सत्य।"],["","पर, यह देखते हुए कि जो वस्तुएँ भाग के रूप में एक में, और संपूर्ण के रूप में एक में भाग लेती हैं, एक से अधिक हैं, क्या वही वस्तुएँ जो एक में भाग लेती हैं संख्या में अनंत नहीं होनी चाहिए?"],["","कैसे?"],["","आओ मामले को इस तरह देखें:—क्या यह तथ्य नहीं कि एक में भाग लेते हुए वे एक नहीं हैं, और जिस समय वे उसमें भाग ले रही हैं उसी समय एक में भाग नहीं लेतीं?"],["","स्पष्ट रूप से।"],["","तो वे ऐसा भीड़ों के रूप में करती हैं जिनमें एक उपस्थित नहीं?"],["","बहुत सत्य।"],["","और यदि हम विचार में उनसे सबसे छोटा अंश अलग करें, तो क्या वह सबसे छोटा अंश, यदि वह एक में भाग नहीं लेता, भीड़ नहीं होना चाहिए और एक नहीं?"],["","होना चाहिए।"],["","और यदि हम उनके स्वभाव के दूसरे पहलू को देखते रहें, सरल रूप से, और स्वयं में देखा जाए, तो क्या वे, जहाँ तक हम उन्हें देखते हैं, संख्या में असीमित नहीं होंगी?"],["","अवश्य।"],["","और फिर भी, जब हर अलग भाग भाग बनता है, तो भागों की संपूर्ण और एक-दूसरे के संबंध में सीमा होती है, और संपूर्ण की भागों के संबंध में।"],["","बिल्कुल ऐसा ही।"],["","एक से अन्य दूसरों के लिए परिणाम यह है कि उनका और एक का मेल उनमें एक नया तत्व उत्पन्न करता दिखता है जो उन्हें एक-दूसरे के संबंध में सीमा देता है; जबकि अपने स्वभाव में उनकी कोई सीमा नहीं।"],["","यह स्पष्ट है।"],["","तो एक से अन्य दूसरे, संपूर्ण और भागों दोनों के रूप में, अनंत हैं, और सीमा में भी भाग लेते हैं।"],["","अवश्य।"],["","तो वे एक-दूसरे के और स्वयं के सदृश और असदूश दोनों हैं।"],["","वह कैसे?"],["","जहाँ तक वे अपने स्वभाव में असीमित हैं, वे सब समान तरह प्रभावित हैं।"],["","सत्य।"],["","और जहाँ तक वे सब सीमा में भाग लेते हैं, वे सब समान तरह प्रभावित हैं।"],["","अवश्य।"],["","पर जहाँ तक उनकी अवस्था सीमित और असीमित दोनों है, वे विपरीत तरीकों से प्रभावित हैं।"],["","हाँ।"],["","और विपरीत वस्तुओं में सबसे असदूश हैं।"],["","अवश्य।"],["","तो, उनके गुणों में से किसी एक के संदर्भ में देखे जाने पर, वे स्वयं के और एक-दूसरे के सदृश होंगे; दोनों के एक साथ संदर्भ में, सबसे विपरीत और सबसे असदूश।"],["","यह सत्य दिखता है।"],["","तो दूसरे स्वयं के और एक-दूसरे के सदृश और असदूश दोनों हैं?"],["","सत्य।"],["","और वे एक-दूसरे के समान और भिन्न भी हैं, और गति में और स्थिर, और हर प्रकार के विपरीत गुण का अनुभव करते हैं, जैसा बिना कठिनाई के उनके बारे में सिद्ध किया जा सकता है, क्योंकि उन्हें उक्त गुणों का अनुभव करते दिखाया जा चुका है?"],["","सत्य।"]]},{"tag":"159b","title":"एक से कटे हुए दूसरे","paras":[["","1.bb. मान लो, अब, कि हम इन मामलों की आगे की चर्चा को स्पष्ट मानकर छोड़ दें, और इस परिकल्पना पर फिर विचार करें कि एक है, कि क्या इस सब का विपरीत दूसरों के बारे में उतना ही सत्य है या नहीं।"],["","अवश्य।"],["","तो आओ फिर से आरंभ करें, और पूछें, यदि एक है, तो दूसरों के गुण क्या होने चाहिए?"],["","आओ वह प्रश्न पूछें।"],["","क्या एक को दूसरों से अलग नहीं होना चाहिए, और दूसरों को एक से?"],["","क्यों?"],["","क्यों, क्योंकि उनके अलावा और कुछ नहीं जो दोनों से अलग हो; क्योंकि 'एक और दूसरे' अभिव्यक्ति में सब वस्तुएँ शामिल हैं।"],["","हाँ, सब वस्तुएँ।"],["","तो हम यह नहीं मान सकते कि उनसे अलग कुछ है जिसमें एक और दूसरे दोनों विद्यमान हो सकें?"],["","कुछ नहीं है।"],["","तो एक और दूसरे कभी समान में नहीं?"],["","सत्य।"],["","तो वे एक-दूसरे से अलग हैं?"],["","हाँ।"],["","और हम निश्चित रूप से नहीं कह सकते कि जो वास्तव में एक है उसके भाग हैं?"],["","असंभव।"],["","तो एक दूसरों में न संपूर्ण के रूप में होगा, न भाग के रूप में, यदि वह दूसरों से अलग है, और उसके भाग नहीं?"],["","असंभव।"],["","तो ऐसा कोई तरीका नहीं जिससे दूसरे एक में भाग ले सकें, यदि वे न संपूर्ण में न भाग में भाग लेते हैं?"],["","ऐसा लगता है कि नहीं।"],["","तो ऐसा कोई तरीका नहीं जिससे दूसरे एक हों, या स्वयं में कोई एकता रखें?"],["","नहीं है।"],["","न ही दूसरे अनेक हैं; क्योंकि यदि वे अनेक होते, तो उनका हर भाग संपूर्ण का भाग होता; पर अब दूसरे, किसी तरह एक में भाग न लेते हुए, न एक हैं न अनेक, न संपूर्ण, न भाग।"],["","सत्य।"],["","तो दूसरे न दो या तीन हैं न उन्हें समाते हैं, यदि एक से पूरी तरह वंचित हैं?"],["","सत्य।"],["","तो दूसरे न एक के सदृश हैं न असदूश, न उनमें सादृश्य और असादृश्य है; क्योंकि यदि वे सदृश और असदूश होते, या उनमें सादृश्य और असादृश्य होता, तो उनमें एक-दूसरे के विपरीत दो स्वभाव होते।"],["","यह स्पष्ट है।"],["","पर जो किसी वस्तु में भाग नहीं लेता उसका दो वस्तुओं में भाग लेना हमारे द्वारा असंभव माना गया था?"],["","असंभव।"],["","तो दूसरे न सदृश हैं न असदूश न दोनों, क्योंकि यदि वे सदृश या असदूश होते तो वे उन दो स्वभावों में से एक में भाग लेते, जो एक वस्तु होती, और यदि वे दोनों होते तो वे विपरीतों में भाग लेते जो दो वस्तुएँ होतीं, और यह असंभव दिखाया जा चुका है।"],["","सत्य।"],["","इसलिए वे न समान हैं, न अन्य, न गति में, न स्थिर, न उत्पत्ति की अवस्था में, न विनाश की, न बड़े, न छोटे, न बराबर, न उन्होंने इस प्रकार का कुछ और अनुभव किया है; क्योंकि, यदि वे ऐसा कोई गुण अनुभव करने में सक्षम हैं, तो वे एक और दो और तीन, और विषम और सम में भाग लेंगे, और इनमें, जैसा सिद्ध किया जा चुका है, वे भाग नहीं लेते, यह देखते हुए कि वे पूरी तरह और हर तरह एक से रहित हैं।"],["","बहुत सत्य।"],["","इसलिए यदि एक है, तो एक सब वस्तुएँ है, और कुछ भी नहीं, स्वयं के संबंध में भी और दूसरी वस्तुओं के संबंध में भी।"],["","अवश्य।"]]},{"tag":"160b","title":"निगमन: यदि एक नहीं है","paras":[["","2.a. अच्छा, और क्या हमें अगला यह विचार नहीं करना चाहिए कि यदि एक नहीं है तो परिणाम क्या होगा?"],["","हाँ; करना चाहिए।"],["","इस परिकल्पना का अर्थ क्या है—यदि एक नहीं है; क्या इसमें और इस परिकल्पना में कोई अंतर है—यदि न-एक नहीं है?"],["","अंतर है, अवश्य।"],["","क्या केवल अंतर है, या बल्कि क्या दो अभिव्यक्तियाँ—यदि एक नहीं है, और यदि न-एक नहीं है, पूरी तरह विपरीत नहीं?"],["","वे पूरी तरह विपरीत हैं।"],["","और मान लो कोई कहे:—यदि बड़प्पन नहीं है, यदि छोटापन नहीं है, या इस तरह की कोई वस्तु, तो क्या उसका अर्थ, जब भी वह ऐसी अभिव्यक्ति का प्रयोग करता है, यह नहीं कि 'जो नहीं है' दूसरी वस्तुओं से अन्य है?"],["","अवश्य।"],["","और इसलिए जब वह कहता है 'यदि एक नहीं है' तो उसका स्पष्ट अर्थ है, कि जो 'नहीं है' वह बाकी सब से अन्य है; हम जानते हैं कि उसका क्या अर्थ है—जानते हैं न?"],["","हाँ, जानते हैं।"],["","जब वह 'एक' कहता है, तो वह कुछ ऐसा कहता है जो ज्ञात है; और दूसरे, कुछ ऐसा जो बाकी सब वस्तुओं से अन्य है; इससे कोई अंतर नहीं पड़ता कि वह एक पर सत् लागू करे या असत्, क्योंकि जिसे 'नहीं है' कहा जाता है वह फिर भी कुछ ज्ञात माना जाता है, और दूसरी वस्तुओं से अलग किया जाता है।"],["","अवश्य।"],["","तो मैं फिर से आरंभ करूँगा, और पूछुँगा: यदि एक नहीं है, तो परिणाम क्या हैं? पहले स्थान पर, जैसा दिखता है, उसका ज्ञान है, वरना 'यदि एक नहीं है' शब्दों का अर्थ ही ज्ञात नहीं होता।"],["","सत्य।"],["","दूसरे, दूसरे उससे भिन्न हैं, वरना उसे दूसरों से भिन्न वर्णित नहीं किया जा सकता था?"],["","अवश्य।"],["","भिन्नता, तो, ज्ञान की तरह उसकी भी है; क्योंकि एक को दूसरों से भिन्न कहते हुए, हम दूसरों में भिन्नता की बात नहीं करते, बल्कि एक में।"],["","स्पष्ट रूप से ऐसा।"],["","इसके अलावा, जो एक नहीं है वह कुछ है और 'वह,' और 'यह,' और 'ये,' और ऐसे से संबंध में भाग लेता है, और 'इस' का गुण है; क्योंकि एक, या एक से अन्य दूसरों की बात नहीं की जा सकती थी, न उस एक का जो नहीं है कोई गुण या संबंधी हो सकता था या कहा जा सकता था, न उसे कुछ होना कहा जा सकता था, यदि वह 'कुछ' में, या अभी बताए गए दूसरे संबंधों में भाग न लेता।"],["","सत्य।"],["","सत्, तो, एक पर लागू नहीं किया जा सकता, क्योंकि वह नहीं है; पर जो एक नहीं है वह अनेक वस्तुओं में भाग ले सकता है या बल्कि उसे लेना ही चाहिए, यदि वह और कुछ और नहीं है; पर यदि, न एक न वह एक जो नहीं है, का न होना माना जाए, और हम किसी भिन्न स्वभाव की वस्तु की बात कर रहे हैं, तो हम उसके बारे में कुछ नहीं कह सकते। पर मान लो कि वह एक जो नहीं है और कुछ और नहीं है, तो उसे 'वह' विधेय में, और अनेक दूसरों में भाग लेना होगा।"],["","अवश्य।"],["","और दूसरों के संबंध में उसमें असादृश्य होगा, क्योंकि दूसरे एक से भिन्न होने से भिन्न प्रकार के होंगे।"],["","अवश्य।"],["","और क्या भिन्न प्रकार की वस्तुएँ प्रकार में अन्य भी नहीं?"],["","अवश्य।"],["","और क्या प्रकार में अन्य वस्तुएँ असदूश नहीं?"],["","वे असदूश हैं।"],["","और यदि वे एक से असदूश हैं, तो जिससे वे असदूश हैं वह स्पष्ट रूप से उनसे असदूश होगा?"],["","स्पष्ट रूप से ऐसा।"],["","तो एक में असादृश्य होगा जिसके संदर्भ में दूसरे उससे असदूश हैं?"],["","यह सत्य लगता है।"],["","और यदि दूसरी वस्तुओं से असादृश्य उससे जुड़ा है, तो उसमें स्वयं से सादृश्य होना चाहिए।"],["","कैसे?"],["","यदि एक में एक से असादृश्य हो, तो कुछ और अर्थ होगा; न ही परिकल्पना एक से संबंधित होगी; बल्कि वह एक से अन्य किसी वस्तु से संबंधित होगी?"],["","बिल्कुल ऐसा।"],["","पर ऐसा नहीं हो सकता।"],["","नहीं।"],["","तो एक में स्वयं से सादृश्य होना चाहिए?"],["","होना चाहिए।"],["","फिर, वह दूसरों के बराबर नहीं; क्योंकि यदि वह बराबर होता, तो वह बराबरी के कारण तुरंत होता और उनके सदृश होता; पर यदि एक का कोई सत् नहीं, तो वह न हो सकता है न सदृश हो सकता है?"],["","नहीं हो सकता।"],["","पर क्योंकि वह दूसरों के बराबर नहीं, तो न ही दूसरे उसके बराबर हो सकते हैं?"],["","निश्चित रूप से नहीं।"],["","और जो वस्तुएँ बराबर नहीं वे असमान हैं?"],["","सत्य।"],["","और वे एक असमान के असमान हैं?"],["","अवश्य।"],["","तो एक असमानता में भाग लेता है, और इसके संदर्भ में दूसरे उससे असमान हैं?"],["","बहुत सत्य।"],["","और असमानता बड़प्पन और छोटेपन को संकेतित करती है?"],["","हाँ।"],["","तो एक, यदि ऐसे स्वभाव का है, तो उसमें बड़प्पन और छोटापन है?"],["","यह सत्य दिखता है।"],["","और बड़प्पन और छोटापन सदा अलग खड़े रहते हैं?"],["","सत्य।"],["","तो उनके बीच सदा कुछ होता है?"],["","होता है।"],["","और क्या तुम बराबरी के अलावा किसी और वस्तु का सोच सकते हो जो उनके बीच हो?"],["","नहीं, बराबरी ही है जो उनके बीच पड़ी है।"],["","तो जिसमें बड़प्पन और छोटापन है उसमें बराबरी भी है, जो उनके बीच पड़ी है?"],["","यह स्पष्ट है।"],["","तो एक, जो नहीं है, जैसा दिखता है, बड़प्पन और छोटेपन और बराबरी में भाग लेता है?"],["","स्पष्ट रूप से।"]]},{"tag":"161e","title":"जो एक नहीं है वह सत् में भाग लेता है","paras":[["","आगे, उसे निश्चित रूप से किसी तरह सत् में भाग लेना चाहिए?"],["","कैसे?"],["","ऐसा होना चाहिए, क्योंकि यदि नहीं, तो यह कहने में कि एक नहीं है हम सत्य नहीं बोलेंगे। पर यदि हम सत्य बोलते हैं, तो स्पष्ट रूप से हमें वह कहना चाहिए जो है। क्या मैं सही नहीं?"],["","हाँ।"],["","और क्योंकि हम दावा करते हैं कि हम सत्य बोलते हैं, तो हमें यह भी दावा करना चाहिए कि हम वह कहते हैं जो है?"],["","अवश्य।"],["","तो, जैसा दिखता है, एक, जब वह नहीं है, है; क्योंकि यदि वह नहीं होने पर न होता, बल्कि (या, 'असत् के संबंध में अस्तित्व का कुछ भाग छोड़ दे।') सत् का कुछ भाग छोड़ देता, ताकि असत् बन जाए, तो वह तुरंत होता।"],["","बिल्कुल सत्य।"],["","तो एक जो नहीं है, यदि उसे स्वयं को बनाए रखना है, तो असत् के बंधन के रूप में असत् का सत् रखना चाहिए, बिल्कुल जैसे सत् को अपना सत् पूर्ण करने के लिए बंधन के रूप में असत् का असत् रखना चाहिए; क्योंकि सत् के सत् और असत् के असत् का सबसे सच्चा दावा तब है जब सत् सत् के सत् में भाग लेता है, और असत् के सत् में नहीं—यही सत् की पूर्णता है; और जब असत् असत् के असत् में भाग नहीं लेता बल्कि असत् के सत् में—यही असत् की पूर्णता है।"],["","बिल्कुल सत्य।"],["","तो क्योंकि जो है वह असत् में भाग लेता है, और जो नहीं है वह सत् में, तो क्या एक को भी न होने के लिए सत् में भाग नहीं लेना चाहिए?"],["","अवश्य।"],["","तो एक, यदि वह नहीं है, तो स्पष्ट रूप से उसका सत् है?"],["","स्पष्ट रूप से।"],["","और असत् भी है, यदि वह नहीं है?"],["","अवश्य।"],["","पर क्या कोई वस्तु जो एक निश्चित अवस्था में है बिना बदले उस अवस्था में न हो सकती है?"],["","असंभव।"],["","तो हर वस्तु जो एक निश्चित अवस्था में है और नहीं है, परिवर्तन को संकेतित करती है?"],["","अवश्य।"],["","और परिवर्तन गति है—हम यह कह सकते हैं?"],["","हाँ, गति।"],["","और एक को होना और न होना दोनों सिद्ध किया जा चुका है?"],["","हाँ।"],["","और इसलिए समान अवस्था में है और नहीं है?"],["","हाँ।"],["","इस तरह जो एक नहीं है उसकी गति भी दिखाई जा चुकी है, क्योंकि वह सत् से असत् में बदलता है?"],["","यह सत्य दिखता है।"],["","पर निश्चित रूप से यदि वह जो है उनके बीच कहीं नहीं, जैसा कि तथ्य है, क्योंकि वह नहीं है, तो वह एक जगह से दूसरी जगह नहीं बदल सकता?"],["","असंभव।"],["","तो वह जगह बदलकर गति नहीं कर सकता?"],["","नहीं।"],["","न ही वह समान स्थान पर घूम सकता है, क्योंकि वह कहीं समान को नहीं छूता, क्योंकि समान है, और जो नहीं है उसे उन वस्तुओं में नहीं गिना जा सकता जो हैं?"],["","नहीं गिना जा सकता।"],["","तो एक, यदि वह नहीं है, उसमें नहीं घूम सकता जिसमें वह नहीं है?"],["","नहीं।"],["","न ही एक, चाहे वह है या नहीं है, स्वयं से अन्य में बदला जा सकता है, क्योंकि यदि वह बदलता और स्वयं से भिन्न हो जाता, तो हम अब भी एक की बात नहीं कर रहे होते, बल्कि किसी और वस्तु की?"],["","सत्य।"],["","पर यदि एक न बदलाव सहता है, न समान जगह पर घूमता है, न जगह बदलता है, तो क्या वह अब भी गति में सक्षम हो सकता है?"],["","असंभव।"],["","अब जो अचल है उसे निश्चित रूप से स्थिर होना चाहिए, और जो स्थिर है उसे ठहरा रहना चाहिए?"],["","अवश्य।"],["","तो एक जो नहीं है, ठहरा रहता है, और गति में भी है?"],["","यह सत्य लगता है।"],["","पर यदि वह गति में है तो उसे अवश्य बदलाव से गुज़रना होगा, क्योंकि जो कुछ गति करता है, जहाँ तक वह गति करता है, वह अब समान अवस्था में नहीं, बल्कि दूसरी में है?"],["","हाँ।"],["","तो एक, गति करते हुए, बदला जाता है?"],["","हाँ।"],["","और, आगे, यदि किसी तरह गति नहीं करता, तो वह किसी तरह बदला नहीं जाएगा?"],["","नहीं।"],["","तो, जहाँ तक जो एक नहीं है गति करता है, वह बदला जाता है, पर जहाँ तक वह गति नहीं करता, वह बदला नहीं जाता?"],["","सही।"],["","तो जो एक नहीं है वह बदला जाता है और नहीं बदला जाता?"],["","यह स्पष्ट है।"],["","और क्या जो बदला जाता है उसे पहले से अन्य नहीं होना चाहिए, और अपनी पिछली अवस्था खोनी और नष्ट होना चाहिए; पर जो बदला नहीं जाता वह न अस्तित्व में आ सकता है न नष्ट हो सकता है?"],["","बहुत सत्य।"],["","और जो एक नहीं है, बदला जाते हुए, उत्पन्न और नष्ट होता है; और न बदला जाते हुए, न उत्पन्न होता है न नष्ट; और इस तरह जो एक नहीं है वह उत्पन्न और नष्ट होता है, और न उत्पन्न होता है न नष्ट?"],["","सत्य।"]]},{"tag":"163b","title":"जो एक नहीं है, निरपेक्ष रूप से","paras":[["","2.b. और अब, आओ एक बार फिर आरंभ पर लौटें, और देखें कि क्या ये या कोई और परिणाम निकलेंगे।"],["","आओ वैसा करें जैसा तुम कहते हो।"],["","यदि एक नहीं है, तो हम पूछते हैं कि एक के संबंध में क्या होगा? यही प्रश्न है।"],["","हाँ।"],["","क्या 'नहीं है' शब्द उसमें सत् की अनुपस्थिति को नहीं दर्शाते जिस पर हम उन्हें लागू करते हैं?"],["","बिल्कुल ऐसा ही।"],["","और जब हम कहते हैं कि कोई वस्तु नहीं है, तो क्या हमारा अर्थ है कि वह एक तरह से नहीं है पर दूसरी तरह है? या क्या हमारा अर्थ, निरपेक्ष रूप से, यह है कि जो नहीं है उसकी किसी प्रकार या तरह या किस्म में सत् में सहभागिता नहीं?"],["","बिल्कुल निरपेक्ष रूप से।"],["","तो, जो नहीं है वह हो नहीं सकता, या किसी तरह सत् में भाग नहीं ले सकता?"],["","नहीं ले सकता।"],["","और क्या उत्पत्ति, और नष्ट होने से हमारा अर्थ सत् को धारण करना और सत् को खोना नहीं था?"],["","और कुछ नहीं।"],["","और क्या जिसकी सत् में कोई सहभागिता नहीं, वह सत् को धारण कर सकता या खो सकता है?"],["","असंभव।"],["","एक तो, क्योंकि वह किसी तरह नहीं है, किसी तरह सत् को रख या खो या धारण नहीं कर सकता?"],["","सत्य।"],["","तो जो एक नहीं है, क्योंकि वह किसी तरह सत् में भाग नहीं लेता, न नष्ट होता है न उत्पन्न?"],["","नहीं।"],["","तो वह बिल्कुल बदला नहीं जाता; क्योंकि यदि बदला जाता तो वह उत्पन्न और नष्ट होता?"],["","सत्य।"],["","पर यदि वह बदला नहीं जाता तो वह गति नहीं कर सकता?"],["","निश्चित रूप से नहीं।"],["","न ही हम कह सकते हैं कि वह ठहरा है, यदि वह कहीं नहीं; क्योंकि जो ठहरा है उसे सदा एक ही और समान जगह में होना चाहिए?"],["","अवश्य।"],["","तो हमें कहना होगा कि जो एक नहीं है वह कभी ठहरा नहीं रहता और कभी गति नहीं करता?"],["","दोनों नहीं।"],["","न ही कोई विद्यमान वस्तु है जो उससे जोड़ी जा सके; क्योंकि यदि होती, तो वह सत् में भाग लेता?"],["","यह स्पष्ट है।"],["","और इसलिए न छोटापन, न बड़प्पन, न बराबरी, उससे जोड़ी जा सकती है?"],["","नहीं।"],["","न ही सादृश्य न भिन्नता, न स्वयं के संबंध में न दूसरों के?"],["","स्पष्ट रूप से नहीं।"],["","अच्छा, और यदि उससे कुछ नहीं जोड़ा जाना चाहिए, तो क्या दूसरी वस्तुएँ उससे जोड़ी जा सकती हैं?"],["","निश्चित रूप से नहीं।"],["","और इसलिए दूसरी वस्तुएँ उसके संबंध में न सदृश हो सकती हैं न असदूश, न समान, न भिन्न?"],["","नहीं हो सकतीं।"],["","न ही जो नहीं है वह कुछ हो सकता है, या यह वस्तु हो सकता है, या इस या उस या अन्य से संबंधित या उसका गुण हो सकता है, या अतीत, वर्तमान, या भविष्य हो सकता है। न ही ज्ञान, या मत, या प्रत्यक्ष, या अभिव्यक्ति, या नाम, या कोई और वस्तु जो है, उससे कोई संबंध रख सकती है?"],["","नहीं।"],["","तो जो एक नहीं है उसकी किसी प्रकार की कोई अवस्था नहीं?"],["","ऐसा ही निष्कर्ष दिखता है।"]]},{"tag":"164b","title":"यदि एक नहीं है: आभास के रूप में दूसरे","paras":[["","2.aa. फिर भी एक बार और; यदि एक नहीं है, तो दूसरों का क्या होता है? आओ यह तय करें।"],["","हाँ; आओ यह तय करें।"],["","दूसरे निश्चित रूप से होने चाहिए; क्योंकि यदि वे, एक की तरह, न होते, तो हम अब उनकी बात नहीं कर रहे होते।"],["","सत्य।"],["","पर दूसरों की बात करना भिन्नता को संकेतित करता है—'अन्य' और 'भिन्न' पद पर्यायवाची हैं?"],["","सत्य।"],["","अन्य का अर्थ अन्य से अन्य है, और भिन्न, भिन्न से भिन्न?"],["","हाँ।"],["","तो, यदि दूसरे होने हैं, तो कुछ है जिससे वे अन्य होंगे?"],["","अवश्य।"],["","और वह क्या हो सकता है?—क्योंकि यदि एक नहीं है, तो वे एक से अन्य नहीं होंगे।"],["","नहीं होंगे।"],["","तो वे एक-दूसरे से अन्य होंगे; क्योंकि एकमात्र बचा विकल्प यह है कि वे कुछ नहीं से अन्य हैं।"],["","सत्य।"],["","और वे हर एक एक-दूसरे से अन्य हैं, बहुवचन होने से और एकवचन नहीं; क्योंकि यदि एक नहीं है, तो वे एकवचन नहीं हो सकते, बल्कि उनका हर कण संख्या में अनंत है; और यदि कोई वह ले जो सबसे छोटा अंश दिखता है, तो यह, जो एक दिखता था, एक क्षण में अनेक में उड़ जाता है, जैसे स्वप्र में, और सबसे छोटा होने से बहुत बड़ा हो जाता है, उन अंशों की तुलना में जिनमें वह टूट जाता है?"],["","बहुत सत्य।"],["","और ऐसे कणों में दूसरे एक-दूसरे से अन्य होंगे, यदि दूसरे हैं, और एक नहीं है?"],["","बिल्कुल।"],["","और क्या अनेक कण नहीं होंगे, हर एक एक दिखते हुए, पर एक न होते हुए, यदि एक नहीं है?"],["","सत्य।"],["","और ऐसा लगता है कि उनके बारे में संख्या कही जा सकती है यदि उनमें से हर एक एक दिखता है, यद्यपि वह वास्तव में अनेक है?"],["","कही जा सकती है।"],["","और उनमें विषम और सम दिखेंगे, जिनकी भी कोई वास्तविकता नहीं होगी, यदि एक नहीं है?"],["","हाँ।"],["","और उनमें एक सबसे छोटा दिखेगा; और यह भी उन अनेक छोटे अंशों की तुलना में बड़ा और बहुविध दिखेगा जो उसमें समाए हैं?"],["","अवश्य।"],["","और हर कण को अनेक और थोड़े के बराबर कल्पित किया जाएगा; क्योंकि वह बड़े से छोटे में जाता नहीं दिख सकता था बिना मध्य तक पहुँचता दिखे; और इस तरह बराबरी का आभास उत्पन्न होगा।"],["","हाँ।"],["","और न आरंभ, न मध्य, न अंत रखते हुए, हर अलग कण फिर भी स्वयं के और दूसरे के संबंध में सीमा रखता दिखता है।"],["","कैसे?"],["","क्योंकि, जब कोई इनमें से किसी एक की ऐसी कल्पना करता है, तो आरंभ से पहले एक और आरंभ दिखता है, और अंत के बाद बचा एक और अंत है, और मध्य में भीतर अधिक सच्चे पर छोटे मध्य, क्योंकि उनमें से किसी की कोई एकता कल्पित नहीं की जा सकती, क्योंकि एक नहीं है।"],["","बहुत सत्य।"],["","और इस तरह सारा सत्, जो भी हम सोचें, अंशों में टूट जाना चाहिए, क्योंकि कण की कल्पना एकता के बिना करनी होगी?"],["","अवश्य।"],["","और ऐसा सत् जब धुँधला और दूर से देखा जाए, तो एक दिखता है; पर जब पास से और तीक्ष्ण बुद्धि से देखा जाए, तो हर एक वस्तु अनंत दिखती है, क्योंकि वह एक से वंचित है, जो नहीं है?"],["","इससे अधिक निश्चित कुछ नहीं।"],["","तो दूसरों में से हर एक को अनंत और सीमित, और एक और अनेक दिखना चाहिए, यदि एक से अन्य दूसरे विद्यमान हैं और एक नहीं।"],["","दिखना चाहिए।"],["","तो क्या वे सदृश और असदूश नहीं दिखेंगे?"],["","किस तरह?"],["","बिल्कुल जैसे एक चित्र में दूर खड़े व्यक्ति को वस्तुएँ सब एक, और समान अवस्था में और सदृश दिखती हैं?"],["","सत्य।"],["","पर जब तुम उनके पास जाते हो, तो वे अनेक और भिन्न दिखती हैं; और भिन्नता के आभास के कारण, प्रकार में भिन्न, और स्वयं से असदूश?"],["","सत्य।"],["","और इसी तरह कणों को स्वयं के और एक-दूसरे के सदृश और असदूश दिखना चाहिए।"],["","अवश्य।"],["","और क्या उन्हें समान और फिर भी एक-दूसरे से भिन्न, और स्वयं के संपर्क में, यद्यपि वे अलग हैं, और हर प्रकार की गति, और हर प्रकार की स्थिरता रखते हुए, और उत्पन्न और नष्ट होते हुए, और दोनों अवस्थाओं में से किसी में नहीं, और ऐसे, नहीं होना चाहिए, जिन सब वस्तुओं की आसानी से गणना की जा सकती है, यदि एक नहीं है और अनेक हैं?"],["","बिल्कुल सत्य।"]]},{"tag":"165e","title":"यदि एक नहीं है, तो कुछ नहीं है","paras":[["","2.bb. एक बार फिर, आओ आरंभ पर लौटें, और पूछें कि यदि एक नहीं है, और एक के दूसरे हैं, तो क्या निकलेगा।"],["","आओ वह प्रश्न पूछें।"],["","पहले स्थान पर, दूसरे एक नहीं होंगे?"],["","असंभव।"],["","न ही वे अनेक होंगे; क्योंकि यदि वे अनेक होते तो उनमें एक समाया होता। पर यदि उनमें से कोई एक एक नहीं, तो वे सब शून्य हैं, और इसलिए वे अनेक नहीं होंगे।"],["","सत्य।"],["","यदि दूसरों में कोई एक नहीं, तो दूसरे न अनेक हैं न एक।"],["","नहीं हैं।"],["","न ही वे एक या अनेक के रूप में दिखते हैं।"],["","क्यों नहीं?"],["","क्योंकि दूसरों का किसी प्रकार के असत् के साथ किसी प्रकार या ढंग या तरीके का सहभागिता नहीं, न ही जो नहीं है वह दूसरों में से किसी से जुड़ा हो सकता है; क्योंकि जो नहीं है उसके भाग नहीं।"],["","सत्य।"],["","न ही दूसरों के संबंध में असत् का कोई मत या कोई आभास है, न असत् कभी किसी तरह दूसरों से जोड़ा जाता है।"],["","नहीं।"],["","तो यदि एक नहीं है, तो दूसरों में से किसी की न एक के रूप में न अनेक के रूप में कोई धारणा है; क्योंकि तुम एक के बिना अनेक की धारणा नहीं कर सकते।"],["","नहीं कर सकते।"],["","तो यदि एक नहीं है, तो दूसरे न हैं, न एक या अनेक होने की कल्पना की जा सकती है?"],["","ऐसा लगता है कि नहीं।"],["","न सदृश या असदूश के रूप में?"],["","नहीं।"],["","न समान या भिन्न के रूप में, न संपर्क या अलगाव में, न उन अवस्थाओं में से किसी में जिनकी गणना हमने दिखने के रूप में की;—दूसरे इनमें से न कुछ हैं न कुछ दिखते हैं, यदि एक नहीं है?"],["","सत्य।"],["","तो क्या हम तर्क को एक शब्द में समेटकर सत्य नहीं कह सकते: यदि एक नहीं है, तो कुछ नहीं है?"],["","अवश्य।"],["","इतना कहा जाए; और आगे आओ वह दावा करें जो सत्य लगता है, कि, चाहे एक है या नहीं है, एक और दूसरे स्वयं के और एक-दूसरे के संबंध में, सब के सब, हर तरह से, हैं और नहीं हैं, और होने का आभास देते हैं और न होने का आभास देते हैं।"],["","बिल्कुल सत्य।"]]}]}});
